cron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T11:34:33-08:00","id":55580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=55549#post55549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So apparently the first step on the &quot;How To Save Creation From Raksha&quot; path is &quot;PROFIT&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm okay with this!</div> </div> </div> </div>An army marches on its stomach, and truth be told, I like roleplaying out the nuances of using social charms to create markets and the like, the Community's aversion to &quot;UGH BRAINWASHING&quot; be damned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T11:45:48-08:00","id":55585,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't qualify your usage of Terrifying Lust Infliction to be brainwashing... its more akin to creating a Market Need so that you can fulfill it (which from what I can gather, is the whole point of the charm).<br /> <br /> Glad everyone's happy so far! See, this is why I try to 