nt that more for the other two. And I am fine with having more people join. The more the merrier (assuming that it is not too much for you).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T15:44:22-08:00","id":72280,"title":"","content":"HAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAAA.. I got a valentine's card form someone today that said, &quot;Hey baby, Come to Yu-Shan with me.... and I'll show you how to play my Games of Divinity!&quot; It was so great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T22:42:47-08:00","id":72477,"title":"","content":"Just replied. Sorry, my work is keeping me away from the computer lately. Also, nice card, Hyuga!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T09:15:04-08:00","id":73229,"title":"","content":"Hey, hi, it's me. Sorry, got distracted. Where am I and what should I do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T10:42:58-08:00","id":73260,"title":"","content":"No problem guys. You've just received provisional support of one of the Elders of Gens Ptreas, and have declared your intent to head downriver to the capital. So I suppose you could be getting transport?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T13:38:30-08:00","id":77296,"title":"","content":"Omni.. are you still playing? You have been really quiet. I feel like I am starting to take over the game by posting all the time, but it has gotten REALLY slow. Should we just stop with the small chat conversations and just jump straight to every point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T21:51:33-08:00","id":77470,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I know, I know. I've been run ragged as of late with Grad School apps and work. However, I'm going to make an effort to keep on top of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T11:49:21-08:00","id":77763,"title":"","content":"Reposting from the recruitment thread:<br /> <br /> Sheet<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_1X-SK603ZelTAMp_bwEFABN2l2IiHJsMXb9mn7qCwc/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...b9mn7qCwc/edit</a><br /> <br /> Backstory:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Yi Zhinan is a Lookshyan not born of Lookshy. The distinction has condemned him to the life of a metic, but he did not resent it overly much. Sent to the city at a young age, he proved himself worthy of admission to the Academy of Sorcery by answering a difficult koan that had troubled researchers there. Shortly after earning a brevet commission as a Sorcerer-Engineer, Yi met Karal Zhan, a Terrestrial prodigy and his commanding Chozei. He was instantly enthralled by the young Fire Aspect's passion and compassion toward the lower ranks. Through great effort Yi eventually rose to the rank of Sorcerer-Technician and traded many powerful favors to remain assigned to Zhan's command.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">For two decades, a blink of a eye in a Terrestrial's lifespan and half a lifetime to a mortal, this situation continued into the Battle of the Kumrath. What was originally a small skirmish with some of the Mask of Winter's forces near the hamlet of Kumrath turned into a major engagement when the dead troops turned out to supported by a Deathknight. It was during the battle, with Yi commanding the artillery in a desperate duel with their necromantic counterparts, that Zhan was cut off from support and surrounded. Yi violated direct orders and had his squad turn their fire to support the commander. At the same time he took up the sword of a comrade and rallied the leaderless portion of the Lookshy forces to link back up with the Zhan and drive the enemy back.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">It was in the midst of that frantic charge when Yi rejoined Zhan and finally told him how he felt. In proof that even the Most High can have terrible timing, that was when he took his second breath. There were no more words between them that day, nor between any of Yi's and any of his men. They neither fled nor attacked him. He joined the battle against the Abyssal and none questioned or hindered him. Though the battle was won, spirits were low both from the terrible casualties and from the birth of an Anathema from among their own.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">There were no words on the march home to Lookshy, and there was a great deal of space about him. The general staff was furious for his violation of orders and he was court martialed and sentenced to death. The night before his execution a familiar figure met him in prison bearing a heavy bundle. The items within were all great treasures, no doubt stolen at great personal risk, and the figure left the door open as he departed. One item, seemingly worthless besides the artifacts and chance at freedom, Yi still treasures above all the rest. It is a simply made scroll on which is written the short message. &quot;Family is more than blood.&quot;</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T14:46:51-08:00","id":77830,"title":"","content":"Excellent! Everyone, don't pick on the new guy!<br /> <br /> Exthalion- I see an opportunity to work Yi in here 'n' now. Howe'er, I don't want to presume on character motivation/reasoning etc.. So you can introduce him whenever makes sense to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T17:54:21-08:00","id":77933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CitanHyuga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=77296#post77296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Omni.. are you still playing? You have been really quiet. I feel like I am starting to take over the game by posting all the time, but it has gotten REALLY slow. Should we just stop with the small chat conversations and just jump straight to every point?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aaaaaargh hi guys I'm there<br /> <br /> I am lacking... something to really kick myself into starting again. It's hard. Sudden lack of motivation.<br /> <br /> We have a new player? Hi Exthalion. <br /> <br /> I'm still in, right? I'm going to make an IC post in like... Five minutes, tops.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T14:42:45-08:00","id":78627,"title":"","content":"Exthalion, you should always check the errata of Charms you use. Heartfelt Honorific Opportunity doesn't make social attacks unexpected, it makes them unblockable and undodgeable, which means everyone is eating a full 5wp cost to resist your attack. Which, by RAW, also applies to other PCs.<br /> <br /> Could you please try not to do that in the future? I'd like to avoid constant WP-drain from my own allies D:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T15:12:28-08:00","id":78674,"title":"","content":"I was under the impression that the PCs weren't in the market, I got the feeling they were still at the Gens residence or at the docks. If they were not, I sincerely apologize. As for the errata, I blame Anathema for failing to indicate that there was errata, and my own laziness for failing to check anyway. I apologize for that as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T08:54:19-08:00","id":79348,"title":"","content":"After Hyuga;s rap, I think we just found Creation's answer to Kriss Kross.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T18:15:27-08:00","id":79806,"title":"","content":"At least his clothes weren't on backwards....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T18:46:15-08:00","id":79828,"title":"","content":"I was just happy he didn't dress like this <a href=\"http://cdn.static.ovimg.com/episode/302453.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://cdn.static.ovimg.com/episode/302453.jpg</a> and have a team to carry him in a low-rider palanquin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T19:03:30-08:00","id":79843,"title":"","content":"How would you even have a low-rider palanquin? That doesn't even make sense.<br /> <br /> ... Unless all of the bearers are dwarfs...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T20:13:58-08:00","id":79902,"title":"","content":"The box is supported from the top, hanging from a bar that the bearers hold on their shoulders. Or at least thats what it was in the anime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T20:35:54-08:00","id":79914,"title":"","content":"I suppose that would work. But I find my idea more hilarious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T21:58:09-08:00","id":79971,"title":"","content":"Hyuga is just here to feel all the feels being spread around here. He can't do much against all of them. The downfall of a crafter/swordsman. Only two integrity <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I also use a lot of WP will my charms XD I am going to be screwed in every social battle... lol. I am not so crazy as to have them carry me in on a palanquin or anything XD He serves himself. Others don't as far as he is concerned. <br /> <br /> He just had to make a pathetic attempt to help even though he knew he didn't have the skills. Just the way he is ... makes it more fun anyway. He might just become a brilliant performer yet X","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T07:16:55-08:00","id":80223,"title":"","content":"I know, CitanHyuga, I know, but the idea of Hyuga in loose pants, with a variety of sword-themed pieces of clothing, and a cap tilted to one side, being MC Espada...THAT is pretty funny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T08:20:25-08:00","id":80241,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the double post, but I wanted to say that Tirien's actions just now were the result of my thinking long and hard about how she'd react, and honestly, I couldn't think of any other reaction she would reasonably make, given her upbringing and the situation at hand. <br /> <br /> So, I'm not trying to be passive-aggressive, Exthalion, I really appreciate you and Li's proselytizing is very amusing. It's jsut that Tirien has a hair trigger about some things :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T08:34:59-08:00","id":80260,"title":"","content":"I am afraid I am going to have to call for join battle instead, You did not attempt to establish surprise, and it would be be changing the past for you to do so now, so this wasn't an unexpected attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T09:03:38-08:00","id":80281,"title":"","content":"I apologize, I wasn't meaning any lasting damage with my strike, merely to make contact as a means of showing off. <br /> <br /> I will, however, roll join battle, just so everything is square.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T09:06:30-08:00","id":80283,"title":"","content":"No need to join battle. I'll allow it, as it makes sense in a narrative context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T09:48:55-08:00","id":80306,"title":"","content":"Was the attack unexpected (thus meaning my dvs are set to 0), was any damage done and how much, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T10:03:23-08:00","id":80323,"title":"","content":"No, the attack was not unexpected (surprising perhaps, but not &quot;Unexpected&quot;). I would be hard-pressed to find a way that you could defend against it, however, given your low Dodge- and Martial Arts-based DVs, and your lack of a weapon to make your Melee based DV (and corresponding charms) applicable. <br /> <br /> Judging from the tone of the initial post, I would not have had it do (mechanical) damage anyway (Yi probably has a nice bruise though). Dietaku's later post (64 in this thread) appears to indicate Tirien's intention was merely to make the strike connect, as is common in many a culture's Challenge rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T13:48:03-08:00","id":80479,"title":"","content":"I will have to train the people better. I meant that public shaming and call to action would have sent them all running to do those things I suggested. Oh well, Subtle Pavlov's Conditioning will have to wait.<br /> <br /> Edit: What exactly is a duel of coup? I know the word means hit/strike but is this a specific historical or Exalted thing that I just haven't seen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 02-26-2014, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T14:51:44-08:00","id":80527,"title":"","content":"Query, ST-man: What constitutes &quot;First Blood&quot; mechanically?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T15:17:05-08:00","id":80550,"title":"","content":"First blood constitutes the first person to deal at least one level of Lethal or Aggravated damage, or deal at least one level of Bashing Damage with an appropriate stunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T15:29:27-08:00","id":80563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=80479#post80479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: What exactly is a duel of coup? I know the word means hit/strike but is this a specific historical or Exalted thing that I just haven't seen?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, didn't see this until now. The only time I've seen the term used in any context of exalted is Counting Coup, a Lunar dueling tradition that was started in the First Age by the Swords of Luna, and later adopted by the rest of the Silver Pact as a means of non-lethally settling disputes.<br /> <br /> So basically, a non-lethal duel. Usually to first blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T18:50:50-08:00","id":80693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted Core, p. 148</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">STEP FIVE: SUBTRACT EXTERNAL PENALTIES/<br /> APPLY SPECIAL DEFENSES<br /> At this point in attack resolution, the attacker\u2019s player<br /> applies valid external penalties to the roll. The target\u2019s DV<br /> is always the last of these. If the defender is blocking or<br /> dodging, apply her highest DV as the last of these penalties.<br /> The defender\u2019s player may attempt to describe the defense in<br /> order to obtain a stunt bonus, generating a number of dice<br /> added as a static value directly to DV. Similarly, Charms such<br /> as Essence Overwhelming may provide dice to the same effect.<br /> Any other defensive effects that require a dice roll also<br /> occur during this step, except those involving a reroll. <b>If the<br /> attacker has no successes remaining, the attack misses or the<br /> defender manages to deflect it, as appropriate.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Emphasis mine","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T19:34:43-08:00","id":80719,"title":"","content":"After re-reading all the text, I see that in one spot it does say that it would miss if the DV is the same as the attack successes. It is supported in two spots. The DV is not a difficulty and is subtracted from the attack pool and must have at least 1 sux left over. However, in other text it mentions that all successes are added to dmg and implicates that the attack would hit. I am so used to having an attack hit if DV and accuracy pool is the same. It seems the book says both are correct. XD Gotta love all the ambiguity and contradictions in the book sometimes. It also mentions stuff about mortals automatically not hitting if the attack pool is LOWER than the DV of the exalt. I'm wondering if the attack sux being the same is a matter of fighting a mortal/extra or another exalted. This just got way too confusing lol.<br /> <br /> Since both seem to be correct according to the book, I would say that the ST has to decide. Not much else we can do when both are said to be correct in the book :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T20:20:31-08:00","id":80748,"title":"","content":"I asked on the IRC and got this response:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Consolas\">[20:18] &lt;Exthalion&gt; Quick question: If the successes on an attack roll equal the defender's DV, does it fail or go through? Either way, where is the page reference for this?</span></span> <hr /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Consolas\">[20:19] &lt;<span style=\"color:red\">Holden_</span>&gt; Exthalion: Fails. The DV removes successes, so if they were equal, that would leave you with 0 successes.<br /> <br /> Now please excuse me while I go sacrifice the agreed upon goats to the Hamster god.</span></span><br /> <br /> Edit: I want to make it clear that I will gladly accept Noodle's ruling, but I made my choices due to my belief based on the quoted rules text above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 02-27-2014, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T12:40:15-08:00","id":81175,"title":"","content":"I just hope there's no bad blood between us now. Truth be told, Noodle and I (We're both in the same IRL gaming group) have often played fast and loose with a number of the rules, and I guess that came over here. I hope we can all continue having fun together, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T13:07:07-08:00","id":81192,"title":"","content":"Godamn, Exalted is a mess of contradictory rules and text isn't it? And I will be the first to admit that I'm not a master of 2e rules (but seriously who is? It's such an ungainly mess. A beautifully awesome ungainly mess, but still an ungainly mess.).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=81175#post81175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Truth be told, Noodle and I (We're both in the same IRL gaming group) have often played fast and loose with a number of the rules, and I guess that came over here.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, I suppose it has. You left out CitanHyuga, though. <br /> <br /> After much deliberation, I've decided to keep going how I intended. Difficulty is difficulty is difficulty, and it complicates things needlessly (I feel) to make exceptions. If you want, Exthalion, you can alter Yi's action as desired now that you know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T14:40:30-08:00","id":81244,"title":"","content":"Why would there be bad blood? As for the ruling: fine by me so long as it is consistent. Will this affect other things like artifact crafting where only threshold success matter contribute to finishing?<br /> <br /> I will be activating Dipping Swallow Defense for 2m to bring my DV up to 11 thus causing the attack to fail. I will post my attack in a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T15:23:03-08:00","id":81268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=81244#post81244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would there be bad blood? As for the ruling: fine by me so long as it is consistent. Will this affect other things like artifact crafting where only threshold success matter contribute to finishing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rereading the artifact creation rules in Oadenol's Codex, it looks to me like all successes count for the artifact creation, so long as each individual roll passes the set Difficulty. It looks like the only time threshold successes come into play is when trying to get extra dice through reverse engineering. From what I can see ATM, there's no issue, but if you find one, point it out for me, please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T17:25:38-08:00","id":81332,"title":"","content":"When crafting, if you get a certain number of threshold success, it can raise the rating of the item in question. As Noodle said, all rolls count toward the total as long as the roll surpasses the difficulty. If your roll doesn't meet it, you still get those successes, but it introduces a flaw or lowers the rating of said item/artifact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T19:15:34-08:00","id":81362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=81268#post81268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rereading the artifact creation rules in Oadenol's Codex, it looks to me like all successes count for the artifact creation, so long as each individual roll passes the set Difficulty. It looks like the only time threshold successes come into play is when trying to get extra dice through reverse engineering. From what I can see ATM, there's no issue, but if you find one, point it out for me, please.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can hear game balance cracking in half. At least at our level that will something like double the speed at which they are made. None of the discussions I have seen online are THAT generous in their assumptions. (Not that I mind more power as a crafter)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T19:49:30-08:00","id":81374,"title":"","content":"This is why I always wondered why people said that it took too much for crafters. With certain charms... you can make basic things so quickly. It is true that you can't make every type of craft quickly without combining, but it is not hard to do so quickly if you focus on it. The only thing is that artifacts require exotic ingredients. That should take most of the time. You can do rolls for an idea on an artifact at any time. It can only add up to 1/4 of the total though. You then need the materials to finish the rest of experimenting and crafting the actual object. With essence 4 I craft 12x faster with craftsman needs no tools. If I had decided to go FULL craft and gotten 5 essence and the wonder-forging genius charms I would be making artifact 5 items 15x faster. The problem would be collecting exotic ingredients. At least now I have some power to go out and try to get some without as much worry. It is also good to have some ability to fight being exalted and all. Reading the codex is key for crafters","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T21:17:36-08:00","id":81404,"title":"","content":"I'm not seeing anything in the books that contradicts what I'm saying. Could you post the page number for whatever contradictory information, just so everyone can get onto the same page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T21:20:58-08:00","id":81405,"title":"","content":"I wasn't contradicting anything you are saying at all... I was agreeing with you XD I was just adding extra information in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T21:36:02-08:00","id":81413,"title":"","content":"Sorry, communication error. I was indicating Exthalion, regarding how my ruling broke the balance of the crafting system in half.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T21:49:15-08:00","id":81416,"title":"","content":"Let me try to break it down. 1. Almost no one allows flaws a Wp 10 is so useful and bp/xp effidient that not taking it is almost deliberately weakening you character.As such E4 is usually unobtainable at char gen, to say nothing of E5. 2. Crafting requires three abilities and three attributes to all be kept high. Even for a Twilight that is 15 of your starting 28 dots. 3. The base craft interval for artifacts is a season, or 75 days. E5 reducesthat to five days, which is again almost never seen. The essence for CNNT, the excellency, and whatever charms is committed for that entire time. This can be very inconvenient in normal play and most STs don't give months of downtime. 4. Assume you don't use the difficulty success to total houserule Noodle is, the successes can be hard to build up. Assuming an attribute+ability pool of 10, 3 dice specialty, 2 dice stunt, and five successes from the second excellency you will average 12.5 succeses. At art 5's difficulty of 7 you average 5.5 successes per five day roll. It will only take you transhuman smithing god 227.3 days to complete your world shaping wonder. Hope you aren't on a deadline (you probably are). Also, those exotic material components require at least one adventure of their own, with the Wyld being the only quasi-reliable source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T21:59:21-08:00","id":81419,"title":"","content":"What I'm saying is, everywhere I look in the crafting sections it say the project has to accumulate a certain number of total successes. From what I gather from your statements, you perceive that it is only the threshold successes (or the successes gotten on each roll past the difficulty) that apply to the completion of the project. I'm looking for an example that supports that particular claim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T21:59:38-08:00","id":81420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=81413#post81413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, communication error. I was indicating Exthalion, regarding how my ruling broke the balance of the crafting system in half.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sorry to double post, but my phone does like forums. Crafting is an extended roll which per page 122. Only adds threshold successes to the cumulative successes. Which leads to the prior posts points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T17:37:32-08:00","id":81834,"title":"","content":"I hope that third one doesn't mean I have to buy dots in socialize XD He's not gonna like that training... lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14