jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T09:29:29-07:00","id":111547,"title":"","content":"True, but given that Dietaku and CitanHyuga both maxed out their Derail ability, I had to dump a ton of exp into Improv and Improv charms to keep competitive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T10:15:01-07:00","id":111589,"title":"","content":"I somehow always manage to have 4 specialty points in derailing even though it should be a max of 3... It makes things more entertaining though. That is how you wake up hecton-kyres and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T11:51:13-07:00","id":111654,"title":"","content":"I shall have to put more points into my derail ability as well. Right now I am stuck at, &quot;Throw out W-ECT to get me declared dictator for life.&quot; and following it up with &quot;Implement a Stalinist style Five Year Plan to drag Novalesk into technological parity with Lookshy so I can begin acting on my expansionist ambitions.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"