onyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T17:05:54-07:00","id":113019,"title":"","content":"The specific foundry to distill the magical materials from their source material is Resources 4, with Resources 3 being expended with each use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T18:37:43-07:00","id":113055,"title":"","content":"Don't forget the 16 xp for the second degree of of the art of alchemy. Also, weren't the orichalcum mirrors Resources 4 by themselves?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T19:07:49-07:00","id":113062,"title":"","content":"Or you can get a single ritual for 1 EXP. Plus, I allow each ritual to act as a 'down payment' towards learning that associated Art. 'Cause to do otherwise would be stupid. <br /> <br /> Apologies, for being unspecific. The Sidebar in Oadenol's Codex said that the foundry to distill each magical material is Resources 4, which in Orichalcum's case would be the Mirrors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T19:59:28-07:00","id":113086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=113062#post113062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you can get a single ritual for 1 EXP. Plus, I allow each ritual to act as a 'down payment' towards learning that associated Art. 'Cause to do otherwise would be stupid.<br /> <br /> Apologies, for being unspecific. The Sidebar in Oadenol's Codex said that the foundry to distill each magical material is Resources 4, which in Orichalcum's case would be the Mirrors.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that was already the rule, that once you picked up 8 rituals (if Occult was favored) you could trade them in for a degree. This does actually make for a strange game in chargen where you can get degrees for fewer bp by trading in rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T18:48:16-07:00","id":117303,"title":"","content":"Exthalion- Yi's roll is noted, and it's result quantified. That result won't be revealed until one or more of the PCs encounters it's effect howe'er. Just letting you know so you aren't concerned that I missed it or am ignoring it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T20:16:34-07:00","id":117352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=117303#post117303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exthalion- Yi's roll is noted, and it's result quantified. That result won't be revealed until one or more of the PCs encounters it's effect howe'er. Just letting you know so you aren't concerned that I missed it or am ignoring it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem, I guess it wouldn't be dramatic since the charm says that it doesn't affect individuals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 04-21-2014, 11:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T17:40:04-07:00","id":119450,"title":"","content":"I know its my own fault for throwing around country shaping social magic, but I am suddenly really afraid of Sidereal assassins. The fact that we apparently had one who isn't here anymore only enhances this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T17:40:35-07:00","id":119451,"title":"","content":"I present Novalesk Map, Take 2<br /> <a href=\"http://s610.photobucket.com/user/cael_vedaire/media/Novalesk-1.png.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://i610.photobucket.com/albums/tt189/cael_vedaire/Novalesk-1.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> Here's a map of Novalesk and the surrounding area. Each 'dot' represents a city or large town (pretty much anything that would be considered Magnitude 2+ in MoH rules). Red is Novalesk, Yellow Theros, Grey Ordon, Green Geherin. The Purple arrow is the direction of attack from the Fae.<br /> <br /> Brown lines are major thoroughfares, generally stone roads where you'll find a lot of traffic. Dashed lines represent the <b>legal</b> national boundaries; Ordon for example, has de-facto control of significantly more territory between it and the Geherin's forests.<br /> <br /> Above all, remember that this is an approximation, designed to illustrate the rough positions of the nations and cities relative to each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T17:44:45-07:00","id":119455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=119450#post119450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know its my own fault for throwing around country shaping social magic, but I am suddenly really afraid of Sidereal assassins. The fact that we apparently had one who isn't here anymore only enhances this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kehkehkehkeh.<br /> <br /> ... Well, the fact that there's at least two GF Siddies paying attention to the problem means that it will be a while before anything passes the desk of a Bronze. I would be more concerned about the Realm Garrison next door, where I you.<br /> <br /> Or home-grown assassins. They can kill you dead too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T17:52:03-07:00","id":119458,"title":"","content":"I just realized that like an idiot, I haven't been keeping proper track of experience. I know I haven't earned stunt experience.... how much should I have? XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T18:13:36-07:00","id":119474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CitanHyuga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=119458#post119458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just realized that like an idiot, I haven't been keeping proper track of experience. I know I haven't earned stunt experience.... how much should I have? XD</div> </div> </div> </div>I've handed out 9 exp, + Stunts. +1 day to training too, which should finish off both Hyuga and Yi's charm training, IIRC. <br /> <br /> Actually, this is a good time to end 'Session 3'. So, +5 exp to everyone, making the total 14, +stunts. <br /> <br /> While I'm thinking on it, I'm considering adding in a secondary EXP growth, independent of my current 'arbitrary session' + 3 die exp. <br /> <br /> Your thoughts, and criteria suggestions?<br /> <br /> Also, I've been considering allowing Evocations, if y'all desire them. I think they would be helpful to Hyuga and Yi, at least, since they would help you 'power' up your diakliaves. <br /> <br /> Thoughts on this too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T18:27:13-07:00","id":119480,"title":"","content":"KK.. 14 then.. thanks. I will start a bit of new training as well. Since I am not all that great at stunting above 1 dice that secondary way might help me a lot XD<br /> <br /> I hadn't tested 3e with evocations... I don't know how they work. It might be interesting and helpful. They could be like upgrades to the weapon...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T18:31:39-07:00","id":119483,"title":"","content":"I was just thinking of something along the lines of 2E style Charm trees... only for your weapons/armor. Like upgrades for them, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T18:34:06-07:00","id":119486,"title":"","content":"How would the exp cost be? And would they be small mote charges, or regular?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T18:44:00-07:00","id":119494,"title":"","content":"Exp? I would think Favored Charm cost for artifacts incorporating resonant materials, Unfavored for all others.<br /> <br /> Mote costs, I would be roughly the same as the wielders' charms, I think. So smallish for Solars, a bit larger for Sidereals and Lunars, and a bit larger than that for DBs.<br /> <br /> This is one of the reasons I was considering a secondary EXP growth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T18:55:17-07:00","id":119503,"title":"","content":"I think I am going to bank my xp for the moment. E4 is 24 xp, or the cost of three charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T19:10:58-07:00","id":119507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=119503#post119503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I am going to bank my xp for the moment. E4 is 24 xp, or the cost of three charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>No You have to spend it! Spend it ALL!!1!! <br /> <br /> Sure, man. It's your character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T19:23:21-07:00","id":119511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=119507#post119507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No You have to spend it! Spend it ALL!!1!!<br /> <br /> Sure, man. It's your character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, I will need to accomplish my motivation to get the training time discount.<br /> <br /> But I can totally end the Age of Sorrows by the time I get 16 more xp right?<br /> <br /> Edit: Mind if I change what I say? Yi would never be so forthright before the goddess. Which is a bad thing I suppose, considering it means he treats people different based on their station. Or perhaps he is just more honest with humans and pretends at politeness for important people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 04-25-2014, 10:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T19:42:39-07:00","id":119517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=119511#post119511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Mind if I change what I say? Yi would never be so forthright before the goddess. Which is a bad thing I suppose, considering it means he treats people different based on their station. Or perhaps he is just more honest with humans and pretends at politeness for important people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T02:22:48-07:00","id":119647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=119517#post119517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Much obliged<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=119507#post119507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No You have to spend it! Spend it ALL!!1!!<br /> <br /> Sure, man. It's your character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gah! Why must your command move me to action?<br /> <br /> What do you think of this?<br /> <br /> GOLDEN OVERSEER'S MANDATE<br /> Cost: -; Mins: Craft 5, Essence 3; Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instantaneous<br /> Prerequisite Charms: One of Craftsmen Needs No Tools or Crack Mending Technique<br /> The designs of the Lawgivers are in harmony with the essence of the world. When overseeing a workforce no greater in magnitude then their essence, the Chosen may apply the benefits of this charms prerequisites to the whole project. Seeming mistakes in workmanship prove advantageous, no tool is ever misplaced, orders are never misunderstood, and thousands of other minor problems which normally slow work are washed away in the excellence the Lawgiver lends to his assistants. The cost of this charms prerequisite must be committed at the beginning of the project. If commitment lapses for any reason this charm may not be applied again to that task and the workers slow to normal speed.<br /> <br /> At Essence 4 this charm may be repurchased. Doing so grants this charm the stackable keyword, allowing the lawgiver to enhance an number of distinct projects equal to his essence so long as he commits requisite motes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 03-21-2015, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T19:22:35-07:00","id":122148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=119647#post119647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think of this?<br /> <br /> GOLDEN OVERSEER'S MANDATE<br /> Cost: -; Mins: Craft 5, Essence 3; Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instantaneous<br /> Prerequisite Charms: One of Craftsmen Needs No Tools or Crack Mending Technique<br /> The designs of the Lawgivers is at harmony with the essence of the world. When overseeing a workforce no greater in magnitude then their essence, the Chosen may apply the benefits of this charms prerequisites to the whole project. Seeming mistakes in workmanship prove advantageous, no tool is ever misplaced, orders are never misunderstood, and thousands of other minor problems which normally slow work are washed away in the excellence the Lawgiver lends to his assistants. The cost of this charms prerequisite must be committed at the beginning of the project. If commitment lapses for any reason this charm may not be applied again to that task and the workers slow to normal speed.<br /> <br /> At Essence 4 this charm may be repurchased. Doing so grants this charm the stackable keyword, allowing the lawgiver to enhance an number of distinct projects equal to his essence so long as he commits requisite motes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, didn't see your edit till today. <br /> <br /> [Judging]...[/judging] <br /> <br /> Seems legit to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T14:17:19-07:00","id":124759,"title":"","content":"To avoid a back and forth in the IC, can you give me the lowdown on all the gen? Things like location, major source of income, political positions, that sort of thing. When I break them like pots with a rod of iron I want to make sure I have leverage first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T20:37:36-07:00","id":124953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=124759#post124759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To avoid a back and forth in the IC, can you give me the lowdown on all the gen? Things like location, major source of income, political positions, that sort of thing. When I break them like pots with a rod of iron I want to make sure I have leverage first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like this?<br /> <br /> Map, for reference<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">[URL=&quot;http://s610.photobucket.com/user/cael_vedaire/media/Novalesk-1.png.html&quot;]<img src=\"http://i610.photobucket.com/albums/tt189/cael_vedaire/Novalesk-1.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Gens Ptreas</b><br /> <b>Population</b>: ~11000 (6 Boule Seats)<br /> <b>Capital</b>: Greheisolonikon; Cut down to Greheis or Grey Ice colloquially. (Northernmost Novaleski city on map)<br /> <b>Major Industries</b>: Following in their founder's footsteps, Gens Ptreas' major industries are <i>Architecture and Engineering</i>. Most structures in Novalesk are designed and/or built by this Gens. Likewise, their capital was positioned to gain easy access to a number of large quarries and the northern forests, ensuring access to the tools of their trade. <br /> <b>Political Position:</b> Gens Ptreas generally keeps out of Capital politics, and as such lack long-term political alliances with many other Gentes. Gens Spyrus holds a great deal of gratitude for Ptreas, however, as this Gens sheltered the refugees that became Gens Spyrus in the late 3rd century post-contagion. Ptreas has four cadet houses (a high number, most Gentes only have one or two) which effectively double its population. Because of this, Ptreas alternates between advocating for allowing the absorption of cadet houses into their Patron houses and allotting Boule seats based on the population of the Gens and its cadet families. This earns the ire of Gens Althea, who has no cadet houses. <br /> <b>Cadet Families</b>: Palve (~1200), Ruzha (~2700), Melitta (~3100) Kolinos (~3500)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T20:59:08-07:00","id":124964,"title":"","content":"<b>Gens Spyrus</b><br /> <b>Population</b>: ~10000 (5 Boule Seats)<br /> <b>Capital: </b>Spyron (across river, South of Novalesk City)<br /> <b>Major Industries:</b> Descended from a group of nomadic refugees from the north, Gens Spyrus sells their <i>Audacity and Resilience</i>. This Gens maintains several mercenary companies that travel far and wide in the Hundred Kingdoms. The Gens is also skilled metal-workers, maintaining several foundry complexes throughout the nation. The Gens holds an indefinite duration contract, naming them the primary supplier of the national troops' weaponry. Many other Gentes hire Spyrus trainers for their men and buy Spyrus weapons to outfit them.<br /> <b>Political Position: </b>Being to small and non-influential to effect the overall course of the nation, Spyrus has become something of a 'free agent', siding with whichever power bloc makes them the best deal at the time. This has given them a somewhat mercenary reputation. The closest thing they have to an ally is Ptreas, for whom Gens Spyrus believes it owes a blood debt. Spyrus as a whole believes that the nation needs a stronger central government, but they trust neither Zophyrus or Nikoloi to run it.<br /> <b>Cadet Families</b>: Zorica (~4000)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T20:59:46-07:00","id":124966,"title":"","content":"<b>Gens Nikoloi<br /> Population: </b>~26000 (13 Boule Seats)<br /> <b>Capital: </b>Serres (first city north of Novalesk City)<br /> <b>Major Industries:</b> Nikoloi continued their founder's heritage, being the most scholarly Gens in the nation. Indeed, the Academy of Sorcerous Wisdom, despite being a national institution, is owned by Gens Nikoloi, and leased to Novlaesk. The Gens' main industry, however, is <i>Trade</i>. Early in the nation's history, a member of the Nikoloi family discovered a rich silver vein. The family took this windfall and invested in building a fleet of trade vessels and construction a network of strong stone roads between the major townships. With control over the nation's arterials, the family gained a strangelhold on internal carrying trade. <br /> <b>Political Position</b><b>: </b>Gens Nikoloi strongly belieives that there should be a stronger central government, with itself at the head. It has the lukewarm support of Gens Midea in this regard. Otherwise, Nikoloi's political policies tend to direct it towards more complete control the nation's financial system. Nikoloi also advocates often for a closer relationship with Theros, most likely to secure additional foreign markets. Nikoloi has a strongly negative opinion of the Geherin. <br /> <b>Cadet Families:</b> Pachis (~2000), Bojani (~900)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","user":"Noodle","date":". 05-04-2014, 12:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T21:00:20-07:00","id":124967,"title":"","content":"<b>Gens Midea<br /> Population: </b>~14000 (7 Boule Seats)<br /> <b>Capital: </b>Pirae (East of Novalesk City)<br /> <b>Major Industries:</b> Descended from a shapeshifter of indeterminable origins, Gens Midea was a Nikoloi cadet house until the mid sixth century post-contagion. Much like their progenitor, Gens Midea believes strongly in <i>V</i><i>ersatility and Flexibility</i>. As such, they have a highly well-rounded economic portfolio. This synergizes well with Gens Nikoloi, as they can provide a wide variety of goods for Nikoloi merchants. <br /> <b>Political Position: </b>As fitting its former position as a Nikoloi cadet house, Gens Midea is still content to mostly follow Nikoloi's lead. Midea, however, often advocates for increased military activity, especially against Ordon and Theros. This creates some friction between Midea and Nikoloi, but Midea has seen fit to continue to support Nikoloi's power bloc for the time being. <br /> <b>Cadet Families: </b>Diotus (~1300), Oglica (~800)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","user":"Noodle","date":". 05-04-2014, 12:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T21:01:01-07:00","id":124969,"title":"","content":"<b>Gens Zophyrus<br /> Population: </b>~27000 (14 Boule Seats)<br /> <b>Capital: </b>Agio (Central Novlaesk; land-locked)<br /> <b>Major Industries</b>: Gens Zophyrus dominates Novalesk's <i>Agriculture</i>. Their capital city was purposely located to this effect, giving the family easy access to the fields of central Novlaesk. The Gens controls many farms and ranches, and supplies a majority of the nation's food. <br /> <b>Political Position: </b>Zophyrus resents Nikoloi's control over the carrying trade, as it cuts into their profit margins as Novalesk's breadbasket. Due to its position in Novalesk's interior, Zophyrus is somewhat desensitized to the military tensions between Novalesk and its neighbors. Due to Nikoloi's reluctance to trade with the Ordon, and Ordon's near-constant desire for foodstuffs, Zophyrus has begun dominating trade with Novalesk's southern neighbor. This hurts their relationship with Spyrus and Midea, who have borne the brunt of Novalesk's somewhat frequent wars with the Ordoni.<br /> <b>Cadet Families: </b>Metaxas (~2300), Arcadios (~700)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","user":"Noodle","date":". 05-04-2014, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T21:01:43-07:00","id":124970,"title":"","content":"<b>Gens Althea<br /> Population: </b>~9000 (5 Boule Seats)<br /> <b>Capital: </b>Vera (North-east Novalesk; farthest from Novalesk City on bank of Lake)<br /> <b>Major Industries</b>: Althea's primary industry revolves around <i>Raw Material Collection</i>. Althea operates many mines and lumber camps outside of Novalesk's nominal borders, ensuring a steady supply of raw goods to the other Gentes' artisans. Althea also has negotiated trade agreements with the handful of nomadic barbarian tribes to the East, gaining access to even more material. <br /> <b>Political Position: </b>Gens Althea is an elevated Cadet House, formerly under the patronage of Gens Zophyrus. Elevated in the early eighth century post-contagion, many within Althea have yet to grasp yet that they are no longer bound to their former patron's will. Althea tends to follow Zophyrus in lockstep. Their one notable divergence is their positive relationship with the Geherin, who Zophyrus dislikes due to tensions between the barbarian confederation and Ordon.<br /> <b>Cadet Families: </b>None","signature":"","edited":{"userid":155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","user":"Noodle","date":". 05-04-2014, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T09:33:02-07:00","id":125202,"title":"","content":"Yes, that is exactly what I was looking for. If it wouldn't be too much trouble, one of those for Novalesk itself would also be useful.<br /> <br /> I am getting the feeling that thinking of Navalesk as a nation might be a mistake. The Gens seem independent and powerful enough to act more like independent domains who agree to cooperate on matters of mutual interests.<br /> <br /> My current plan is to propose a stronger central government with myself as nominal head. This way none of them will look like they are making a power grab by supporting me. In private I will promise Spyrus, Zophyrus, and Nikoloi all the important possitions in government. In actuality, the possitions will be split to all the Gens based on merit and talent.<br /> <br /> The balance of the promsied offices will have high sounding titles with high nominal authority and no real power. When anything goes wrong I will have perfect justification for dismissing them and removing the offices.<br /> <br /> To sweeten the deal with Nikoloi and ultimately Midea, I will promise the annexation of both Theros and Ordon. That promise is much easier to pull off given that I will be supreme executive of Novalesk a few days after arival. When I am explaining myself, my social magic is strong enough to get them to believe that they got what they wanted.<br /> <br /> Might need to update this once I see the other two gens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T11:33:33-07:00","id":125260,"title":"","content":"Broken down for ease of reading<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=125202#post125202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that is exactly what I was looking for. If it wouldn't be too much trouble, one of those for Novalesk itself would also be useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was in the process of doing this, you just altered the order. I was in the process of doing the neighboring nations, then I was going to do Novalesk, then the Gentes. Novalesk is coming soon. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=125202#post125202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am getting the feeling that thinking of Navalesk as a nation might be a mistake. The Gens seem independent and powerful enough to act more like independent domains who agree to cooperate on matters of mutual interests.</div> </div> </div> </div>... Not quite. This is why I was planning on doing Novalesk itself first. The profiles given where deliberately crafted to highlight the points of friction and differences between the Gentes, and as such fail to take into account the similarities.<br /> <br /> I would call them a Confederation, but that implies a much higher level of independence than they actually have. It would probably be most accurate to say that they're similar to the American States in the first half-century or so post independence. Largely culturally homogeneous, financially and militarily interdependent. Sure they compete politically and economically, but ultimately they know they're in the same boat together, and mostly they're willing to (begrudgingly) play by the central government's rules. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=125202#post125202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My current plan is to propose a stronger central government with myself as nominal head. This way none of them will look like they are making a power grab by supporting me. In private I will promise Spyrus, Zophyrus, and Nikoloi all the important possitions in government. In actuality, the possitions will be split to all the Gens based on merit and talent.<br /> <br /> The balance of the promsied offices will have high sounding titles with high nominal authority and no real power. When anything goes wrong I will have perfect justification for dismissing them and removing the offices.<br /> <br /> To sweeten the deal with Nikoloi and ultimately Midea, I will promise the annexation of both Theros and Ordon. That promise is much easier to pull off given that I will be supreme executive of Novalesk a few days after arival. When I am explaining myself, my social magic is strong enough to get them to believe that they got what they wanted.<br /> <br /> Might need to update this once I see the other two gens.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll definitely need to update this when you see the national profiles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T20:45:59-07:00","id":125515,"title":"","content":"<b>-Novalesk-</b><br /> The nation of Novalesk lies along the Rock River, nearly due East of Mount Metagapala. Descended from a handful of survivors of the Dual disasters of the Great Contagion and Balorian Crusade. Founding the town of Novalesk, they slowly grew their numbers, creating a number splinter towns, a handful of which evolved into cities in their own right. <br /> <br /> The people of Novalesk are, generally speaking, a rough and practical people, lacking in ostentation. This does not make them stupid or provincial; Novalesk has a proud scholarly tradition, dating back centuries. Nor do they despise art, though they much prefer solid, lasting art like statuary and tapestry to more transient art forms. They are stubborn and resilient, though, and that has let them survive and even thrive the strife of the Second Age. <br /> <br /> <b>-Society-</b><br /> There are three classes in Novlaesk: The Citizen, The National, and the Metic. Nationals and Citizens are members of the Gentes and their Cadet Houses, with the only difference between them being that all Citizens are essence users. The Nationals and citizens each have the same Rights, but the Citizens have the franchise and are able to elect Representatives to the Boule, and any Citizen may attend and address the Boule. Metics are resident aliens, who have been granted leave to live and work in Novalesk. <br /> <br /> The great houses of Novalesk are the six Gentes. Each Gens contains a cross section of society, from the lowest beggar to the richest aristocrat. The Gentes gain representation in the Boule assembly based on relative population, and may sponsor Metic families (most commonly large groups of refugees) into 'Cadet Family' status. Members of Cadet Families are considered Citizens or Nationals, though their Representatives to the Boule are merely sanctioned observers. Cadet Houses are generally subservient to their sponsor, though some friction between the two is inevitable. <br /> <br /> Blood ties are highly important to Novalesk; a Cadet Family is only risen Great House Status when the Boule believes that that family integrated their bloodlines and culture with that of the original Novalesk population (With Gens Spyrus being a notable exception, as it was founded before the inception of the Cadet house system). <br /> <br /> <b>-Government-</b><br /> The Legal authority within each city is the ruling Gens, who each have their own methods for creating and enforcing law. Gens law, however, is superseeded by and cannot contradict National law, who are laid down from two sources: The Archon and the Boule. <br /> <br /> The Boule consists of fifty Representatives, each elected by their Gens' Citizen population from the Citizen population. The Boule may pass and redact legislation, as well as ordering the Strategoi. The Boule also sets the taxation rate, as well as any tariffs and trade duties. The Boule also elects a new Archon upon the death, ascension or resignation of the previous Archon (A vote requiring a 60% majority). <br /> <br /> The Archon (who is elected for life) has supreme executive authority in Novalesk, and may appoint and order the Strategoi. The Archon also holds the powers of high, middle and low justice, and is the sole person capable of authorizing binding treaties between Novalesk and any other external power. The Archon may also appoint up to three subordinates, known as Thesmothetes. Each Thesmothete has a lesser set of executive authority, and may speak on their master's behalf. Their power derives from the Archon, however, who may disavow them and their actions at any time. All Thesmothetes are dismissed with the termination of the appointing Archon. An Archon must be a citizen, but in at least two occasions, the Boule has granted citizen status to a national in order to elect them. <br /> <br /> <b>-Economy-</b><br /> Novalesk has the resources to see to all of its own economic needs, and then some. It has thriving agricultural, manufacturing and intellectual sectors, largely due to its need to be self-sufficient form its neighbors. Novalesk's one major resource scarcity is iron, though the nation has sufficient copper and tin deposits to make this merely an annoyance. <br /> <br /> It does, however, trade regularly with neighboring nations, albeit at highly variable rates. Novalesk trades manufactured goods to the Geherin in exchange for a vast collection of exotic plants. With Ordon, foodstuffs (particularly grain and game) are traded for technology and lore from the lost ages. With Theros, Novalesk trades thaumaturgical products and the occasional artifact in exchange for iron. <br /> <br /> Novalesk's primary external trade runs up and down the Rock River, facilitated by the Guild. Novalesk's combination of occult knowledge and natural resources makes it a cheap place to obtain thaumaturgical products. Many a Guild ship pulls into Novalesk laid down with luxury goods from Nexus and Great Forks, and leaves laden down with alchemical solutions and thaumaturgical talismans. <br /> <br /> <b>-Military-</b> <br /> Novalesk is the product of its times; as a child of the Age of Strife, it is a military nation. most members of the Gentes are trained in military tactics and weapons when young, and drill regularly throughout their lives. A small number of residents are career soldiers, forming the skeleton of the military. The meat of Novalesk's military, however, comes from the 'cyclers' a relatively large group which signs up for year-long service stints, after which they return to trade for several years before rotating back into the military. This ensures the military is well stocked with trained artisans, as well as allowing for the maintenance of a larger pool of trained soldiers.<br /> <br /> The ruling military power in Novalesk is the Strategoi. While the Archon and the Boule have the powers to command the Strategoi and raise troops, they rarely interfere with them in times of War. The Strategoi have the power to raise troops and command them independently from the Gentes, and with authorization from the Archon, may order the Gentes to place thier household troops at their command.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T21:02:37-07:00","id":125524,"title":"","content":"A note: Anything I post here about setting material (Such as the above profiles) is not necessarily fact. It is information that I feel your characters would be able to parse out given your resources and contacts (At this point, mostly Dero and random people on the streets). While information on the Gentes and Novalesk are generally reliable, information of the neighboring nations will largely be vague and mutually contradictory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T14:39:43-07:00","id":126988,"title":"","content":"IC I am activating Mastery of Small Manners for 1m.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T08:45:23-07:00","id":127500,"title":"","content":"I just noticed something. Only the Enlightened are franchised, Unless I am forgetting something the only way to get enlightened is one of two thaumaturgy procedures, (one short and risky and one long and safe(r)), being born a god/elemental/fae/etc blooded and having that be one of the [things you spent points on], or endowment by some form of spirit or exalted.<br /> <br /> That being the case, how large is the electorate? It can't be very big relative to the population as a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T12:37:22-07:00","id":127665,"title":"","content":"Lets see, there's (as of Canon):<br /> <br /> (1) Endowment Charm(s), including Endowment itself, Soul-Enlightening Benefice and the like.<br /> (2) Charms that allow for the target to use someone else's Essence, which can unlock the target's essence over a month or three depending on luck of the rolls.<br /> (3) Thaumaturgy, two examples: Essence Enlightening Sutra (takes 5 years, no harmful effects), Essential River Channeling (24 hours, has significant risk of mutation/death unless user is Essence User themselves)<br /> (4) Artifacts, War-Devil's Skull is the only listed artifact (Rated 3), but there are others<br /> (5) Drugs, Celestial Cocaine is listed example, but listed continuum for costs: Resources 3 for regimen drugs; 4 for one-use but risky drugs; 5 for one-use relatively harmless drugs.<br /> (6) Birth, as a: god-blood, half-caste, essence channeling sub-species, essence channeling mutant tribe<br /> (7) Wyld exposure<br /> (8) Exalting<br /> (9) Sorcery, as far as I can remember Imbue Amalgam is the only written one, but hey it's a thing.<br /> <br /> In Novalesk, they are used in the following order (3), (2), (5), (6), (4)/(1), (8).<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The most common method is Essence River Channeling, which with an Essence using thamaturge (or two) holds a much lower risk. There are around fifty Geomancers of this skill in the entire nation (and given the cutural predilections you can bet that they're essence channelers).<br /> <br /> A number of Spirits on Origenes' staff (and a few other divine/dead residents) have access to Touch of Divinity (falling under Category 2), and the roll for enlightenment on that is ([Highest Mental] + MA), difficulty 1. Even without any dots in MA, a person with 2-3 dots in their highest mental attribute will likely succeed by the end of a season.<br /> <br /> The number of thaumaturges in the city allow for the production of a reasonable supply of Regimen-type solutions.<br /> <br /> While the Divine population is low compared to cities like Great Forks, this is a nation where gods, elementals and the dead walk openly. Enough people have gotten funky with them over the years to make supernatural blood not-rare.<br /> <br /> The academy owns a handful of artifacts that can grant a holder essence use over time, but they're jealously guarded since they don't know how to replace them.<br /> <br /> Origenes himself has the Endowment charm (a Panoply charm, if you must know), but with a notable downside (that I'm not telling) that prevents him from spamming it 2-3 times a day.<br /> <br /> There are about a half-dozen native DBs in Novalesk as of present. No native celestials (that are known of)</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But I'm digressing. Among the Gentes, around 7% on average. About half that among the cadet houses, and maybe a half-percent among the Metic population. Somewhere around nine, ten thousand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T14:04:30-07:00","id":127710,"title":"","content":"Okay, that IC post is the best I could come up with that should make most of the people present happy. There was a lot of pressure when I saw how much everyone was expecting of me. Why must my obscenely powerful magic work exactly as advertised and in a way so incredibly advantageous to me personally?<br /> <br /> Also, is that 7% on average typical in your conception of well developed nations? Or is Novalesk particularly blessed with Essence users?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T16:14:21-07:00","id":127803,"title":"","content":"Novalesk is particularly blessed when it comes to Essence users. Because they had what is <i>totally not</i> a Twilight as their Founder and a trio of <i>people who were certainly not </i>Half-castes as their ancestors, they've felt a certain desire to place spiritual enlightenment as a cultural strong point. This comes with some downsides, like the fact that a significant portion of their GDP is earmarked towards enlightening people, and Immaculates loathe them. <br /> <br /> Also, note that the 7% is among the Gentes only. A large part of that is the simple fact that they have the resources to invest in those endeavors. Novalesk has a population of about 200k, so the actual percentage is somewhere around 5%. Still high, but a bit smaller. <br /> <br /> Your average well-developed nation likely has somewhere between 10 and 20 essence users per 1000 humans. Places like Great Forks might have something as high as 60 or 70 essence users per 1000 humans across the board. Highly Immaculate nations like Lookshy and the Realm will be on the lower end, but they're more likely to have thriving Terrestrial bloodlines, so they'll have individually stronger people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T18:27:08-07:00","id":127889,"title":"","content":"Considering that the Roman Imperium had around 600-1K voters through the Senate, Novalesk with it's 5-7% Essence Franchise is actually quite generous. This also takes into account the possibility of upward mobility through distinction and hard work, which Origennes and the Priesthood seem keen to propagate. Of course, this is also knowing that Novalesk, through its cultural mores as seen, its vocabulary and its society are Not<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Attica\" target=\"_blank\">Attica</a>. while Geherin and Ordon are <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Picts\" target=\"_blank\">Not-Picts innawoods</a> and North Korea, respectively.<br /> <br /> (I'm Noodle's Brother IRL. He actually asked for my input about the surrounding nations, and Ordon and the Geherin are as much my brainchildren as his.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T18:46:57-07:00","id":127897,"title":"","content":"Hadn't given Geherin and Ordon much thought yet so I couldn't say. As for Novalesk, the oi and os suffixes don't show up in many non Greek inspired places. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I will also enjoy greatly the resulting social upheaval when I reform the education system to make Enlightenment the equivalent of literacy in the modern world.<br /> <br /> Edit: Should we look into recruiting more players? We seem to be down to just three. I don't mind honestly, but some people like a more developed dynamic and we are all playing somewhat separate games at the moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 05-07-2014, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T20:17:37-07:00","id":127947,"title":"","content":"I was actually looking to find a way to bring the extra character back in, but I realized Hyuga wouldn't be able to find her easily and stay in the loop. Hyuga is mostly hiding out, though he will make a move soon. Having another player might help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T20:36:24-07:00","id":127951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=127897#post127897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Should we look into recruiting more players? We seem to be down to just three. I don't mind honestly, but some people like a more developed dynamic and we are all playing somewhat separate games at the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CitanHyuga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=127947#post127947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having another player might help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very well, recruitment is re-opened! We'll see if anyone bites.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CitanHyuga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=127947#post127947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was actually looking to find a way to bring the extra character back in, but I realized Hyuga wouldn't be able to find her easily and stay in the loop. Hyuga is mostly hiding out, though he will make a move soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mind if I made some suggestions? If you do, they're spoiler'd below so you don't have to look at them<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Hyuga could...<br /> ... help get the Academy's production lines rolling<br /> ... help build weapons and armor for troops<br /> ... visit the Salles and Dojos within the city<br /> ... mingle with his fellow Scavenger Lords<br /> ... travel to the front lines and do righteous battle at the side of the valiant Hero of Justice Ba Rai</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T20:59:40-07:00","id":127961,"title":"","content":"I actually have two of those plans mixed together for what I will do. I was going to mingle with scavenger lords and the academy.. while helping production. I was thinking about spreading the word that I am a descendant of the founder overtly. It seemed to work slightly the first time. I'm still not sure how I want to do it. I have an idea though. I'm hoping I can get in on one of the courts though. My social skills SUCK though :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T21:03:55-07:00","id":127964,"title":"","content":"Well, you have Ptreas sponsorship, which could help get you into a Gens court. Also, Maia may be able to help, or at least suggest someone who could.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T21:06:07-07:00","id":127965,"title":"","content":"You could always be a powerless figurehead in MY court, seeing as how I will be Archon by the end of business today.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, I am signaling that I have begun training Wyld Revelry Approach, and will be finished learning it tomorrow. It helps when you can make people like the things you make them do, The Perfect can eat my molten golden dust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T21:07:58-07:00","id":127967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=127965#post127965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could always be a powerless figurehead in MY court, seeing as how I will be Archon by the end of business today.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, I am signaling that I have begun training Wyld Revelry Approach, and will be finished learning it tomorrow. It helps when you can make people like the things you make them do, The Perfect can eat my molten golden dust.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which Gens are you planning on joining?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T22:53:12-07:00","id":128002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=127967#post127967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which Gens are you planning on joining?</div> </div> </div> </div>My own. After all, I have enough social magic to have myself declared a Cadet house then elevated to the Archonship. I believe the polite term is &quot;legal fiction&quot; and the more accurate term is &quot;Tyrant.&quot;<br /> <br /> More seriously, I have a really big plan for the nation which I am not certain I can adequately sell without explaining that I am Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 05-08-2014, 03:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T13:48:24-07:00","id":128493,"title":"","content":"<b>-Geherin-</b><br /> The confederation of the Vicruith clans lives in a densely forested area south-east of the nations of Ordon and Novalesk. They are known to the outsiders as the &quot;Geherin&quot; a word that means &quot;tea-eater&quot; in their tribal dialect. This word is the name of their warrior caste, referencing their consumption of a certain species of tea-leaves before battle. These leaves are said to grant the eater the strength of ten men and steel them against pain. <br /> <br /> The Geherin are a bellicose and bombastic people. They have a proud warrior tradition, as well as a strong love of aural arts. The only people afforded equality to the clan chieftains are their Skalds. <br /> <br /> The Geherin's favored weapon is the bearded axe. Many Geherin will travel into battle with nothing more than a half dozen of these axes, which they will use as both melee and thrown weapons. They rarely fight with any form of formation, as that reduces a warrior's chance for individual glory. <br /> <br /> The clan chieftains each hold absolute power over their clan's territory. The clan chieftains meet in moot once a season to discuss news and trade stories. Any disputes between the clans are adjudicated by the High King, a former chieftain elected for a decade for that sole purpose.<br /> <br /> The Geherin worship a being known as 'The Silver-Horned Mother' who has taken over the local spirit courts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T14:04:10-07:00","id":128507,"title":"","content":"<b>-Ordon-</b><br /> The Glorious Free City of Ordon sits south of Novalesk along the Rock River. This nation consists of three cities (Ordon, Sayat and Ahal from east to west) and numerous outlying communities. In they few instances where Novalesk has waged war on Ordon's soil, those communities were noted to be highly organized and regimented. <br /> <br /> The only interactions that have occurred between Novalesk and Ordon have been between either their military and diplomats. Interactions with the diplomats have hinted as a highly stratified caste-based society. The discipline and precision of their military corps supports this notion. <br /> <br /> The Ordon appear to have a strong technical tradition. Their cities and towns are all walled more often than not, and their nation in crisscrossed with a network of solid stone roads. Their siege engineer rival those of Gens Ptreas in skill and ingenuity. <br /> <br /> Ordon itself if a heavily fortified city with strong walls and magical artillery, though it is much too small to house its purported population. Nevertheless, Ordon devours large amounts of natural resources, and exports only a fraction of that input. Where the rest goes is anyone's guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T14:59:05-07:00","id":128539,"title":"","content":"Geherin is a Lunar Thousand Streams River Project, possibly in their origins and definitely now.<br /> <br /> Ordon is someone's project, and possibly has a connection to the Mountain Folk. Or a factory ruin of some sort. Heck, with our luck its where the Seal of Eight Divinities was broken and the armies of Sova are coming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T15:12:22-07:00","id":128548,"title":"","content":"Here is my first attempt at my Dawn Caste Solar, Jensven Vargsmed. I will edit this post as necessary to update his information.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Concept</b></u><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagN