 the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T14:39:05-07:00","id":137167,"title":"","content":"Agreed. That may be the way to go, Magnusar. <br /> <br /> Anyways, I would like to point out for the record, that I did not intend for the one commoner to become a Noble. However, he rolled so wonderfully, magnificently well (All successes, of which half are tens) that I had to give him something. I mean, if this were a heroic mortal, I probably would have Exalted him for that kind of roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T15:40:17-07:00","id":137280,"title":"","content":"Alright so then I took the sorcery background and do I have to pay to begin with demon already summoned ? I also have backing at 3 what are the organisation or people that could provide such backing in the region ? and would you allow these charms<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Transcendent Mastery of the Arts<br /> Cost: --; Mins: Occult 5, Essence 2; Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: Mirror<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> Mortal thaumaturges must wrestle with the innate energies of Creation to shape reality according to their will, learning to do so a little at a time, but Solar occultists manipulate Essence at a whim--such energies are theirs to command. With study and observation of the arcane principles embedded in the very fabric of the world, a champion of the Sun's insight far surpasses the life's work of a mortal mind in mere days. Upon learning this Charm, the Solar learns all Arts of Thaumaturgy as though he had accumulated the Initiate Degrees of the 11 Arts. This Charm can be repurchased two more times for the Adept and master Degrees.<br /> <br /> <br /> Demon Binding Magnificence<br /> Cost: -; Mins: Occult 5, Essence 3; Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Varies<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Spirit-Cutting Attack<br /> After the defeat of the Primordial, the Unconquered Sun in his wisdom allowed his chosen to summon their defeated forms in the management of creation. Many of the Chosen used these Demons to great effect. Occasionally the summoning would go amiss and this would lead to unnecessary complications for the newly formed Solar Nation.<br /> This charm can be taken three times, once after each time he has learned a new circle of sorcery. This charm increases the Solar\u2019s ability to summon Demons in the following ways.<br /> This charm increases the dice pool of the Solar for the summoning contest by 2 per time the charm has been purchased.<br /> In the event of failure, this charm reduces the difficulty of a banishment check by 1. If the check is reduced to zero the demon is banished automatically.<br /> This charm only works on summoned demons and has no bearing on Elementals<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 05-14-2014, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T16:22:26-07:00","id":137323,"title":"","content":"Okay, let's take this one thing at a time.<br /> <br /> (1) You can have one First Circle summoned with you from the get-go.<br /> <br /> (2) Organizations that you can have backing from:<br /> (a)The Cult of the Illuminated (which would make an excellent source of Sorcery knowledge in the future)<br /> (b)The Guild<br /> (c)Basically anything you want. Let's be honest here, if you make up a 'sorcerer's fraternity' or something like that, it would only make my job easier, because you're doing the world-building job for me.<br /> <br /> (3) Transcendent Mastery of the Arts is rather over-powered. It gives you 88 exp worth of things for 8 exp. What I could allow:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Transcendent Mastery of the Arts</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: --; <b>Mins</b>: Occult 5, Essence 2; <b>Type</b>: Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Mirror<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: One Occult Excellency<br /> Mortal thaumaturges must wrestle with the innate energies of Creation to shape reality according to their will, learning to do so a little at a time. Solar occultists manipulate Essence at a whim--such energies are theirs to command. With study and observation of the arcane principles embedded in the very fabric of the world, a champion of the Sun's insight far surpasses the life's work of a mortal mind with consummate ease. Upon learning this Charm, the Solar reduces the experience cost of Thaumaturgy by half. This effect is retroactive, refunding appropriate experience (and only experience) spent on Thaumaturgy before learning this charm.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> (4) Also seems a bit unthematic for a Solar, so here's how I would write it<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Demon Binding Magnificence</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: - (+5m per First Circle, +10m per second circle); <b>Mins</b>: Occult 5, Essence 3; <b>Type</b>: Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Varies<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: Spirit-Cutting Attack, Appropriate Sorcery Initiation<br /> After the defeat of the Primordials, the Unconquered Sun in his wisdom allowed his chosen to summon their defeated forms in the management of creation. Many of the Chosen used these Demons to great effect.<br /> This charm can be taken three times, once after each time he has learned a new circle of sorcery. It must be purchased after each initiation for it's effects to enhance Demon summoning at that level. This charm increases the Solar\u2019s ability to summon Demons in the following ways.<br /> -This charm increases the dice pool of the Solar for the summoning contest by 2 per time the charm has been purchased.<br /> -The Solar may summon multiple demons (to a maximum of Essence total demons) with a single summoning spell. For Demon of the First Circle, all summoned Demons must be of the same species. For Demon of the Second Circle, all additional demons must be first circle demons descended from the Summoned second circle. For Demon of the Third Circle, all additional demons must be subsidiary souls of the summoned Third Circle. In all cases, each additional demon adds their essence rating to the Demons' rolls to resist the bindings; if the demons win the contest, they are all freed. The conditions of the binding are applied to all demons equally; if task-bound, all summoned demons are bound to the same task.<br /> Since this charm is predicated on use of the Surrender Oaths, it only works on summoned demons and has no bearing on Elementals or Daevas.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","user":"Noodle","date":". 05-14-2014, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T17:19:04-07:00","id":137404,"title":"","content":"Noodle: You need to be clearer on the multi demon summoning. Does it let you summon one more? As many as you want? Does doing so make it harder? This has the potential to get VERY broken by letting you conjure up armies in a month or the like. Also, the sorcery spells themselves are predicated on the surrender oaths, thats why Thaumaturgy doesn't let you bind demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T17:43:19-07:00","id":137418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=137404#post137404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Noodle: You need to be clearer on the multi demon summoning. Does it let you summon one more? As many as you want?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. I forgot to add the limit. It's (essence) demons with one Summoning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=137404#post137404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does doing so make it harder? This has the potential to get VERY broken by letting you conjure up armies in a month or the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes it harder to bind them, adding some practical limitations to the rate of summoning. Though I suppose a per-demon mote cost addition to the spell might not be remiss. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=137404#post137404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the sorcery spells themselves are predicated on the surrender oaths, thats why Thaumaturgy doesn't let you bind demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am aware; the purpose of that statement is to give a IC reason for it not working on Summon Elemental and the hypothetical Daeva Summoning spells postulated in Shards. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T18:34:47-07:00","id":137465,"title":"","content":"Two questions: Can someone point me to the sorcery background? I don't recall it and it seems really nice since 3xp is less then 8 for spells.<br /> <br /> Also, can I get a general description of what the various fey's equipment is? I gather that the noble can alter the form of his weapon, but are they heavily armored? Asking for stunt reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T07:37:13-07:00","id":138043,"title":"","content":"Sorcery x: No spells known \u2022: 1 terrestrial spell \u2022\u2022: 2 terrestrial spells \u2022\u2022\u2022: 3 terrestrial spells \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022: 5 terrestrial or celestial spells \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022: 7 terrestrial or celestial spells","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T08:14:54-07:00","id":138066,"title":"","content":"Hyuga: That action you did IC was a flurry and you didn't include penalties. Since you took 3 actions they would be at -3, -4, and -5 in order. I am going to guess they are in the order listed.<br /> <br /> Your Attack is Dex 2 + Melee 3 + Accuracy 3 + Stunt 2 and is DV -1<br /> Your Feat of Strength is Strength 4 + Athletics 2 is DV -1 plus subtract 2 dice due to being distracted by doing it in combat (Its also speed five which sets the speed for everything else)<br /> You Palm thrust is a martial arts attack Dex 2 + MA 2 - Offhand 1 and is DV -1<br /> <br /> So:<br /> <br /> 1. 3 successes<br /> 2. 0 dice due to combat and multiple action penalties<br /> 3. 0 dice due to multiple action penalties<br /> <br /> Also, your DV is 4, Protection of Celestial Bliss means your own attacks don't penalize DV but the Feat of Strength wasn't an attack.<br /> <br /> Note: All this is assuming that you activated PoCB before combat, because that would also be an action in the flurry and impose a higher penalty.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T08:43:51-07:00","id":138094,"title":"","content":"Ah.. I wasn't thinking and put my stunt dice into the original pool for feat and the palm strike. I knew it would be speed five because of my palm attack (punch) anyway. I already had pocb activated when I ran to the scene. I did forget to take one dice off of the palm strike though... Wasn't thinking about the feat as part of a flurry even though it is. And I need to separate my stunt dice out of the last two. My first action should be at full dice though and each one after with a penalty one higher than the last right? Why are you starting with -3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T08:55:25-07:00","id":138100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CitanHyuga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=138094#post138094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first action should be at full dice though and each one after with a penalty one higher than the last right? Why are you starting with -3?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, we were doing it wrong, back then. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted 2e Core, p124-125</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whatever the situation, characters who take multiple actions suffer a special form of internal penalty. The first action loses dice equal to the number of actions attempted, with each successive action cumulatively increasing the penalty by one die. Therefore, a character taking three actions would be at -3 dice to the first action, -4 to the second and -5 to the third. <br /> In combat, multiple actions are extremely common and known as flurries.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T09:05:16-07:00","id":138109,"title":"","content":"For why it started at -3 and worked its way down:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Core p. 124-125</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The first action loses dice equal to the number of actions attempted, with each successive action cumulatively increasing the penalty by one die. Therefore, a character taking three actions would be at -3 dice to the first action, -4 to the second and -5 to the third.</div> </div> </div> </div>For why the stunts don't matter for the other two actions:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Core p. 121</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a character ever has a dice pool of zero dice or less after applying all bonuses and does not benefit from bonus successes, she cannot even attempt that action.</div> </div> </div> </div>The penalties reduce your base pool to zero so you cannot attempt it and so cannot add stunts on top of actions you cannot take.<br /> <br /> Edit: But you could channel a point of WP for an auto success or to channel a virtue, that would raise your pools into the positive. (Though I don't know if you can edit it in after the fact)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T09:19:15-07:00","id":138129,"title":"","content":"Argh.. I was using the same rules we used back then... Is it alright if I change it to be just the first melee attack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T09:20:03-07:00","id":138131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CitanHyuga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=138129#post138129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Argh.. I was using the same rules we used back then... Is it alright if I change it to be just the first melee attack?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T09:23:42-07:00","id":138143,"title":"","content":"My iPad won't let me change the text right now. Can you just pretend that the other parts don't exist right now? If it hits, it would still be sux+ 9/2L","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T13:14:02-07:00","id":138359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=137465#post137465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two questions: Can someone point me to the sorcery background? I don't recall it and it seems really nice since 3xp is less then 8 for spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two things:<br /> <br /> One, The Sorcery Background is above, as Hyuga wrote. It was a 1E background, and never translated up to 2E, though my groups always tended to allow it. <br /> <br /> Two: I don't charge EXP for backgrounds, as I require them to be raised through play and roleplay. So you could raise your Sorcery Background, but it would require digging around in ancient ruins for occult lore, messing around with gods and demons and elementals and ghosts, and/or attending an academy for extended periods of time, IC.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=137465#post137465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, can I get a general description of what the various fey's equipment is? I gather that the noble can alter the form of his weapon, but are they heavily armored? Asking for stunt reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shu-Yin is bedecked in a ridiculous ensemble, consisting of baggy pants, something that hovers in the territory between suspenders and a vest, with unattached pauldrons and sleeves. This ensemble is heavily belted to his body, and none of it appears particularly armored per se. He has no apparent weapons, aside from his daiklaive. <br /> <br /> The other Raksha are unclothed, though they bear somewhat barbaric looking jewelry (which knowing the Fae could very well be armor). They have no obvious weapons, save the beasts they ride. And... *rolling Perception+Awareness* the beasts have hilts sticking from their backs. If they had endoskelletons, I would say those hilts would be in the middle of their shoulder-blades. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T14:26:34-07:00","id":138398,"title":"","content":"Would it be possible for Vykos to have the backing of one of the Gens ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T14:38:47-07:00","id":138406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=138398#post138398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be possible for Vykos to have the backing of one of the Gens ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Um. If he's a native, then it would be possible, yes. Otherwise, He could get backing from Nikoloi if he went to Novalesk's academy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T15:35:32-07:00","id":138487,"title":"","content":"How much did he beat my DV by? Was I reduced to minimum damage? Is the 12L pre or post soak? How on earth did I deflect the blade from Hyuga? I most certainly wasn't using Defend Other on him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 05-15-2014, 06:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T15:46:09-07:00","id":138497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=138487#post138487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much did he beat my DV by?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some. Not a lot, but by a relatively small margin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=138487#post138487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was I reduced to minimum damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=138487#post138487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the 12L pre or post soak?</div> </div> </div> </div>12L base damage; therefore Pre-soak. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=138487#post138487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How on earth did I deflect the blade from Hyuga? I most certainly wasn't using Defend Other on him.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was more of a narrative convenience, due to him rolling shitty after doing a single swing, multi-target flurry. The idea is that he took a single wide swing at both of you, but your attempts to defend yourself also had the effect of knocking the attack of kilter, making it easier for Hyuga to defend himself. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T15:56:19-07:00","id":138525,"title":"","content":"Last question, in the interests of hurting the fey: Did Hyuga get to take advantage of an onslaught penalty? Would that help at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T16:04:01-07:00","id":138531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=138525#post138525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last question, in the interests of hurting the fey: Did Hyuga get to take advantage of an onslaught penalty? Would that help at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're referring to Hyuga's missed attack? Yes, he did take advantage of an onslaught penalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T17:31:31-07:00","id":138665,"title":"","content":"<b>-Rumor Mill-</b><br /> <br /> <b>Ordon #2</b><br /> <br /> -Ordon is built on a burial ground dating back to the first war between the gods and demons.<br /> <br /> -The Ordoni wage an eternal war with an infinite army of underground demons.<br /> <br /> -Ordoni prophets replace their eyes with metallic orbs to receive visions from their god.<br /> <br /> - The Ordoni worship focuses on trio of divinities, known as the Architect, the Maker, and the Engineer.<br /> <br /> Previous Ordon rumors<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Unconfirmed (at least one true)<br /> -Ordon's leadership caste is comprised of a group of quasi-divine Jade statues. These beings lead the Ordoni in the worship of a mechanical god run by smoke and clockwork.<br /> -Ordon sits upon a portal to an alien world of darkness and metal. A Realm of Brass and Shadows, if you will.<br /> -Ordon is a Lookshan puppet-state.<br /> -All residents of Ordon have their brain removed and replaced with a machine when they reach adulthood.<br /> -Ordoni are not born, they're grown.<br /> -The Ordon have dug too greedily and too deep. In so doing, they've released something dark and evil.<br /> -Ordon is built atop a military facility constructed as a fallout bunker by a paranoid Anathema god-king in the Age of Glories.<br /> -The Ordon build clockwork men and use them as warriors.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T18:17:30-07:00","id":138686,"title":"","content":"I would like to solicit the opinion of the thread: Should I try to stunt my defense and thereby risk not stopping the Fey attack or blow out my PoCB?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T18:33:33-07:00","id":138699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=138665#post138665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-The Ordoni wage an eternal war with an infinite army of underground demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will place my money on this option for this round of rumors.<br /> <br /> @Exthalion: I say stunt the sucker, that way you have PoCB ready should you need it later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T13:32:06-07:00","id":139729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=137323#post137323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (3) Transcendent Mastery of the Arts is rather over-powered. It gives you 88 exp worth of things for 8 exp. What I could allow:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Transcendent Mastery of the Arts</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: --; <b>Mins</b>: Occult 5, Essence 2; <b>Type</b>: Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Mirror<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: One Occult Excellency<br /> Mortal thaumaturges must wrestle with the innate energies of Creation to shape reality according to their will, learning to do so a little at a time. Solar occultists manipulate Essence at a whim--such energies are theirs to command. With study and observation of the arcane principles embedded in the very fabric of the world, a champion of the Sun's insight far surpasses the life's work of a mortal mind with consummate ease. Upon learning this Charm, the Solar reduces the experience cost of Thaumaturgy by half. This effect is retroactive, refunding appropriate experience (and only experience) spent on Thaumaturgy before learning this charm.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think It's overpowered after all thaumarturgical Rituals are cheap parlor trick (useful but still cheap) when you compare them to sorcery spells. I don't think it's fair that you have to pay the same price in Exp for thaumaturgy than you would for a terretrial sorcery spell that is easily a 100 time more powerful than any master degree procedure and not to mention celestial or solar circle spell beside it's a solar charm is it not supposed to be overpowered <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (I really like to use these little guys).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T13:37:37-07:00","id":139735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=139729#post139729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think It's overpowered after all thaumarturgical Rituals are cheap parlor trick (useful but still cheap) when you compare them to sorcery spells. I don't think it's fair that you have to pay the same price in Exp for thaumaturgy than you would for a terretrial sorcery spell that is easily a 100 time more powerful than any master degree procedure and not to mention celestial or solar circle spell beside it's a solar charm is it not supposed to be overpowered <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (I really like to use these little guys).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, each individual procedure is weak, but they're are a TON of them, and when put together they become an incredibly useful tool. If I allowed the charm as you wrote, that Solar would literally have a magic 'tool' that would help them in any conceivable circumstance. No dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T14:21:29-07:00","id":139794,"title":"","content":"Well I won't argue that there is a ton of them that is true still it is quite expensive XP wise for the number of different art but you're the ST what you say goes and I'm grateful for your take on the charm and the fact that you allow it but would it be possible for it to be taken more than once or for a form of upgrade after all thaumaturgy is quite useful for a sorcerer.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh and I forgot to ask which version of the anima banner do we use for the twilight personally I think both are lame but that is just me we had or own version in the IRL game but I don't want to push the button too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 05-16-2014, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T15:23:06-07:00","id":139867,"title":"","content":"Art of Warding + Occult Excellency = kill anything that doesn't have countermagic.<br /> <br /> How about the charm grants two or three free degrees and makes all future purchases half price? (Which would still put it on the &quot;Must Buy&quot; list)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T15:49:38-07:00","id":139901,"title":"","content":"Kill anything ? I don't think so but you are half right many things won't be able to cross some of the ward but it won't keep a noble raksha out or a second circle demon. Since Noodle is right about the fact that thaumaturgy is useful and it should not be free or close to, their could be 11 variation of the charm that could give you a master degree in the chosen art then again it remain quite a powerful charm but I think it fits the solar theme, you would still be required to buy the charm 11 time to have all the art of thaumaturgy which is still expensive and long to get (Now I realise my IRL ST was quite laid back with the rules)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T16:10:50-07:00","id":139934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=139794#post139794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Oh and I forgot to ask which version of the anima banner do we use for the twilight personally I think both are lame but that is just me we had or own version in the IRL game but I don't want to push the button too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're using any and all official Errata, including the Twilight anima. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T16:18:42-07:00","id":139938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=139867#post139867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Art of Warding + Occult Excellency = kill anything that doesn't have countermagic.<br /> <br /> How about the charm grants two or three free degrees and makes all future purchases half price? (Which would still put it on the &quot;Must Buy&quot; list)</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I think that it's a solid charm as is. In my mind this charm operates under a similar principle to Swallowing the Lotus Root, in that the semi-divine perspective makes learning lesser magical arts easier. <br /> <br /> If you're char concept focuses on thaumaturgy, its a must buy anyway, as you break even after only two Degrees. Anything further is severely discounted. I stand by my decision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T16:22:21-07:00","id":139940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=139901#post139901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kill anything ? I don't think so but you are half right many things won't be able to cross some of the ward but it won't keep a noble raksha out or a second circle demon. Since Noodle is right about the fact that thaumaturgy is useful and it should not be free or close to, their could be 11 variation of the charm that could give you a master degree in the chosen art then again it remain quite a powerful charm but I think it fits the solar theme, you would still be required to buy the charm 11 time to have all the art of thaumaturgy which is still expensive and long to get (Now I realise my IRL ST was quite laid back with the rules)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that charms to instantly master anything, especially discrete chunks of an entire subsystem, are in anyone's charmspace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","user":"Noodle","date":". 05-16-2014, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T18:39:22-07:00","id":140131,"title":"","content":"Like I said your the ST what you say goes, we were just throwing ideas around, though if I annoyed the crap out of you I apologize it was not my intention. I'm trying to make Vykos work but I must admit hat I am failing miserably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T18:49:08-07:00","id":140135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=140131#post140131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said your the ST what you say goes, we were just throwing ideas around, though if I annoyed the crap out of you I apologize it was not my intention. I'm trying to make Vykos work but I must admit hat I am failing miserably.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just trying to make sure I address your points. I have no hard feelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T19:06:35-07:00","id":140146,"title":"","content":"Well thank you for that but I can't seem to get Vykos working so I'm gonna change characters I'll post the new guy tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T15:32:08-07:00","id":141885,"title":"","content":"Alright so here's Vykos rebuilt from the ground up and brand new I just miss the background story(can't seem to get any inspiration for it)<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Vykos Antalek (Twilight Caste Solar Exalted)<br /> Anima Banner: A summoning cirlce appears on the ground underneat him as DNA strands emerge from it and start to turn in an helix pattern around him.<br /> Motivation: Create a second more evolved form of Humans and have them replace the first.<br /> Limit Break: Deliberate Cruelty<br /> <br /> Parry DV: 1<br /> Dodge DV: 5<br /> Mental DV: 6<br /> <br /> Strenght: 2<br /> Dexterity: 3<br /> Stamina: 2<br /> <br /> Charisma: 3<br /> Manipulation: 2<br /> Appearance: 4<br /> <br /> Perception: 3<br /> Intelligence: 5<br /> Wits: 3<br /> <br /> Caste Abilities<br /> Craft: 3 Genesis<br /> Investigation: 4<br /> Medicine: 4<br /> Lore: 4<br /> Occult: 5<br /> <br /> Favored Abilities<br /> Dodge: 2<br /> Integrity: 2<br /> Linguistic: 2<br /> Melee: 1<br /> Presence: 1<br /> <br /> Specialty<br /> - Lore Biology +2<br /> - Occult Demonology + 2<br /> -<br /> <br /> Language<br /> - Riverspeak (native)<br /> - Low Realm<br /> - Old Realm<br /> <br /> Charms<br /> - First Craft Excellncy<br /> - First Medicine Excellency<br /> - First Occult Excellency<br /> - First Investigation Excellency<br /> - First Lore Excellency<br /> - Crafty Observation Method<br /> - Terrestrial Circle Sorcery<br /> - Transcendant Mastery of the Arts<br /> - Spirit Detecting Glance<br /> - Integrity Protecting Prana<br /> <br /> Spells<br /> - Emerald Countermagic<br /> - Emerald Cirlce Banishment<br /> - Summon Demon of the first circle<br /> - Summon Elemental<br /> - Death of Obsidian Butterflies<br /> <br /> Backgrounds<br /> - Sorcery 4 (2)<br /> - Backing 3 (House Nikoloi)<br /> - Manse 1 (Wood Aspect) (A small house manse from the sogunate era) (Dragon Willow agate heartstone)<br /> -<br /> -<br /> <br /> Willpower: 7 (2)<br /> Valor: 2<br /> Conviction: 3<br /> Compassion: 2<br /> Temperance: 2<br /> <br /> Essence: 4 (14)<br /> Personnal: 19<br /> Peripheral: 44<br /> <br /> Weapons<br /> <br /> Armor<br /> <br /> Merits and Flaws<br /> <br /> Physical Description<br /> A young man of slender built Vykos is well dressed in dark blue robes his silver hair help enhance his smooth facial features and his bright blue eyes.<br /> <br /> Background story<br /> A resident of Novalesk Vykos was the son of a gifted surgeon in the employ of House Nikoloi after his father's death he entered in the service of house Nikoloi as an occultist and healer after seeing the menace of the fairfolk in the region Vykos began to study the Wyld and secretly initiated himself in the first circle of sorcery and the studies of Bio- Essence thanks to some of the ancient relic of the dragon kings,with this knowledge he wants to conduct experiment into augmenting the human body to better resist wyld energies but the lack of suitable tools and equipment as stopped him for now.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 07-16-2014, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T16:22:31-07:00","id":141898,"title":"","content":"What is this DNA and Evolution you speak of? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (I am fairly certain the concepts, if they exist at all, are fairly esoteric genesis science discussed only in rare First Age caches or known to very obscure spirits.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 05-18-2014, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","