conquering the surrounding Nations as part of an elaborate plot to encircle Nasaru and Gunzota Redoubts.<br /> -King Urlik of Theros has been possessed by the baleful spirit of his black blade.<br /> - An Anathema cult, known as the 'Black Cowl', secretly controls Theros' aristocracy.<br /> - An Anathema cult, known as the 'Gilded Triangle', secretly controls Theros' aristocracy.<br /> - An Anathema cult, known as the 'Haired Beast', secretly controls Theros' aristocracy. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T20:57:20-07:00","id":143005,"title":"","content":"<b>-Rumor Mill- </b>Glory and Honor to Novalesk!<br /> <br /> -Gens Althea has a necromantic assassin, an unkillable warrior who glows with the unholy pyre-flame of the Underworld.<br /> <br /> -One of Ptreas Nikon's sons has sired a flaxen-haired termagant; a cocksure warrior who slay a yeddim with one strike.<br /> <br /> -On Ramshackle Street, one can find a pub run by a quartet of bestial Fae. Any dish in Creation can be found there, except curry dishes.<br /> <br /> -Althea Sanna is the illegitimate daughter of a Therian noble.<br /> <br /> Previous Novalesk Rumors<br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Unconfirmed: At least one true<br /> -Gens Spyrus secretly worships an entity known as the &quot;Chariot of Embers&quot;.<br /> -Gens Midea has a covert group of shape-shifting assassins all descended from the &quot;True Midea Bloodline&quot;.<br /> -Chancellor Feiro occasionally sacrifices troublesome students to a giant crystalline fire-ball.<br /> -The Guild secretly controls Gens Nikoloi.<br /> <br /> At least one true<br /> -In the north of Novalesk, there are ancient monoliths in the shape of The Sorcerer. On moonless nights, demons can be summoned there without sorcery or thaumaturgy.<br /> -Strategos Eugene has a crippling Bright Morning addiction.<br /> -On Ramshackle Street in Novalesk city, take three lefts. There you will find a man who knows where all things lost are. But, you must pay him three and a half yen, a brass tack, and the skin of a 9-year cicada for him to reveal one of his secrets.<br /> -A ghastly horseman travels the hills of Novalesk, reaping the souls of the treacherous.<br /> <br /> Confirmed false<br /> -Origenon Larissa has an Anathema lover.<br /> -Origenes is actually an Anathema.</div></div> </div> </div></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","user":"Noodle","date":". 05-20-2014, 12:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T21:05:05-07:00","id":143009,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the lack of rumor mills lately, I had a hectic weekend. Above are two of them that I owed you.<br /> <br /> Also, I find myself not being as inspired for rumors as much as I thought. SO! I will intersperse the Rumor mill with 'Solid Facts' about varying surrounding locales, peoples, things, places, etc. If you want to request upcoming Solid Facts things be it about a specific thing like 'The barbarian tribes that live on the plains between Novalesk and Geherin' or something vague, like 'Tell me about the nearest major Shadowland'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T21:35:49-07:00","id":143038,"title":"","content":"<b>Gens Origenon</b><br /> While the Cadet family system allows a Gens to foster extended groups of immigrants and refugees, individuals and households are brought in as part of Gens Origenon. Origenon lacks any centralized hierarchy or organization, though it's members gain Native and Citizen status like their cousins in the Gentes or Cadet houses. Over time, members of Gens Origenon usually clump together to form cadet families, or get themselves adopted as members of the Gentes (usually through marriage). <br /> <br /> Most members of Origenon are clustered in the capital, though they can be found anywhere throughout the nation. Despite being the nominal 'Seventh Gens', Orgienon lacks representation in the Boule. This fails to truly impact the 'Gens' as a whole, as those members that are offended by this typically marry into one of the Six Great Gentes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T22:03:24-07:00","id":143057,"title":"","content":"Wait... does this mean Origenes is going to be my father in law even if I don't marry Larissa?<br /> <br /> Also, was this inspired by my need to be adopted or was it there from the beginning? Not trying to sound like need special things put in, but it is very convenient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T22:08:01-07:00","id":143071,"title":"","content":"<b>Ramshackle Street</b><br /> The legends of Ramshackle Street stretch all throughout Creation. It is said to be mystical boulevard that defies space and time, wherein one might find anything they desire. Exotic beings buy and sell and trade wonders forged in the Age of Glories, the First Age, or even the time before Creation, beneath a star-spackled sky. <br /> <br /> This is not the Ramshackle Street of which I speak.<br /> <br /> No, the street in Novalesk that has gained fame as 'Ramshackle Street' is merely a street in the poorer section of the city (Novalesk is much too small to have 'slums'). This Ramshackle steet is home to dozens of tiny Bazaars, each one a pale imitation of a shadow of the mythical boulevard. Though, rumors suggest that this Ramshackle Street is one of the locations where a traveller, if they lose their way, may find themselves upon the starry avenue. But those are just rumors, aren't they?<br /> <br /> Many a child in Creation knows of the rhyme of Ramshackle Street:<br /> <br /> Ramshackle Street, Ramshackle Street,<br /> Where you'll find items that are rather neat.<br /> Where are you going? You should watch your feet.<br /> You'll get lost forever on Ramshackle Street. <br /> Caught in the wonders of Ramshackle Street.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T22:09:36-07:00","id":143073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=143057#post143057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait... does this mean Origenes is going to be my father in law even if I don't marry Larissa?<br /> <br /> Also, was this inspired by my need to be adopted or was it there from the beginning? Not trying to sound like need special things put in, but it is very convenient.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was an idea from the get-go, I just kept forgetting to post it.<br /> <br /> Oh, and if you join Origenon, Origenes will be your family Deity, not your Father-in-law. Unless you also marry Larissa, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T07:14:33-07:00","id":143406,"title":"","content":"Cool I'll wait till you introduce me then","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T10:05:40-07:00","id":143633,"title":"","content":"Exthalion, I'm imagining Yi being played by Sean Bean now. Either that or a younger Tim Curry. He's just GNAWING on that scenery. I love it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T10:41:01-07:00","id":143694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=143633#post143633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exthalion, I'm imagining Yi being played by Sean Bean now. Either that or a younger Tim Curry. He's just GNAWING on that scenery. I love it.</div> </div> </div> </div>My fault for playing Red Alert 3 and watching the Color of Magic in the same week I guess.<br /> <br /> Edit: Anything in particular stand out? Also, is it the good kind or the bad kind? (I wasn't doing it on purpose so I am unsure)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 05-20-2014, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T11:12:35-07:00","id":143722,"title":"","content":"The &quot;Show me a Hero, and I will write you a Tragedy&quot; line stands out to me, although the whole exchange that Yi and Shu-Yin has is pretty memorable. If I'm reading Noodle right, Shu-Yin is a riff on JRPG heroes, particularly of the Modern Final Fantasies, so that Yi was able to out-Ham a King of Camp like that is pretty notable.<br /> <br /> I'm of the opinion that, due to being derived from larger than life myths, Exalts ought to thrive on such theatrics, so I am quite enjoying it. I hope that answers your question(s).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T11:20:33-07:00","id":143729,"title":"","content":"It does, thank you.<br /> <br /> Hm... you wouldn't happen to have the Grace Forging Charms would you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T11:39:24-07:00","id":143740,"title":"","content":"Sadly, Tirien has no crafting charms, her primary focuses being on raw charisma, oratory and proficiency in Beastman-Fu. Although, her contacts with Estrayan's court could probably hook ye up with some graces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T11:43:10-07:00","id":143741,"title":"","content":"Yes, the next time we fight fey we must do it the proper way: Dance Fighting!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T13:35:52-07:00","id":143824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=143000#post143000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Theros is preparing for an invasion of Novalesk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is my bet for the true one in this batch. It seems to me that any Realm Satrapy would be looking to do just such a thing to help mitigate the crushing taxes the Realm asks of them as well as gain favor in the eyes of their masters. Just my thoughts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=143005#post143005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Althea Sanna is the illegitimate daughter of a Therian noble.</div> </div> </div> </div>This one is also a safe bet. Notice that I am not going for anything that is way out there. I'm trying to go with the simplest explanation route.<br /> <br /> As far as to what I would like to hear about, I would like to hear about the Shadowland, definitely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":1146,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","user":"Belkra","date":".  Adding additional quote, etc. 05-20-2014, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T17:53:15-07:00","id":143981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=143722#post143722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;Show me a Hero, and I will write you a Tragedy&quot; line stands out to me, although the whole exchange that Yi and Shu-Yin has is pretty memorable. If I'm reading Noodle right, Shu-Yin is a riff on JRPG heroes, particularly of the Modern Final Fantasies, so that Yi was able to out-Ham a King of Camp like that is pretty notable.<br /> <br /> I'm of the opinion that, due to being derived from larger than life myths, Exalts ought to thrive on such theatrics, so I am quite enjoying it. I hope that answers your question(s).</div> </div> </div> </div>You would be correct. More specifically, he's an exaggerated take on Cloud Strife, Squall Leonhart, and Tidus. Wait till you see the rest of his party!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=143741#post143741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, the next time we fight fey we must do it the proper way: Dance Fighting!</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Can you chew enough scenery, King of Ham?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T18:19:59-07:00","id":144001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=143981#post143981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You would be correct. More specifically, he's an exaggerated take on Cloud Strife, Squall Leonhart, and Tidus. Wait till you see the rest of his party!<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> Can you chew enough scenery, King of Ham?</div> </div> </div> </div>Noavelsk can wait, we have a new quest: We journey into the Wyld to find the King of ham and then I slaughter in in so gory a way that the genre changes!<br /> <br /> (I was actually aiming for Baltheir with his Leading Man bit)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T22:18:27-07:00","id":144174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=143824#post143824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as to what I would like to hear about, I would like to hear about the Shadowland, definitely.</div> </div> </div> </div>As per your request:<br /> <br /> <b>-The Forests of Bone and the Ash-Mount Hill-</b><br /> <br /> Forming the majority of Theros' Western border, the Forests of Bone consists of an ovoid shadowland, nearly two-hundred square kilometers in area. It's territory is covered mostly by the eponymous bone-like evergreens. From whence this shadowland came, none know; or in the very least, none who know speak.<br /> <br /> The Forests of Bone was long &quot;ruled&quot; by a &quot;Council&quot; of assasinated Therian monarchs, who were bent on revenge on their treacherous kin. The truth of the matter is, though, that those shades were too divisive and egotistical to do much and no one ghost lasted for long. The Minister of the Chambers, however, has existed in his position longer than any can remember, and the Dead have long memories. <br /> <br /> Recently however, a coup has taken place. The Minister revealed himself to be a powerful necromancer, and, with the assistance of a being called &quot;The Bloodied Monarch Raised Upon The Bones Of Trees&quot;. Together the Minister and the Monarch took complete control over the Forest's loose government, and now run it like a totalitarian Dictatorship. Fun times. <br /> <br /> The new government's first action was to declare war upon the closest major shadowland, the Ash-Mount Hill. This shadowland which lies to the south-east of the Forest, is a near-perfect circle a mere mile in radius. It has no permanent residents. A powerful spectre, bedecked in ancient, ornate armor, wielding mismatched Underworld Jade Swords and shrouded in a cloak of white feathers, claims it has his own territory, however, and does not tolerate trespassers. The Monarch attempted to oust this spectre shortly after conquering the Forests. The attempt failed horribly. <br /> <br /> <i>Okay. Requests, requests. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T07:59:13-07:00","id":144474,"title":"","content":"I want to hear more about Ramshackle Street.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T08:30:50-07:00","id":144494,"title":"","content":"Would that be Novalesk Ramshackle Street, or Legendary parallel-dimension-type-thing Ramshackle street?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T08:47:21-07:00","id":144512,"title":"","content":"A little of both would be great. Also, how does one actually enter the legendary street, per chance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T08:58:55-07:00","id":144516,"title":"","content":"How about a survey of local opinions of different groups. I assume they do not like Fey, but are there negative opinions on Solar/Lunar anathema? What about toward ancestor ghosts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 05-21-2014, 12:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T14:15:39-07:00","id":144846,"title":"","content":"I'm really wondering where you are all getting the conclusion that this newcomer is a DB. I haven't said anything about her that would directly indicate that, I think. I mean, I specifically didn't use the term 'red-headed' to describe her, because I wanted to communicate that she had what is considered &quot;red&quot; hair IRL, as opposed to the literal red fair that is possible in in creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T14:40:15-07:00","id":144868,"title":"","content":"Well you did say that she's wearing a jade breastplate so... do you want me to modify my post ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T14:57:32-07:00","id":144910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=144868#post144868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well you did say that she's wearing a jade breastplate so... do you want me to modify my post ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this is Novalesk. Essence users are not uncommon, and many of them have artifacts (note I'm not saying a majority, just that significant number of them do). While a majority of the artifacts in Novalesk aren't constructed from the Prime Magical Materials, the most common magical material you'll see anywhere is jade. With Novalesk's relatively small terrestrial population (I seem to recall saying at one point that there are around a half-dozen terrestrials in the entire nation) you have long odds against you if you bet anyone that walks around in Jade is a DB.<br /> <br /> Heck, Eugene showed up wearing a Jade Lamellar, and he's not Exalted at all. <br /> <br /> That said, she IS a DB (Fire Aspect, if you care to know), and Vykos of anyone would have seen this first-hand due to his fighting beside her briefly, but still. It's a matter of principle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T15:02:01-07:00","id":144916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=144868#post144868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well you did say that she's wearing a jade breastplate so... do you want me to modify my post ?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is why I asked if I should be running.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T15:07:16-07:00","id":144918,"title":"","content":"Profile for Hyuga's new behemoth.<br /> <br /> When used as a Melee weapon, the behemoth has the following stats:<br /> Speed 5, Accuracy +3, Damage +3L, Defense +2, Rate 2, Tags 2, R, Th, Attune 3<br /> <br /> When released as a beast, it uses the handler's stats, with the following modifications:<br /> +2 to all soaks<br /> Gains sword profile as N-tag attack<br /> Gains the following Thrown attack:<br /> Speed 5, Accuracy +2, Damage +2L, Defense -, Rate 2, Tags -","signature":"","edited":{"userid":155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","user":"Noodle","date":". 05-21-2014, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T15:27:25-07:00","id":144934,"title":"","content":"Just to make sure, but it would cost me 6m to attune to it since it is not made from ori correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T15:29:52-07:00","id":144936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CitanHyuga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=144934#post144934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to make sure, but it would cost me 6m to attune to it since it is not made from ori correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. That only applies if it has a MM bonus that you want other then your own. So you could attune a soulsteel daiklaive for exactly as much as an ori one, its just that you wouldn't get the mote drain and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T15:31:13-07:00","id":144938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=144516#post144516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about a survey of local opinions of different groups. I assume they do not like Fey, but are there negative opinions on Solar/Lunar anathema? What about toward ancestor ghosts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>suppose </i>this would be an important thing to know.<br /> <br /> <b>-Local Opinions on Various Supernatural Entities-</b><br /> <br /> Theros is a strongly Immaculate nation, and behaves as such. Anathema are openly hunted, Fae slain, and ghosts exorcised. Small cults to various individuals spring up form time to time, though they are often quashed violently by local authorities. One notable example, the Gilded Triangle, has managed to survive for several generations despite constant attempts at eradication. <br /> <br /> The Geherin strongly support Lunars. Because their patron goddess is supposedly a child of the moon, they view the Stewards with a certain degree of filial respect, almost as if they were beloved Aunts and Uncles. Their relationship with other Exalted is resolved on a case-by-case basis, though they tend to view them as proven Champions. This means that they will be accorded some form of respect, provided the Exalt doesn't expect the Geherin to be subservient to them. Ghosts are tolerated, so long as they are the shades of noble warriors, though the Geherin's lack of shadowlands makes any form of reliable contact between the living and the dead problematic. <br /> <br /> No-one other than the Ordoni know the Ordoni's relationship with the dead, Fae, or Anathema. They seem content to keep it that way. <br /> <br /> Novalesk has mixed views of the Anathema. On the one hand, there have purportedly been a number of Anathema in Novalesk's history, such as the Myrinne and Midea. On the other, Novalesk has dealt with a number of hostile Anathema in the past. As a whole, Anathema in Novlaesk are kept at arm's length unless they are members of one of the Gentes. Regardless, they are encouraged to not be very open about their powers, in order to keep their Immaculate neighbors at bay. The law, as decreed by Origenes at the founding of the nation, was that neither the Dead nor Divine may hold direct temporal power. The Anathema, with their powers stemming from the Celestines, are generally considered to fall under the purview of the latter. <br /> <br /> The Dead are treated with dignity and respect in Novalesk, though they are generally expected to just move along with their &quot;lives&quot; and pass into Lethe. Some exceptions exist, especially if they were respected individuals in life; the current Pyrtaneis, for example, was the Archon prior to Larissa's election.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T15:33:33-07:00","id":144962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=144936#post144936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope. That only applies if it has a MM bonus that you want other then your own. So you could attune a soulsteel daiklaive for exactly as much as an ori one, its just that you wouldn't get the mote drain and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is correct. As it has no MM, you don't have to force resonance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T17:37:47-07:00","id":145039,"title":"","content":"Alright I wasn't sure if it was MM or not. I had to attune to it in the first place. Glad to know though thanks. Also, I forgot to ask earlier, but if it has my stats, does that mean it has increased health like me through my ox-body charm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T17:47:11-07:00","id":145069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CitanHyuga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=145039#post145039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright I wasn't sure if it was MM or not. I had to attune to it in the first place. Glad to know though thanks. Also, I forgot to ask earlier, but if it has my stats, does that mean it has increased health like me through my ox-body charm?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true facts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T18:13:38-07:00","id":145087,"title":"","content":"Okay, there is a topic for discussion I would like to present to everybody. The forum has some issues, like eating posts or the reply box showing up, but those are little annoyances that are easy enough to live with. However, it isn\u2019t really set up for forum games. Threads get unwieldy and information is sort of scattered around.<br /> <br /> There is a site I have played a little on that is better designed I think. It\u2019s called RPdom, and I think moving this game there would be a good idea. Things like character sheets and rumors could have their own subforums so they are easy to find, and when we split the party like now we could have our own threads in the same game forum.<br /> <br /> Just a thought I had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T21:41:00-07:00","id":145272,"title":"","content":"If people want to switch to that forum, it is fine with me. I don't mind staying on this one either. <br /> <br /> Noodle: Please let me know how long it will take per roll to re-build and how many mortal aides, or assistants I will have. I am counting Jensven as a celestial exalted aide of course. Also, do you want me to just do one roll at a time? Or should I do multiple rolls until I hit the required successes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T21:59:33-07:00","id":145303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CitanHyuga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=145272#post145272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If people want to switch to that forum, it is fine with me. I don't mind staying on this one either.<br /> <br /> Noodle: Please let me know how long it will take per roll to re-build and how many mortal aides, or assistants I will have. I am counting Jensven as a celestial exalted aide of course. Also, do you want me to just do one roll at a time? Or should I do multiple rolls until I hit the required successes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget CNNT to make it 12 times faster then normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T05:30:41-07:00","id":145572,"title":"","content":"Don't worry. I will be using CNNT and W-a-WM. Plus all the bonuses from help and my peerless paragon of fire XD. This will be quick and easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T07:30:38-07:00","id":145646,"title":"","content":"As per Exthalion's proposal, I'm fine with it as well; just a little wary, as I've moved pbp games around, and they tended to die when I did so. However, if everyone else wishes to do so, I'll defer to the consensus, then.<br /> <br /> Also, Tirien's past lives finally kicked in. Fun times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","user":"Dietaku","date":". 05-22-2014, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T14:25:14-07:00","id":146027,"title":"","content":"The only issue I would really have with us moving the game is that we wouldn't be contributing to the community at Onyx Path with our posts. Any post not on the Onyx Path forums is one less to generate traffic here. On the other hand, we would be generating interest on the other forum to potentially lead those other eyes here. Hmm...<br /> <br /> Long story short, I'm up for anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T20:35:16-07:00","id":146292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=144474#post144474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to hear more about Ramshackle Street.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this is the only pending request. However, giving more information may tip my hand when it comes to this, so... Time for something completely different! <br /> <br /> <b>-Novalesk Military Doctrine-</b><br /> <br /> Novalesk military doctrine focuses around a highly-mobile light infantry model. The typical Novaleski soldier is outfitted with the following items; a short spear, straight sword, shield, linen cuirass, three light javelins, a sling and fifteen bullets. These troopers are organized into squads of thirty men, which are then grouped together into a maniple consisting of five infantry squads, and an artillerist squad that mans and constructs long-range dart-throwers and/or balistae (whose parts are scattered among the rest of the maniple for ease of movement). Novalesk has no permanent formations larger than a maniple, though the informal 'Stratos' is used whenever five or more maniples are organized into a single force. <br /> <br /> Due to cultural predilections (addressed in the Novalesk national profile) the military consists of a core of semi-professional troops. <br /> <br /> The Novalesk military doctrine, therefore, revolves around bringing their superior arms and mobility to bear in conflict. This has led to use of three major tactical doctrines, each formulated around the Novaleskis primary foes. <br /> <br /> Against heavily armored tight formations like the Ordoni phallanxes, typical doctrine is to engage in a skirmisher role, using the superior mobility to stay stay outside of melee while peppering the enemy with ranged attacks. <br /> <br /> Against conscript armies, like the Therian's, doctrine calls for the general to use their superior maneuvering capability to pepper advancing enemies at range to decrease morale and then charge into melee, relying on superior discipline. <br /> <br /> Barbarian forces are fought similar to the above, but are never charged, often due to the negligible effect on morale. Typically, the general attempts to obtain a superior position, and then to hold it against on rushing barbarians. Strategos Vasil attempted to use this tactic during the current conflict, but was rendered flat-footed by the previously hidden Fae forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T20:46:54-07:00","id":146309,"title":"","content":"I would like to know about the academy's main focus for the arts and its main production of goods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T15:14:47-07:00","id":147196,"title":"","content":"This may be a stupid question Noodle but does anybody knows that I am a solar ? It's kinda hard to hide when you are summoning demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T15:22:32-07:00","id":147206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=147196#post147196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may be a stupid question Noodle but does anybody knows that I am a solar ? It's kinda hard to hide when you are summoning demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're referring to the other PCs? Probably not. You could be a thaumaturge or other sort of Exalt, as far as they know. <br /> <br /> For NPCs? Chancellor Fiero and some trusted members of his staff know. Your house patriarch knows, and probably passed the information onto the patriarch of House Nikoloi. Origenes, being a savvy and intelligent guy likely knows. Larissa, as the goddess of Novalesk's Citizenry (which you qualify as due to being a native-born Essence User) definitely knows. <br /> <br /> Select high-ranking members of the other Gentes probably know as well. I mean, those shape-shifting and necromantic assassins are as good for intelligence gathering as for killing people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T19:24:30-07:00","id":147451,"title":"","content":"Thanks Noodle, as a native of Novalesk how do the people feel towards outsiders meddling in their affairs ? Since my character was raised here I think it would affect him towards the other characters since none of them are natives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T20:10:14-07:00","id":147490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=147451#post147451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks Noodle, as a native of Novalesk how do the people feel towards outsiders meddling in their affairs ? Since my character was raised here I think it would affect him towards the other characters since none of them are natives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I threw out nation changing social magic to make the majority of people want me to be supreme leader, so you might like me regardless of anything else. If not, give me a few days to essence up and I will change your motivation to, &quot;Love, Honor, and Obey Yi Zhinan&quot; for you. No charge even. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T20:26:13-07:00","id":147496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CitanHyuga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=146309#post146309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to know about the academy's main focus for the arts and its main production of goods.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>-Academy of Sorcerous Wisdom-</b><br /> <br /> The Academy of Sorcerous Wisdom lies in a Wood-Aspected Manse in the northern section of Novalesk city. This proud institution has thirteen paths of study; eleven corresponding to each of the Arts of Thaumaturgy, as well as one each for Artificery and Sorcery. The Alchemy and Geomancy programs are the largest, with Enchantment and Exorcism programs trailing at a modest distance (though the Exorcist program's numbers are artificially inflated by the cross-pollination with the Elementalist, Demonology, Spiritism, and Necromancy programs). Following those programs are the cluster of Elementalist, Weather-Working and Husbandry, which are in-turn followed by the Demonology, Spiritism, Artificery programs. The Sorcery program would be the smallest if not for the incredibly tiny Astrology and Necromancy programs (calling them programs is considered something of an in-joke by a majority of the faculty). Thaumaturgy Programs are all designed to teach to the Adept degree, with the more specialized training condensed in a formal tutelage to a Master. Many thaumaturges pursue multiple paths simultaneously or concurrently.<br /> <br /> The Sorcery program is designed to initiate the student into Emerald Circle Sorcery only. It assumes that one who is capable of achieving the level of enlightenment and occult knowledge required to learn sorcery can learn Spells on their own without being spoon fed by a teacher. That said, the openness of the library to such students and the examples given by professors give enough information that most students don't leave the Academy without knowing a spell or two. <br /> <br /> The Artificery program is officially meant only for graduates of the Geomancy and Enchantment Programs. Though promising candidates will not be turned away, the curriculum assumes a certain level of occult knowledge and thaumaturgical expertise. Graduates of this program generally obtain at least the Initiate degree in the non-qualifying art, as well as a smattering of Elementalist rituals. <br /> <br /> The primary production of goods for the Academy are Alchemical solutions, primarily those with medicinal properties, such as the Blood-Stanching Compress, or Draught of Blessed Respite. Such items keep well and fetch a tidy sum in the metropolises in the Confederation of Rivers. Lookshy for one is constantly looking for low-price medicinal compounds, and often attempts to negotiate trade contracts for the goods the Academy produces (though their close relationship with Ordon prevents any such agreement from occurring). A significant percentage of the products produced are purchased by the infirmaries and hospices in Novalesk, who hoard them for emergency cases. This is only the most common grouping of products; if an Alchemical formulae exists, chances are you can find it at the Academy.<br /> <br /> Other products produced are a number of magically treated tools and weapons, designed to be the next-best-thing to artifacts (such as sword blades that won't break and plows that stay good for decades). Many of these goods are sold at profit to local merchants, who distribute them among the nation; the rest are sold to the resident Guild factors. <br /> <br /> The Artificery also produces a small number of artifacts (primarily weapons) each year. They repair man more, however, as Scavenger Lord is a respectable profession among Novalesk's elite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T21:40:32-07:00","id":147564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=147451#post147451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks Noodle, as a native of Novalesk how do the people feel towards outsiders meddling in their affairs ? Since my character was raised here I think it would affect him towards the other characters since none of them are natives.</div> </div> </div> </div>The nation is built on migrant groups; the Cadet houses almost exclusively come from large migrations or groups of refugees. This lends most to a somewhat cosmopolitan viewpoint. As long as you speak the language, and don't go preaching Immaculate bullshit, they'll probably tolerate you.<br /> <br /> Certain groups aren't really well received though. Lookshans, for example, have a history of helping Ordon, and are therefore viewed with suspicion by many (including pretty much all of Gens Spyrus).<br /> <br /> They're generally somewhat wary of outsiders trying to muck around inside the Gov't though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid"