"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=147842#post147842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow well this is gonna be a fun game... (obvious sarcasm) We are suppose to work <b>together </b> not <b>for</b> you and talking can only take so you so far.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the info about the academy Noodle very useful to know these things</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a joke, and if that wasn't communicated well enough by the <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I am sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T10:51:53-07:00","id":147968,"title":"","content":"Nah it's ok I had bad experience with players trying to force the other players character to do what they wanted with mind altering magic so I just don't take these sort of things easily, I'm sorry if overreacted","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T22:07:40-07:00","id":148388,"title":"","content":"Yeah! Controlling other peoples' PCs is MY JOB.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T22:30:01-07:00","id":148395,"title":"","content":"Noodle, can I get people's motivations from MoSM?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T22:32:55-07:00","id":148397,"title":"","content":"<b>-The Gilded Triangle-</b><br /> <br /> Of the many Anathema Cults that have sprung up in Theros over the centuries, none are more tenacious than the Gilded Triangle. The Black Cowl may boast a longer history, but it had the advantage of basing its operations outside of Theros' borders. <br /> <br /> The Therian authorities first became aware of the Gilded Triangle in RY 658. It had managed to subvert a number of peasants through mild subversion of immaculate dogma. These deviations seemed inconsequential to the average layman, but when examined by the proper authorities, they collectively constituted a major heresy in Immaculate canon. Though the heresy was quickly stamped down, a two decades later, a different heresy of similar structure, but differing dogma appeared. The two incidents seemed unconnected, until a third incident of similar pattern appeared thirteen years later. The pattern continued to repeat itself, reappearing between ten and twenty years after the previous purge. The last resurgence was twelve years ago. <br /> <br /> Authorities have been baffled as to the root of these incidents. If the dogma had been the same thing resurging later, they would simply concluded that the purges where incomplete. However, each heresy was similar in structure, but differing in details, suggesting that some intelligence is controlling them from the shadows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T09:22:59-07:00","id":148738,"title":"","content":"Noodle do I have access to tools and laboratories in the academy ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T13:57:31-07:00","id":148925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=148397#post148397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>-The Gilded Triangle-</b><br /> <br /> Of the many Anathema Cults that have sprung up in Theros over the centuries, none are more tenacious than the Gilded Triangle. The Black Cowl may boast a longer history, but it had the advantage of basing its operations outside of Theros' borders.<br /> <br /> The Therian authorities first became aware of the Gilded Triangle in RY 658. It had managed to subvert a number of peasants through mild subversion of immaculate dogma. These deviations seemed inconsequential to the average layman, but when examined by the proper authorities, they collectively constituted a major heresy in Immaculate canon. Though the heresy was quickly stamped down, a two decades later, a different heresy of similar structure, but differing dogma appeared. The two incidents seemed unconnected, until a third incident of similar pattern appeared thirteen years later. The pattern continued to repeat itself, reappearing between ten and twenty years after the previous purge. The last resurgence was twelve years ago.<br /> <br /> Authorities have been baffled as to the root of these incidents. If the dogma had been the same thing resurging later, they would simply concluded that the purges where incomplete. However, each heresy was similar in structure, but differing in details, suggesting that some intelligence is controlling them from the shadows.</div> </div> </div> </div>And why hasn't the Wyld Hunt just burned the city to the ground yet, then? These people have clearly been tainted by Evil Destiny.<br /> <br /> (Ecumenicism/Dogmatism as a weapon? How deliciously subversive)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T19:42:00-07:00","id":149086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=148397#post148397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>-The Gilded Triangle-</b><br /> <br /> Of the many Anathema Cults that have sprung up in Theros over the centuries, none are more tenacious than the Gilded Triangle. The Black Cowl may boast a longer history, but it had the advantage of basing its operations outside of Theros' borders.<br /> <br /> The Therian authorities first became aware of the Gilded Triangle in RY 658. It had managed to subvert a number of peasants through mild subversion of immaculate dogma. These deviations seemed inconsequential to the average layman, but when examined by the proper authorities, they collectively constituted a major heresy in Immaculate canon. Though the heresy was quickly stamped down, a two decades later, a different heresy of similar structure, but differing dogma appeared. The two incidents seemed unconnected, until a third incident of similar pattern appeared thirteen years later. The pattern continued to repeat itself, reappearing between ten and twenty years after the previous purge. The last resurgence was twelve years ago.<br /> <br /> Authorities have been baffled as to the root of these incidents. If the dogma had been the same thing resurging later, they would simply concluded that the purges where incomplete. However, each heresy was similar in structure, but differing in details, suggesting that some intelligence is controlling them from the shadows.</div> </div> </div> </div>I smell Gold Faction involvement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T16:18:04-07:00","id":149782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=148738#post148738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Noodle do I have access to tools and laboratories in the academy ?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a faculty member, you would have access to the academy's resources, yes.<br /> <br /> However, any expended material (like reagents for Alchemy or metals for artifice) must be checked out, and their cost will be docked from your pay; items constructed can be immediately sold back to the academy for a quick profit, or placed in the Academy stores for a more substantial cut when sold to a third party.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T17:59:52-07:00","id":149879,"title":"","content":"Still no requests, so I continue with the randomness.<br /> <br /> <b>-Midea-</b><br /> <br /> According to folklore, the founder of Gens Midea arrived in the court of the Archon from parts unknown shortly after the turn of the fifth century Post-Contagion. The woman entered the court, and demanded she be given a position of power. The Archon asked for a demonstration of her skills, demanding that she prove herself worthy of a position within his court. To answer, she fought his bodyguard to a standstill, and preved herself equal to the Chancellor in Sorcery. And a dozen other tests, each one proving herself a master of many skills. <br /> <br /> Though he found her skills awe inspiring, the Archon stated that she had not proven herself worthy of his court in any one skill. To this she responded that, while his court boasted warriors and poets and sorcerers to match her skill, did he have anyone who was a master of all of those skills? Inspired, the Archon, a member of House Nikoloi, adopted her into his court, and granted her status as a Cadet branch of his family.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T19:26:51-07:00","id":150952,"title":"","content":"Do you have a history for my cadet house ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T08:39:21-07:00","id":151325,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://i880.photobucket.com/albums/ac10/Dietaku/1401238390197.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> I found this guy while on the Exalted general on /tg/, and thought, &quot;Hey, It's Jensven!&quot; Just thought I'd share it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.the