sage\">What is the difficulty and number of target successes? Depending on how well Jensven does... I might do it too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Difficulty is 3, Target successes is 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T21:41:20-07:00","id":165616,"title":"","content":"You could also investigate the fae weapon I gave to you for your lab. You could even summon an agate for travel or something tonight too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T21:42:01-07:00","id":165617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=165583#post165583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Noodle I seem to have small problem since I mostly play Dawn type characters I don't have the slightest clue of what to do with Vykos, I can't really summon things since it takes about a day per summoning and my other skills seem to be mostly for the library type of action, some advice would be welcomed if you don't mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could play politics with Yi. You could summon Demons (It only takes all night). You could use your Investigative prowess to watch out for Fae activity; be an early warning system. <br /> <br /> Or you could do one of your specialties. the Genesis might not work right now. But hey, you might be able to find something relevant in the libraries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T21:43:12-07:00","id":165618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CitanHyuga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=165616#post165616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could also investigate the fae weapon I gave to you for your lab. You could even summon an agate for travel or something tonight too.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are also things!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T22:17:37-07:00","id":165641,"title":"","content":"@Belkra-<br /> <br /> I see your post. It is awesome, you did good, and qualifies as a 3-die. I'm going to hold off posting in response till I hear what the other academy people will be doing, and to try to keep the day rolling as close as possible for those in one location.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T18:21:46-07:00","id":168439,"title":"","content":"Part three of Terrestrials of Novalesk! Here we have a man who recently appeared in the narrative<br /> <br /> <b>-Nikoloi Argyus-</b><br /> <br /> Well known to be well into his second century of life, this Earth dragon is also a childhood friend of the current Pyrtaneis, Zophyrus Linon. Fascinated with bureaucracy and economics, many in Novalesk would have considered his chosen profession below that of a prince of the Earth. However, Argyus has proven himself to be a wizard in managing projects and performing complex economic calculations. If he were born in the Realm, Argyus would likely be a high-ranking bureaucrat in the thousand scales. Indeed, his (relatively) high breeding and recent Therian ancestry cause some to believe that he has Ragara blood in his veins.<br /> <br /> Argyus has a peculiar fascination with roads. None know exactly what started this; only that he has been instrumental in causing his house in expand its road network, and is constantly pushing the Capital government for funding to do even more.<br /> <br /> Due to their being of the same Gens, many assume that Argyus and Chancellor Feiro are closely related. This is a false assumption; they come from completely different branches of the family, and, at absolute closest, are fourth cousins.<br /> <br /> Argyus looks to be an oldish man of middling height, with a large balding plate. His terrestrial heritage shows through when he smiles, however, as his teeth are seemingly made of the purest white marble. Rumor is that his entire skeleton is like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","user":"Noodle","date":". 06-13-2014, 11:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T21:01:54-07:00","id":168581,"title":"","content":"Part four of Terrestrials of Novalesk! this young lady has been making a lot of waves in the political scene!<br /> <br /> -Althea Sanna-<br /> <br /> This young lady exalted nearly eight months ago, and has caused many a ripple in Novalesk since. This charismatic and strongly opinionated young woman exalted in her fifteenth year, indiciating strong terrestrial lineage. This has caused many to believe that her mother, who was a member of the Novlaeski embassy in Theros for several years before Sanna's birth was not very faithful to her husband. <br /> <br /> While her charisma and leadership talent would make her a strong candidate for the Archon, her lack of experience and general naivete hold many at pause for the moment. The potential of being crushed under long-term Zophyrus-controlled hegemony also brings many to oppose the young idealist. <br /> <br /> Sanna is a short, stocky young woman. She has a pale complexion as if perpetually sea-sick, and she sports long straight navy hair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T22:33:25-07:00","id":168642,"title":"","content":"Just to hit the hornet's nest with a daiklave:<br /> <br /> You mentioned that celestial exalts are generally considered quasi divine for the purpose of holding political office (aka, they aren't technically supposed to). How does that work with Terrestrials? Given that the Elemental dragons are at the very least the Terrestrial analog of the celestial incarna, DBs could be held to the same godly standard. Sanna's blurb indicates this is not the case. Is this hypocracy, or one of those cultural blindspots I can wedge myself in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T22:46:12-07:00","id":168644,"title":"","content":"Part five of Terrestrials of Novalesk! The swashbuckling captain:<br /> <br /> -Spyrus Thales- <br /> <br /> A thirty-two year year old water aspect, Thales is the commander of Novalesk's middling naval forces. When he came of age, Thales left his family to make his fortune (an old tradition in Novalesk, though it is only really practiced by Spyrus and Ptreas these days). Rather than joining one of the family mercenary companies, however, he joined a completely unrelated Confederation of Rivers river-boat based mercenary band. Over the next three years, he rose in ranks in the mercenary company, until he eventually became the head and primary owner of the company. He amassed a small fortune over the five following years. During this time frame, he also amassed a reputation as a womanizing, swashbuckling rogue. With a fortune in silver and a fleet of river-borne mercenaries, and a Terrestrial exaltation Thales returned home. <br /> <br /> That was seven years ago. In the intervening time, he has turned his mercenary band into a crack naval force, patrolling the waterways around his homeland. His reputation as a womanizing scoundrel continues, though none can give any definitive proof to either allegation. <br /> <br /> Thales wears flamboyant clothes, made by a divine tailor in Great Forks. He is tall and swarthy, and shares his cousin Artemia's flaxen hair (His father is Artemia's mother's older brother). He wields dual wavecrasher diaklaives in battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T23:02:03-07:00","id":168651,"title":"","content":"What? Come on, man. It's obvious.<br /> <br /> The Anathema, no matter of whether they stole their power or had it granted upon them, are still directly imbued by the Divine Powers of the Celestines. Their powers are still <i>of</i> the Celestines, making them Divine by brevet.<br /> <br /> The Terrestrials are chosen champions of the Elemental Dragons, an Exalted host raised by blood and spiritual enlightenment to rule and guide mankind. They are Exalted <i>by </i>the Dragons, not <i>of</i> the Dragons.<br /> <br /> Silly Exthalion. It's totally obvious!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","user":"Noodle","date":". 06-14-2014, 02:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T17:19:41-07:00","id":171223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=169521#post169521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The resplendent sun smiled, though no one saw it.<br /> <br /> Yi had a lot of smiles. He had the polite smile when paying attention to fools not worth the air they fouled with their next breath. He had the smile for when other people accomplished something and he couldn't bring himself to be genuinely happy for them. He even had a few for when the feelings inside him couldn't stay in the tiny vessel beating in his chest and had to spill over into the muscles of his face. This one was of that last kind, a smile for when what happened was unwanted but expected and he could not bring himself to be upset by it.<br /> <br /> &quot;You are right, much work shall be required. We will find a way through this, even if it means I must depart. I revealed myself to help this nation and if it is better for this nation I shall remove myself. I do not think it will come to that, there is too much good yet undone for me to be so selfish as to run. Yet whatever troubles or triumphs are or might come about, this too shall pass.&quot;<br /> <br /> After sitting down at the table he said, &quot;Would you like any help in preparing your response? I am hardly in a position to brag, but I was the 'Young Tiger of the River' who beggared the 'Five Silver Kings' and negotiated the Accord of Earth and Water.&quot;<br /> <br /> It was bragging of the most shameless sort, bringing up two of the biggest diplomatic victories Lookshy had won in the Scavenger Lands in living memory. The so called &quot;Five Kings&quot;, really four factors and one reigning plutocrat, had attempted to popularize the silver standard in the Confederation of Rivers. When the dust settled all five were paupers and Lookshy sat on a stockpile of exotic materials and silver. The Accord of Earth and Water that followed was Lookshy's response to the collapse of several of the largest fortunes in the Confederation, greatly expanding its own supply networks and prestige.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Well, this explains why he was at the command level of an artillery unit without any dots in, you know, Archery. Or War. He was a political officer!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T18:01:39-07:00","id":171246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=171223#post171223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh. Well, this explains why he was at the command level of an artillery unit without any dots in, you know, Archery. Or War. He was a political officer!</div> </div> </div> </div>5 dots in Bureaucracy = &quot;I'm sorry, was that red tape? I thought you were just hanging festive ribbon. Not like it was doing anything anyway.&quot;<br /> 5 dots in Socialize = &quot;I'm sorry, did you say something? I was just confirming my lunch appointment with your boss, my dinner appointment with his boss, and my rsvp to the private party for the general staff this weekend.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T18:11:54-07:00","id":171252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=171246#post171246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 5 dots in Bureaucracy = &quot;I'm sorry, was that red tape? I thought you were just hanging festive ribbon. Not like it was doing anything anyway.&quot;<br /> 5 dots in Socialize = &quot;I'm sorry, did you say something? I was just confirming my lunch appointment with your boss, my dinner appointment with his boss, and my rsvp to the private party for the general staff this weekend.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This just reinforces my assertion that he was a politico this whole time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T18:15:37-07:00","id":171254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=171252#post171252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This just reinforces my assertion that he was a politico this whole time.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Please</i>, it isn't like he traded political favors to stay assigned to the unit of the DB he had a crush on or was given insanely simple and specific orders that required him to know nothing of actual tactics and just act as a maintenance man while trained soldiers did the shooting.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh wait... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (I mean he certainly wasn't put in charge because a small scale exercise to response to a border skirmish turned into a major battle when enemy forces proved larger then reported and the actual artillery commander was killed in the opening ambush. That would just be silly and totally isn't what his backstory says.)<br /> <br /> Edit 2: I mean he has Valor1, would he hide out in the unit that is far from the front like a certain Commissar known to be a hero of the Imperium?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 06-16-2014, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T18:29:48-07:00","id":171261,"title":"","content":"YI ZHINAN, HERO OF THE SHOGUNATE, huh?<br /> <br /> ... I'm strangely okay with this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T18:42:34-07:00","id":171269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=171254#post171254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Please</i>, it isn't like he traded political favors to stay assigned to the unit of the DB he had a crush on or was given insanely simple and specific orders that required him to know nothing of actual tactics and just act as a maintenance man while trained soldiers did the shooting.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh wait... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (I mean he certainly wasn't put in charge because a small scale exercise to response to a border skirmish turned into a major battle when enemy forces proved larger then reported and the actual artillery commander was killed in the opening ambush. That would just be silly and totally isn't what his backstory says.)<br /> <br /> Edit 2: I mean he has Valor1, would he hide out in the unit that is far from the front like a certain Commissar known to be a hero of the Imperium?</div> </div> </div> </div>You. I like you. <br /> <br /> Also, reminds me of one of Noodle's Sid's backstories. Tell the man about Ascendant Sword; the man who got the go-ahead from the Mouth of Peace to not only be a married itinerant monk., but also to keep his head un-shaved.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> He knew a Solar who looked like Sextes Jylis and the two conned her into approving it</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T16:30:23-07:00","id":172156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=171269#post171269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You. I like you.<br /> <br /> Also, reminds me of one of Noodle's Sid's backstories. Tell the man about Ascendant Sword; the man who got the go-ahead from the Mouth of Peace to not only be a married itinerant monk., but also to keep his head un-shaved.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> He knew a Solar who looked like Sextes Jylis and the two conned her into approving it</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, Sword. My favorite PC ever. His backstory was an ever-evolving mess.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> He grew up on the mean streets of Great Forks, until his family was adopted into a minor Lookshan Gens when his older Brother Exalted as an Earth Dragon. After passing twenty without exaltation, he left Lookshy to make his fortune, eventually being picked up by the BoD and Exalting as a Chosen of Secrets. There he became bestest buddies with an enlightened Pterok sorcerer.<br /> <br /> After his training, he set up an identity as an Air Dragon outcaste who was adopted into house Ledaal (The Elders of House Ledaal knew he was a Sidereal). As part of his 'Dynastic training' he got sent to the Palace of the Tamed Storm. Using his Sidereal training and the dreaded half-brick-in-a-sock (a dread weapon from the Streets of Great Forks), he graduated in exactly a day; there was a riot, in which the entire dorm was destroyed. Despite everyone knowing that he started it, the fact that no one could pin it on him, and the fact that both his uniform and bunk were completely immaculate, got him an early graduation.<br /> <br /> He got married to a native Ledaal Air Dragon, became a wandering itinerant monk WHILE married, with a full head of hair, and without knowing any of the Immaculate Styles, and then &quot;joined the Cult of the Illuminated&quot;, as a reformed Immaculate, in order to Be the liaison between the Cult and an independent Solar association. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That's just the bones, too. He had many other exploits, like winning the Tournament of Flames, getting a behemoth daughter, and pretending to be a Terrestrial so well that none of the ten or so Celestials he regularly interacted with caught on until he told them.<br /> <br /> Basically, every single session, something else was added on to his backstory, making it more ridiculous as the game went on.<br /> <br /> Also, he hugged Paisap. This happened during play. My games are weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T16:55:56-07:00","id":172183,"title":"","content":"Sixth and Final installment of Terrestrials of Novalesk!<br /> <br /> <b>-Origenon Hollidane-</b><br /> <br /> Origenon Hollidane (she prefers Holly) was found on the steps of the Temple of Origenes eighteen years ago by the deity himself. The deity found the babe wrapped in fine silks, with a jade token giving the child's name on one side and an ornate High Realm &quot;R&quot; on the other. Origenes adopted her as his own child, and raised her himself, with the aid of his elderly wife and the support of his then fifty-five year old biological daughter. It came as a shock to many when the young woman, who was seemingly being groomed to enter the priesthood, exalted as a Wood Dragon three years ago. <br /> <br /> Since then, she her skills as a performer and a churegeon have rocketed to supernatural levels, and she has discovered a knack for archery and woodsmanship. She has yet to show any interest in politics, finding simple joy in travelling the nation. She is rumored to be a close friend of the recently-exalted Artemia. <br /> <br /> Holly is a heavily tanned athletic woman of average height. She typically wears red woodsman's leathers, and uses a green jade powerbow. She is rumored to be studying an ancient martial art that uses such weapons. According to those rumors, her teacher is a Lesser Elemental Dragon who Origenes blackmailed into taking the job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T17:29:22-07:00","id":173381,"title":"","content":"So I just saw in Dreams of the First Age you can make a living manse does that mean that you can make living tools and other things like ship or living daiklave ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T19:20:22-07:00","id":173497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=173381#post173381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I just saw in Dreams of the First Age you can make a living manse does that mean that you can make living tools and other things like ship or living daiklave ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! All you have to do is get some demons, render them into chalcanth, and then use that in the construction of the artifact to make it gain a demonic intelligence. <br /> <br /> What? You don't want an infernal blade? Then you just need to get a ton of gossamer, head into the Wyld and weave it together.<br /> <br /> You don't want it to be a giant Wyld monster either? Well, then, you can talk to a biotechnician, then. I'm sure they can make living arms, armor and vehicles, too.<br /> <br /> Or, do you mean a ship or weapon with a sentient animating intelligence or aware little god? For Manses and ships, yes, this is possible. For swords, not as written, no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T19:48:16-07:00","id":173524,"title":"","content":"Oh, going to give your metody any standing orders, Magnusar? Just for the record.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T19:56:05-07:00","id":173538,"title":"","content":"Order him to keep being snarky. He's fun.