7:00","id":211378,"title":"","content":"Sure, I'll help, if you don't mind doing this after the war. I'm kinda indisposed at the moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T13:23:26-07:00","id":211600,"title":"","content":"I was referring more for the ability to raise a force for vengeance. Point is, someone seen as an ally to Jensven comes up missing and he will find out why they are missing. If they just happen to be killed because of some stupid prejudice for a &quot;sins of the fathers&quot; scenario, well he's just going to call bull on it and wreck house. He doesn't realize this would be his motivation, but his player is thinking further down-board than make armor/golems, play with Shadow, and fight if I have to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T14:17:46-07:00","id":211655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=211600#post211600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was referring more for the ability to raise a force for vengeance. Point is, someone seen as an ally to Jensven comes up missing and he will find out why they are missing. If they just happen to be killed because of some stupid prejudice for a &quot;sins of the fathers&quot; scenario, well he's just going to call bull on it and wreck house. He doesn't realize this would be his motivation, but his player is thinking further down-board than make armor/golems, play with Shadow, and fight if I have to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Our characters will have to speak before I leave then. After all, the foundation of diplomacy is the ability to threaten unwinnable war to the other party. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T14:29:11-07:00","id":211662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=211655#post211655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Our characters will have to speak before I leave then. After all, the foundation of diplomacy is the ability to threaten unwinnable war to the other party. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I guess you're screwed then. Ordon has never lost a defensive war, and everyone in the area knows it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T17:48:46-07:00","id":211863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=211662#post211662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess you're screwed then. Ordon has never lost a defensive war, and everyone in the area knows it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have they won a war waged against them by three Chosen of the Sun, one Chosen of Luna, and one Chosen of the Maiden of Secrets? (This is not counting Yi, of course)<br /> <br /> The point we are forgetting here with this bit of conversation is that the Fae present a more pressing threat to Novalesk. If we are to see the nation to the point that it will even be able to think about waging war on Ordon, we need to deal with those fricken' fairies first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T22:03:36-07:00","id":212073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=211662#post211662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess you're screwed then. Ordon has never lost a defensive war, and everyone in the area knows it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jadeborn don't have perfect social defenses. :P<br /> <br /> Just to be clear, I would never do most of the things I say. It wouldn't be fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T16:44:24-07:00","id":214019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=212073#post212073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Jadeborn don't have perfect social defenses. :P<br /> <br /> Just to be clear, I would never do most of the things I say. It wouldn't be fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's hard to tell sometimes. Once, I had an NPC request 'The Heart of A Sun' from the players. They spent half an hour trying to figure out how to remove the Solar's heart and have him survive with the resources they had on hand. Cut to two sessions down the road, when this is a moot point (they had found one elsewhere), they find a doctor and <i>have her remove the Solar's heart anyway. </i>I find it hard to tell when my players will and will not actually do something in Exalted because of situations like this. <br /> <br /> Riddle me this though; If the Jadefolk run Ordon, why did the Ambassador, who is likely a high ranking member of their society, not know who Autochthon is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T17:56:56-07:00","id":214124,"title":"","content":"hey! He got an orichalcum heart! And she was great at the surgery! It was only a small risk of dying... it worked out well though <br /> XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T12:52:38-07:00","id":214999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=214019#post214019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Riddle me this though; If the Jadefolk run Ordon, why did the Ambassador, who is likely a high ranking member of their society, not know who Autochthon is?</div> </div> </div> </div>I had indeed considered that point. It is possible that the jadeborn do not use the name, perhaps reasoning that Autochthon is too holy or numinous for human conception. The Architect, Maker, and Engineer are all aspects of him as exemplified by the various castes, (which humans do not have a great deal of contact with).<br /> <br /> You did say that AT LEAST one rumor was true. <br /> <br /> Or they could actually be gods (made by Autochthon or otherwise). Or (in character) Autochthon isn't anyone important and the throwaway line where Yi read about him in a fragment of text from the first age was just venerating some minor diety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T18:36:49-07:00","id":218645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=214999#post214999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You did say that AT LEAST one rumor was true.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is truth. I will also say that, at this point, at least one of the posts is comprised entirely of ture rumors. Stew on that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T18:38:38-07:00","id":218646,"title":"","content":"Before we continue on, I would like to inform the group that Magnusar has informed me that he has lost interest in playing Vykos, and therefore has bowed out of the game. Like Sea before him, Vykos is now an NPC. <br /> <br /> That is all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T18:54:33-07:00","id":218674,"title":"","content":"I'm working on making enough awesome ruins and stuff to throw you guys (Read: Hyuga) off of my scent after Diekatu's statements. Have some other stuff instead!<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons of Novalesk</b><br /> Novalesk is the progeny of the Second age, born from the Balorian Crusade and shaped by countless conflicts. Is it any wonder then, that regalia there is solely weaponry? What follows is a cross section of the regalia of certain positions in Novalesk.<br /> <br /> <b>The Blade of the Archon</b>: Forged by Myrinne for her own use, and left behind on her final fateful journey, this blade of Starmetal and Gossamer is a long and broad Daikliave with an ornate Orichalcum hilt. It's origin and imposing nature made it an easy choice as the symbol of the Archon on the formalization of the Nation. It is rumored that the blade can imbue the holder with a portion of the fabled founder's strength and intellect.<br /> <br /> <b>The Three Swords of the Founders</b>: Nikoloi made these three Short Daikliaves after his mother's death for his brothers and himself. Made of White Jade and Bronze, the sole distinguishing feature between these blades is the respective Mons of their original owners inscribed in the forte. Asside from their construction and origin, there is nothing truly spectacular about them. Regardless, these three blades are the official regalia of the patriarchs of the original three Gentes.<br /> <br /> <b>The Pyrtanein Scepter</b>: Given the pattern of weapons as regalia, a Scepter seems discordant, at least until one considers that a scepter is really just an increadibly ornate cudgel. Found in a first-age ruin by a local scavenger lord, it was donated to the state in the fifth century Post-Contagion. The Ruby-encrusted gold cudgel is rumored to have eldritch powers that bind individuals to speak the truth and obey basic rules of etiquette.<br /> <br /> <b>Magisterial Axes</b>: Each one of these jade-steel Grimcleavers is supposedly made at the hand of Origenes himself for use by his law-enforcer priests. It is said that the magistrate's Essence is interwoven with that of their weapon, making it impossible for anyone else to use it. The weapons are therefore symbols of the wielder's authority to enforce laws and adjudicate trials of National law. Traditionally, when a magistrate levies the death penalty, they use these weapons to enforce their ruling.<br /> <br /> <b>Panoply of Origenes</b>: Historically, Orignenes has owned two pieces of Divine Panolpy; a silvery stave etched with jade, and a straight broad blade of similar construction (how a relatively minor Terrestrial spirit managed this feat, he does not reveal). Accoriding to rumor, these artifacts possess the power to gift and remove Essence, respectively. The blade, however, was granted to Archon Larissa upon her apotheosis, making her own.<br /> <br /> Ruins and Tombs will be coming soon, I promise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T19:15:33-07:00","id":218685,"title":"","content":"Muahahaha. Derailing skill max! Improvise faster! Ahahahahaha! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","