"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=219001#post219001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No mention of defensive implements. No shields, no armor....I'm a sad puppy.</div> </div> </div> </div>That just means you get to be the one to forge them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T10:49:38-07:00","id":222298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=221378#post221378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That just means you get to be the one to forge them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the way you think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T11:49:56-07:00","id":222324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=219001#post219001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No mention of defensive implements. No shields, no armor....I'm a sad puppy.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I wasn't really considering them t be included in the 'only weapons category'. Also to be honest, the whole thing stemmed from me deciding to make the symbol of the Archon a sword on a whim and then extrapolating from there; the Founders have been established to mimic their mother in many things, the Pyrtanneis is the most formal/bureaucratic position, so they get the least weapon-like weapon. The Magisterial axes are actually me lifting and altering the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fasces\" target=\"_blank\">fasces</a> from Imperial Rome, and Origenes' panoply was established as soon as you guy's got to the city, so... yeah. One could argue that the replica-stave that Yi is running round with would count as a regail-wepaon, but he lacks the strength to use it effectively, so... yeah.<br /> <br /> Looking back at it, it is rather sword-centric, which is not my intention. I said in the Chancellor's background post that his staff is the Chancellor's regalia. [memo to self: make compilation doc of setting info] The Stragoi have paired half-spears, one of Red Jade, one of Blue. I haven't even decided yet what the heads of the three other Gentes have, but none of them fit swords. Thesmothetes get their own regalia-weapon, either one of their own, or one gifted by the Archon (but since there are no Thesmothetes at present, its a moot point).<br /> <br /> But I digress. Thinking on it, I can only think of one instance in which some sort of defensive implement would be appropriate:<br /> <br /> <b>The Guardian Shield</b><br /> This moonsilver shield has no official name, but it is recognized throughout Novalesk as the &quot;Guardian Shield&quot;. It is the shield of the Archon's bodyguard, and it marks the bearer as able to carry any weapons wherever in violation of any law or custom. When inactive, the moonsilver shield condenses into a large bracer. When active, it flows out into an amorphous disk that independently defends the owner or any one individual they desire. It is said that Midea made this shield with her own hands to protect the Archon; because of this, the bodyguards of the Archon have been Mideans for the past several centuries.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=221378#post221378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That just means you get to be the one to forge them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would require someone in power to solidify their authority and make it official regalia. I have no idea how you would plan to do THAT one. [/sarcasm]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","user":"Noodle","date":". 08-08-2014, 02:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T14:53:03-07:00","id":222473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CitanHyuga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=218685#post218685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Muahahaha. Derailing skill max! Improvise faster! Ahahahahaha! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Fine!<br /> <br /> <b>The Kree Monoliths</b><br /> In the north of Novalesk, there lies a series of giant monoliths. Seemingly grown from the ground out of yellow stone and garnet crystals, these monoliths predate the Shogunate. They serve no known purpose or function, despite the attempts of Novaleski savants to discover their purpose. Some say that they serve as gateways to the Demon City or the Underworld. Others, that the offer protection from the Wyld. The only thing that is known is found on the smallest stone, only the size of a large desk. The stone bears precise Old Realm Script which says, &quot;Kree Red-Wings raised these stones.&quot; Who Kree Red-Wings was, and why they raised the stones, however, is left shrouded in mystery.<br /> <br /> <b>The Singing Statues</b><br /> In the marshlands of southern Geherin, there is a large ruin that the Geherin give wide berth. This ruin is a lightly walled complex, some three square miles in area, and it has no known form of traps, save its occupants. Hundreds of living statues reside in the ruins, either pacing through endless loops or fixed in place. These beings, often resembling disproportionate humans or beastfolk, are not aggressive, and will not even defend themselves if attacked. Each one, however, roars out a unique hauntingly sick song, which together forms a cacophonous din that drives men mad, and few who enter leave with their sanity, if ever at all. Those occasional Geherin that enter that manage to leave with a portion of their wits intact often become Skalds, as the experience supposedly grants them the ability to see the future. Such is the fate of Orin Dead-Eyes, a Terrestrial Hero who braved the ruins two decades ago, and lost his sight in the process.<br /> Even the Fae are not immune to this, as the music of the statues rends asunder their thin venier of story and narrative. Some claim that Fae slain this way calcify into new statues, adding a new song to the horrid cacophony.<br /> <br /> <b>The Lumen Pyramid</b><br /> Two weeks travel South-Southeast of Lake Vera, the rolling green Grasslands break way into red-brown desert. At the rough center of the desert, there lies a giant gilded pyramid. Despite being the proving grounds for young, foolhardy Novaleski Scavenger Lords for centuries, the site remains undespoiled. The Pyramid is rife with deadly traps, automaton scarabs that suck all the fluids from their victims, and golden mummified warriors. Most who survive simply encounter the corpes of a previous expedition and leave.<br /> <br /> One man, centuries ago, emerged from the pyramid, half delirious with thirst and mortally wounded. He claimed to have made it to the treasure-room, wherein an Anathema god-king is interred in all his regalia, his heart still blazing with his unholy power. He died not long after.<br /> <br /> <b>The Tomb of Gens Heftes</b><br /> The region now encompassing Theros and Novalesk and Ordon was known as Towering Prefecture during the Shogunate. The Prefecture was ruled by Gens Heftes, who claimed to have lived in the area for thousands of years. The northwestern portion of the prefecture bordered into the Metagapalan mountain range, and there the Gens laid its dead. A sprawling underground complex holds hundreds of individual tombs, each one the final resting place of a single Gens member. Though each of the Terrestrial was entombed with a full regalia of artifacts and other goods personally important to them.<br /> Yet, even a Terrestrial Gens of great history and wealth could not afford to leave such a wealth of magics unused. A decade after death, the Gens would exhume the dead, to remove any items of magical puissance or great material value. Only items with only sentimental value would be left behind with the stripped corpse. Only two dozen or so corpses were left with their artifacts when the Contagion-weakened Gens retreated from the Balorian legions.<br /> <br /> <i>That should be enough to obfuscate matters. Now that that's done with, does anyone have any other requests?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T15:29:40-07:00","id":223657,"title":"","content":"I am definitely interested in more information concerning the nearest shadowland if you have any. Also, any rumors concerning Infernal Anathema or Akuma would be appreciated. I have been playing all this background information off as something that my character doesn't know, but may eventually figure out if he asks the right questions and pokes his nose into the right businesses. Am I correct in this assumption.<br /> <br /> Definitely excited about the Lumen Pyramid. We aren't going to be going there for a while I would wager, but it would be exciting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T17:04:36-07:00","id":223724,"title":"","content":"Noodle, a couple of quick questions:<br /> <br /> Approximately how long will it take for the second force to head out against the fey?<br /> How long is the trip to Ordon?<br /> What are the procedures for a new Gens joining Novalesk?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T18:39:36-07:00","id":223749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=223657#post223657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am definitely interested in more information concerning the nearest shadowland if you have any. Also, any rumors concerning Infernal Anathema or Akuma would be appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regarding the Shadowland; do you mean the Forests of Bone, or the Ash-Mount Hill? There is more I can tell you of the former, but there's not much I can say about the latter. <br /> <br /> Infernals and Akuma? They'd probably be hiding too well to be directly noticeable as such. Plus, me telling you would ruin the surprise when I drop RotSE on you. Wait! Uh... forget I said that?<br /> <br /> And who's to say I haven't been dropping rumors of Infernal and Akuma activity already? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=223657#post223657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been playing all this background information off as something that my character doesn't know, but may eventually figure out if he asks the right questions and pokes his nose into the right businesses. Am I correct in this assumption.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're ... about right.<br /> <br /> The background information is assumed to be information that would be readily available; it's things that you would either find out in normal conversations with the locals or information that people would readily offer if asked. Essentially, it's info I wouldn't force you to roll to get if we were around a tabletop. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=223657#post223657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Definitely excited about the Lumen Pyramid. We aren't going to be going there for a while I would wager, but it would be exciting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I aim to please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T19:15:21-07:00","id":223768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=223724#post223724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Noodle, a couple of quick questions:<br /> <br /> Approximately how long will it take for the second force to head out against the fey?<br /> How long is the trip to Ordon?<br /> What are the procedures for a new Gens joining Novalesk?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Four days, forced march. A week or so otherwise. Maybe more if the weather is against you. <br /> <br /> 2) Ordon the Nation? You could be on its borders in a day if you traveled by boat. Ordon the city? Five days or so, depending on method of transportation. <br /> <br /> 3) Ah. I wondered when this would be asked. <br /> <br /> First, one must obtain a sponsor Gens. While the law doesn't say so, after the inclusion of Gens Spyrus and the creation of the Cadet House system, it is expected that the family be a Cadet House, and the sponsor Gens is their patron. <br /> <br /> Second, the prospective Gens must be considered to have been &quot;tied into Novalesk by bonds of culture and blood&quot;. This is interpreted as of present to be that at least 75% of the House in question must have been born and raised in Novalesk, as must have their parents. <br /> <br /> Third, the prospective family must be large enough to have at least one Representative in the Boule with population alone. (So, you need to have at least 2% of the total Gentes population after you're added in. At present, that would be slightly over 2000 members). <br /> <br /> Fourth, the sponsored family must have a home town or city. It is expected that this town/city is built by the family (either by their hands or purses) for it's own use. This town must contain a temple to Origenes and the family's genius, as well as a military garrison facility. The house in question must pay for the construction and upkeep of both facilities. <br /> <br /> Fifth; the sponsor Gens and prospective Gens' (patri)/(matri)archs must have a formal audience before the collected Gens heads, Archon and Origenes (if the Archon is indisposed, a Thesmothete or the Pyrtannies takes their place). There, they present their case for the inclusion of another Great House. A majority vote is taken at the end of this audience. However, if there are more than two &quot;no&quot; votes from Orgienes, the Archon and the Original Gentes, the vote is deemed failed even if a majority is otherwise reached.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T21:05:24-07:00","id":223839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=223768#post223768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) Four days, forced march. A week or so otherwise. Maybe more if the weather is against you.<br /> <br /> 2) Ordon the Nation? You could be on its borders in a day if you traveled by boat. Ordon the city? Five days or so, depending on method of transportation.<br /> <br /> 3) Ah. I wondered when this would be asked.<br /> <br /> First, one must obtain a sponsor Gens. While the law doesn't say so, after the inclusion of Gens Spyrus and the creation of the Cadet House system, it is expected that the family be a Cadet House, and the sponsor Gens is their patron.<br /> <br /> Second, the prospective Gens must be considered to have been &quot;tied into Novalesk by bonds of culture and blood&quot;. This is interpreted as of present to be that at least 75% of the House in question must have been born and raised in Novalesk, as must have their parents.<br /> <br /> Third, the prospective family must be large enough to have at least one Representative in the Boule with population alone. (So, you need to have at least 2% of the total Gentes population after you're added in. At present, that would be slightly over 2000 members).<br /> <br /> Fourth, the sponsored family must have a home town or city. It is expected that this town/city is built by the family (either by their hands or purses) for it's own use. This town must contain a temple to Origenes and the family's genius, as well as a military garrison facility. The house in question must pay for the construction and upkeep of both facilities.<br /> <br /> Fifth; the sponsor Gens and prospective Gens' (patri)/(matri)archs must have a formal audience before the collected Gens heads, Archon and Origenes (if the Archon is indisposed, a Thesmothete or the Pyrtannies takes their place). There, they present their case for the inclusion of another Great House. A majority vote is taken at the end of this audience. However, if there are more than two &quot;no&quot; votes from Orgienes, the Archon and the Original Gentes, the vote is deemed failed even if a majority is otherwise reached.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect, exactly what I was looking for.<br /> <br /> One clarification: I meant how long until the offensive is launched. Right now they are doing things like gathering new levies and making all those wards I ordered. How long is all this kind of stuff going to take?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 08-10-2014, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T14:08:20-07:00","id":236915,"title":"","content":"The primary concern will be equipping and shaking the rust off the levies. It will be at least a month before the army will be ready to march. Which is not so great, when you consider that it's more time than Esstryaan said his knights could contain the Horde, best case scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T15:47:44-07:00","id":237014,"title":"","content":"Oh good, I should have time then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T07:31:51-07:00","id":243913,"title":"","content":"Okay, guys I have been lurking here almost daily, anxiously awaiting an update. I would post, but I am in a state of waiting for a process that I am working on to complete before I move on. I'm excited about this game and where it is headed. I just want to make sure we aren't waiting on me to keep rolling. If that is the case, let me know and I will get on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T18:00:30-07:00","id":247302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=244053#post244053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless Larissa had something pressing for him to do, Yi intended to offer another lesson to his cult and then look for some form of fast travel to Ordon. Perhaps a magical hawk man of some sort.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point: Larissa and Eugene are probably your biggest supporters in Novalesk right now.<br /> Point: This is a course of action that Larissa and Eugene specifically told you to avoid. <br /> Conclusion 1: This course of action will likely alienate your closest supporters.<br /> <br /> Point: The trials are dangerous.<br /> Conclusion 2A: Yi may be severely injured or die over the course of the trials<br /> Conclusion 2B: Yi may be unable to travel for some time after the trials due to injury or other incapacitation. <br /> <br /> Point: It will take some time to reach Ordon and return.<br /> Point: It is unknown as to how long the trials will take<br /> Point: Conclusion 2B<br /> Conclusion 2: Yi will be shut out of the loop of the rest of the game for an unknowable amount of time (perhaps long enough to miss the climactic battle with the Fae<br /> <br /> Do you still want to continue with this course of action?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=246086#post246086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Here's a question: Is Cinder trying to elicit worship as 'payment' for the information he is giving out? What would I roll to figure that out?</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>He is not. Cinder is lonely. Most people ignore him or actively try to shut him up, since he's &quot;just a Need Fire&quot;, without considering what's happening to the lowly elemental for doing the work of a god. He wants someone to talk to (primary) and he wants to have the title for the work he's doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T09:02:37-07:00","id":247896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=247302#post247302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point: Larissa and Eugene are probably your biggest supporters in Novalesk right now.<br /> Point: This is a course of action that Larissa and Eugene specifically told you to avoid.<br /> Conclusion 1: This course of action will likely alienate your closest supporters.<br /> <br /> Point: The trials are dangerous.<br /> Conclusion 2A: Yi may be severely injured or die over the course of the trials<br /> Conclusion 2B: Yi may be unable to travel for some time after the trials due to injury or other incapacitation.<br /> <br /> Point: It will take some time to reach Ordon and return.<br /> Point: It is unknown as to how long the trials will take<br /> Point: Conclusion 2B<br /> Conclusion 2: Yi will be shut out of the loop of the rest of the game for an unknowable amount of time (perhaps long enough to miss the climactic battle with the Fae<br /> <br /> Do you still want to continue with this course of action?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> He is not. Cinder is lonely. Most people ignore him or actively try to shut him up, since he's &quot;just a Need Fire&quot;, without considering what's happening to the lowly elemental for doing the work of a god. He wants someone to talk to (primary) and he wants to have the title for the work he's doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do I have to invest xp in the common sense merit I just picked up? :P<br /> <br /> Sorry, I was thinking more in terms of open ended games like Skyrim where the ongoing civil war will wait for the player to clear out old mines and take over a major guild before advancing. I will not be going to Ordon. I will however need to start getting some serious charm mojo though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby"