rote her essence so she has personal and peripheral now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T17:15:35-08:00","id":300546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=300527#post300527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nice Thanks so you posted before I could post so with the exp I didn't need beacon of power anymore so I removed it and four bonus points of stuff was removed (one favored charm and conviction was reduced from 3 to 2) and I used the exp to buy a favored charms I rewrote her essence so she has personal and peripheral now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay! <br /> <br /> (Ten characters)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T08:45:44-08:00","id":301149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=300454#post300454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ordon #5</b><br /> <br /> - Ordon uses ancient technology to make its cities bigger on the inside.<br /> - The Ordon are growing rice on trees.<br /> - Ordon has discovered an apocalyptic weapon whose destructive potential is on par with the Thousand-Forged Dragons<br /> - Ordon has obtained the ability to produce Gunosha commandos</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that if anyone of these is true it will be good for us if we can get our hands on it. Though I am in favor of the gunzosha commandos, tiger warrior training technique is something I intend to get quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 11-03-2014, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T18:34:50-08:00","id":301644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=301149#post301149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that if anyone of these is true it will be good for us if we can get our hands on it. Though I am in favor of the gunzosha commandos, tiger warrior training technique is something I intend to get quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because the ability to grow cereal crops on trees is just as useful as spatial warping technosorcery, an apocalyptic death cannon from the Age of Dreams, and the ability to produce bio-mechanical super-soldiers. <br /> <br /> Yep.<br /> <br /> Okay, to be fair, it is the thing that would have the largest effect on the nation as a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T18:38:18-08:00","id":301648,"title":"","content":"<b>Theros #5</b><br /> <br /> - The Haired Beast has returned<br /> - Several northern Therian households are preparing to declare independence<br /> - An army of unknown provenance is amassing to the southeast of Theros<br /> - A cosmopolitan guild-trained thaumaturge summons demons for fun and profits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T18:56:03-08:00","id":301674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=301644#post301644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, because the ability to grow cereal crops on trees is just as useful as spatial warping technosorcery, an apocalyptic death cannon from the Age of Dreams, and the ability to produce bio-mechanical super-soldiers.<br /> <br /> Yep.<br /> <br /> Okay, to be fair, it is the thing that would have the largest effect on the nation as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the gunzosha, spatial warping magic and doom weapon is expected the tree that grow rice is not so for me it gains point for the cool factor. Being able to boost our food supplies in times of war and expansion of our soon to be nascent empire will help a lot more than the rest, who needs doom weapons when you got solars and lunars exalted on your side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T13:28:43-08:00","id":302603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=301648#post301648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Theros #5</b><br /> <br /> - The Haired Beast has returned<br /> - Several northern Therian households are preparing to declare independence<br /> - An army of unknown provenance is amassing to the southeast of Theros<br /> - A cosmopolitan guild-trained thaumaturge summons demons for fun and profits.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is the last one even a rumor? Isn't that just what guild thaumaturges do? How else are they supposed to bring about a future where their evil is law?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T15:53:55-08:00","id":302719,"title":"","content":"Yeah, well, what's a guild thaumaturge even doing in Theros?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T17:35:19-08:00","id":302780,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity, is an archon being Anathema actually illegal? Seems like Larissa would have brought it up before now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T17:47:38-08:00","id":302787,"title":"","content":"Explicitly, no.<br /> <br /> Under some interpretations of the law, yes.<br /> <br /> You must remember, that Larissa is Divine. She got a run-down of the actual history of things, including the Mandate of Heaven from ol' daddy-o. That skews her perspective on you. Holly knows more than most, but doesn't have the whole picture. Either way, what matters is the popular conception, which is that Anathema count as &quot;divine&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T07:15:55-08:00","id":303255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=300453#post300453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- A new strain of Beastmen has emerged, aiding the squirrel men in their battles with the Geherin.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the one that I believe has the best chance of being real.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=300454#post300454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Ordon uses ancient technology to make its cities bigger on the inside.<br /> - The Ordon are growing rice on trees.<br /> - Ordon has discovered an apocalyptic weapon whose destructive potential is on par with the Thousand-Forged Dragons<br /> - Ordon has obtained the ability to produce Gunosha commandos</div> </div> </div> </div>All of these are actually pretty cool. I want them all to be true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=301648#post301648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Several northern Therian households are preparing to declare independence</div> </div> </div> </div>This is wishful thinking. If they were to become independent they could be convinced more readily to ally with Novalesk. Of course, we would have to guarantee that they wouldn't be promptly annexed by Theros again...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":1146,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","user":"Belkra","date":". 11-05-2014, 10:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T07:51:49-08:00","id":303271,"title":"","content":"Posted in the IC thread. Man, Geherin seems to be wacky now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T08:04:56-08:00","id":303291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=303255#post303255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is wishful thinking. If they were to become independent they could be convinced more readily to ally with Novalesk. Of course, we would have to guarantee that they wouldn't be promptly annexed by Theros again...</div> </div> </div> </div>I certainly hope they are, or I might default on my campaign promises to my new daughter-aged mother.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, I thought this was adoption by the house rather than by a particular person. If it is by a particular person, why does it have to be Hollidane? Couldn't she just tell Origines X that I am not going to hollow out their soul and let a golden demon live there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 11-05-2014, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T10:59:31-08:00","id":303407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=303255#post303255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is wishful thinking. If they were to become independent they could be convinced more readily to ally with Novalesk. Of course, we would have to guarantee that they wouldn't be promptly annexed by Theros again...</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=303291#post303291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I certainly hope they are, or I might default on my campaign promises to my new daughter-aged mother.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe you should talk to a member of a northern Novaleski household. I mean, they might know what's what, if some of their neighbors are planning on making their own nation. Those neighbors might even have asked them for assistance, maybe even arranged a marriage between two eligible young people closely related to the house Patriarchs.<br /> <br /> It's not like you know anyone in that type of situation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=303291#post303291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come to think of it, I thought this was adoption by the house rather than by a particular person. If it is by a particular person, why does it have to be Hollidane? Couldn't she just tell Origines X that I am not going to hollow out their soul and let a golden demon live there?</div> </div> </div> </div>A particular person adopts you into their household, which makes you part of the Gens. Households can be adopted into the Gens wholesale, but that requires multiple elders to agree to it.<br /> <br /> Technically, it would make Holly somewhere in a nebulous legal zone between your &quot;Aunt&quot; and your &quot;Mother&quot;.<br /> <br /> You could get Holly to try to convince someone else to adopt you, but her saying &quot;Hey this guy is neat. He's Enlightened, and has some pretty sweet political connections. Oh, and he's an Anathema, but don't worry, he won't turn you into his puppet, he's cool.&quot; to another elder would be suspicious, since they would then consider why she isn't poaching him herself. It's possible, but would complicate things a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T11:04:04-08:00","id":303435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=303407#post303407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A particular person adopts you into their household, which makes you part of the Gens. Households can be adopted into the Gens wholesale, but that requires multiple elders to agree to it.<br /> <br /> Technically, it would make Holly somewhere in a nebulous legal zone between your &quot;Aunt&quot; and your &quot;Mother&quot;.<br /> <br /> You could get Holly to try to convince someone else to adopt you, but her saying &quot;Hey this guy is neat. He's Enlightened, and has some pretty sweet political connections. Oh, and he's an Anathema, but don't worry, he won't turn you into his puppet, he's cool.&quot; to another elder would be suspicious, since they would then consider why she isn't poaching him herself. It's possible, but would complicate things a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what your saying is, &quot;Unexpected social attack backed by excellencies vs someone who almost by definition does not have perfect mental defense charms&quot;?<br /> <br /> (That was a joke.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T11:11:51-08:00","id":303442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=303435#post303435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So what your saying is, &quot;Unexpected social attack backed by excellencies vs someone who almost by definition does not have perfect mental defense charms&quot;?<br /> <br /> (That was a joke.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That could work. <br /> <br /> Before I update for Holly in character, is that a course of action (the convincing someone else. Not the social magic. Though, knowing Yi, the convincing may very well involve social magic.) you want to pursue, or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T11:36:22-08:00","id":303502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=303407#post303407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A particular person adopts you into their household, which makes you part of the Gens. Households can be adopted into the Gens wholesale, but that requires multiple elders to agree to it.<br /> <br /> Technically, it would make Holly somewhere in a nebulous legal zone between your &quot;Aunt&quot; and your &quot;Mother&quot;.<br /> <br /> You could get Holly to try to convince someone else to adopt you, but her saying &quot;Hey this guy is neat. He's Enlightened, and has some pretty sweet political connections. Oh, and he's an Anathema, but don't worry, he won't turn you into his puppet, he's cool.&quot; to another elder would be suspicious, since they would then consider why she isn't poaching him herself. It's possible, but would complicate things a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda want to see this happen now, as I imagine Holly taking Yi by the ear, acting like a stereotypical doting mom would, packing him lunch and yelling angrily at the Boule when they dismiss his ideas. It'd be pretty funny. <br /> <br /> Did Holly even have a mother figure, or was it all Larissa and Origenon when she was adopted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T11:44:24-08:00","id":303529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=303502#post303502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did Holly even have a mother figure, or was it all Larissa and Origenon when she was adopted?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to get down to it, Larissa was as much of her mother figure as her sister, since she was in her late fourties at the time of her adoption. <br /> <br /> Though Larissa's mother passed several years before that, if that's what you're asking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T11:52:31-08:00","id":303560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=303442#post303442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That could work.<br /> <br /> Before I update for Holly in character, is that a course of action (the convincing someone else. Not the social magic. Though, knowing Yi, the convincing may very well involve social magic.) you want to pursue, or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Holly will be fine. (You would think it would occur to him to throw around a few excellencies at least when addressing the Boule instead of just trusting the system and the integrity of the members.)<br /> <br /> Edit: Does Cinder know the Ride charm? Does Larissa?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 11-05-2014, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T15:53:06-08:00","id":303813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=303560#post303560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Does Cinder know the Ride charm? Does Larissa?</div> </div> </div> </div>Respectively:<br /> <br /> Yes. Cinder is no longer the Need Fire he came into existence as; he is something more. Is he becoming more divine, or simply more powerful? Or is he becoming something else altogether?<br /> <br /> No. Most of Larissa's charms are relics of her God-blooded existence. She couldn't learn Dematerialize, and was naturally material, so powers like Ride that rely on an immaterial state were outside of her grasp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T17:55:24-08:00","id":303935,"title":"","content":"<b>Shadowlands #5</b><br /> <br /> - An ancient order of ghostly aesthetics lives in the local underworld.<br /> - The shade of Odal Thousand-Fangs has returned.<br /> - There's a dead-zone in the local underworld, where the natural geomancy devours the dragon lines.<br /> - The Crown-Prince of Theros is a member of the Black Cowl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T12:52:13-08:00","id":304920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=303935#post303935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- The Crown-Prince of Theros is a member of the Black Cowl.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the one I will bet on. I wonder if our bets have any indicator on what is true. I would suspect they don't and it is decided which rumors are true and which aren't before we even get to look at the list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T13:36:30-08:00","id":304953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=304920#post304920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is the one I will bet on. I wonder if our bets have any indicator on what is true. I would suspect they don't and it is decided which rumors are true and which aren't before we even get to look at the list.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is true in the only way that matters: &quot;Is it a reasonable excuse to use when my legions go to conquer the nation?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T12:50:27-08:00","id":306056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=304920#post304920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the one I will bet on. I wonder if our bets have any indicator on what is true. I would suspect they don't and it is decided which rumors are true and which aren't before we even get to look at the list.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct; I decide what's true and what's not while compiling the list. This is important, cause I have to look at the development of true rumors and untrue ones in an entirely different way. <br /> <br /> True rumors are actually pretty easy for me to make! Usually, this involves think up something, someone or someplace new, or coming with something new about something extant. Then I just have to phrase it right, and bam! True rumor. Since what you've seen is just the tip of the iceburg of what I've come up with brain about the nations, people, etc., This is pretty damn easy. Frankly, the hard part is making sure that the true rumors aren't things that would be common knowledge. <br /> <br /> Untrue rumors are more difficult. I have to think more about the places and ways that people interact in the setting, the constraints that established information impose on me, and the gaps in those interactions and constraints. More importantly, I have to think about how the people in the setting would view a certain place, person or thing, how they perceive it, the gaps in their knowledge, and the place it has in both their culture and their mythos. Being a Hellen-abu and having a Historian whose focus is classical Rome as a brother certainly help with this, but still, this can get pretty hard. Especially with places like Ordon, where I have to be careful about spilling, well, anything really. <br /> <br /> Though... if a rumor is untrue and it gets a lot of attention from you guys, the WAY that it's untrue may change, based on what you zeroed in on. Also, I like seeing what you zero in on. It lets me see what things you think are neat, and that lets me shape the game in ways I think you may enjoy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T12:57:14-08:00","id":306061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=304953#post304953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is true in the only way that matters: &quot;Is it a reasonable excuse to use when my legions go to conquer the nation?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would be a more relevant excuse if the King was a member of the Cult. Then you could invade with the excuse of deposing the King and placing his more pliable (but still legitimate!) brother on the throne as a puppet ruler/vassal!<br /> <br /> I literally cannot count the number of times I've done that in Crusader Kings. &quot;You're (rebelling against the empire/a heretic)! I declare war, to depose you and place your cousin, the rightful and just heir, as ruler of Phyrigia! What? No, the cousin being one of my vassals has absolutely nothing to do with it!&quot; Heh. Good times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T16:00:54-08:00","id":306997,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Squirrel Men</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The squirrel men hordes invade the lands of the Geherin, and have every year for nearly centuries. Their young flood the Eastern borders of the Vicruith forests, and the Vicruith must wage war for a season to push back the beastman masses. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The average squirrel man stands just over five feet tall at the shoulder, though it would be taller if not for their perpetual stoop. Their large bushy tail gives them superb balance, and their sharp claws both serve to aid climbing and as natural weaponry. Despite these advantages, they come at a significant price. The minds of the squirrel-men are fleeting, and they seem to lack the ability to focus on a task for much time. Also their eyes are positioned much closer to the sides of their head, much like the animal they resemble. While this gives them a larger field of vision, their depth perception is abysmal. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The squirrel men appear to have a leadership caste that serves both as thier political and spiritual leaders. The leaders seem to emit some sort of pheromone that cause the others to serve and follow them blindly. These leaders appear to have far greater mental capacity than the others. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One hundred and fifty years ago, the Vicruith decided they had had enough of these invasions. A massive warband, formed from all of the clans, fought off the initial thrust of the beastman invasion and promptly took the fight into their territory. The land they found was foul and wretched. Despite the fact that they slew more Squirrel men that year than any other, the next year's invasion was the largest in recorded history. </span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T19:37:22-08:00","id":308752,"title":"","content":"Squirrel Men confirmed for being the perfect forest skirmisher race. fast breeding, dumb enough to take suicidal orders, and also unpredictable to confound professional soldiers. Some Lunar had a laugh with these guys, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T13:06:28-08:00","id":309416,"title":"","content":"<b>Darumfel</b><br /> <br /> Though Novalesk, Theros, and Ordon are the regional powers in this age, they were not the only nations to be born from the chaos since the fall of the Shogunate. No, they were simply the only ones to survive.<br /> <br /> The loremasters of Aved raised their brass towers along the banks of the White Rock River. When threatened by Ordon, the loremasters activated a First Age machine, which caused the earth to crumble. The River filled in the sunken earth, destroying the nation utterly, and forming Lake Vera. <br /> <br /> The city of Otranto stood to the North of Theros city. The two cities engaged in warfare since their birth. In the end, Theros\u2019 Terrestrial magics proved victorious, and razed the city. Fifty years later, Theros founded the city of Tyros on that very spot. <br /> <br /> The Akertian Confederacy stood in the eastern steppes, on the border of the forestlands. Then one of their soldiers became a Solar Anathema, and forged a mighty army, invading Novalesk. The Novaleski army defeated them, and in retaliation, utterly destroyed the small confederation of townships. <br /> <br /> There were more cities, more tribes, more clans, but by the beginning of the second century post contagion, there were but four; Ordon, Theros, Novalesk, and Darumfel. <br /> <br /> Located to the south-south-east of Ordon, Darumfel was founded in the remains of a Shogunate military outpost by a group of animistic cultists. They owed their survival to the powerful spirit beckoning arts they had mastered, and to the potent sorcery wielded by their Outcaste god-king. Using their magics, they bound spirits to raise mighty walls. They bred a force of god-blooded super-soldiers, who led into battle minor spirits and semi-divine beasts, and mundane troops enhanced by divine blessings. They conquered and subjugated all in their local vicinity, and their expansion was only checked by Ordoni technosorcery in the north, and the pre-Geherin forest tribes' audacity to the south. <br /> <br /> It was in the mid-third century post contagion that the four regional powers became three. Darumfel claimed to have uncovered a Thousand-forged Dragon, which they would unleash on their enemies if they did not submit to Darumfelian Hegemony. Not knowing if the claim was a bluff, and unwilling to wager their lives on whether it was, an event that was never seen before, nor replicated since, occurred; Ordon, Theros, and Novalesk joined forces and attacked their enemy as one. <br /> <br /> Though the walls of Darumfel were mighty indeed, they could not stand against the Magical Artillery wielded by the Ordon. Though their god-blooded warriors were mighty, they could not stand against the primordial fire of Theros' Terrestrials. Though their troops were divinely empowered, that could not compare to the wonders wrought by Novalesk's mortal sorcerers. <br /> <br /> The three nations knew their alliance was simply one of convenience, and as such sought to destroy those spoils that would be most useful to the others. Therians aided Novaleskis in destroying the remains of the shogunate technical facilities to keep them from falling into Ordoni hands, while at the same time helping Ordonis destroy the reliquaries of Thaumaturgy that Novalesk desired. Soldiers of Novalesk and Ordon ensured the complete extermination of the Darumfelian royal family, to prevent Theros from gaining control over another Terrestrial bloodline. The destruction wrought by the armies was so severe that the city was utterly destroyed. Yet, so intent were they on betraying their allies, that a significant portion of the city's population survived, and became a tribe of nomads upon the Steppes. <br /> <br /> In the end, though, the true prize remained elusive; none of the allies claimed to have found the rumored Thousand Forged Dragon. While many would take this as proof that it never existed, some hold the belief that one of the allies found it, and are waiting to get it fully operational to announce the fact. Others claim that the nomadic survivors of Darumfel hold the relic. And still more believe it is in the city still, buried when Novalesk's god called down a torrent of fire and ice to utterly annihilate the city's ruins. <br /> <br /> The destruction of the city was so quick, so utterly devastating, that a ghastly replica of Darumfel appeared in the underworld. In the intervening centuries, the lords of the fallen city have built tall, nigh inviolate walls of Iron and Jade, determined that their city would never fall again. They have also turned their mastery of now-useless spirit beckoning and binding arts to the control over the dead and necrosurgery. And in their mighty towers, the dead smoulder, waiting for the day they can enact vengeance on their killers' descendants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T13:25:59-08:00","id":309423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=308752#post308752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Squirrel Men confirmed for being the perfect forest skirmisher race. fast breeding, dumb enough to take suicidal orders, and also unpredictable to confound professional soldiers. Some Lunar had a laugh with these guys, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit, that part of this comes from wanting to avoid the whole apex animals as only beastman. Also, the whole &quot;Beastmen are superior to humans&quot; because they get all of the benefits of their animal bits but have none of the downsides. Like you should be able to poison wolfmen with wine (both grapes and alcohol are toxic to canines), or catmen should be dedicated carnivores. <br /> <br /> Also, there is no evidence that a Lunar was involved in their creation or anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T13:50:03-08:00","id":309433,"title":"","content":"I like it. The only thing I wonder at is anyone actually knowing what a thousand forged dragon is, or at least knowing it by that name.<br /> <br /> Also, we are totally planning an expedition to the underword so I can examine the ghostly version of the Shogunate facility.<br /> <br /> Lets see,<br /> <br /> -Exterminate the Squirrel Men<br /> -Save Novalesk from the Fey<br /> -Trials of Ordon<br /> -Conquer Theros<br /> -Expedition to the Underworld<br /> -Nationwide Mandala/prayer machine<br /> -Successfully court Larissa<br /> -Attain the Archonship<br /> -Build the promised temples to Asclepios<br /> -Pay back the promised money and ambrosia to Origenes<br /> -Reorganize the armed forces<br /> -Make good on my various promises to the Gens<br /> -Bring about the Third Age of Transcendent Glory and Sublime Awe<br /> <br /> My to do list is getting a little long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T17:04:26-08:00","id":309590,"title":"","content":"Let's see,<br /> <br /> -Help Novalesk with the current Fae troubles<br /> -Learn how to make artifact armor<br /> -Make Shadow a veritable demigod<br /> -Perfect the art of fighting with Bastard Daiklaives<br /> -Maybe figure out what all this Dawn Caste Solar business is about<br /> -Indulge morbid (see what I did there?) curiosity of the Underworld<br /> -Complete the challenges of Helios' siblings<br /> <br /> Not quite as long, but I think it will get there eventually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T19:44:33-08:00","id":309764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=309433#post309433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it. The only thing I wonder at is anyone actually knowing what a thousand forged dragon is, or at least knowing it by that name.<br /> <br /> Also, we are totally planning an expedition to the underword so I can examine the ghostly version of the Shogunate facility.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Thousand Forged Dragons were a rather important Shogunate era superweapon....<br /> <br /> Long story short, they probably don't know what it's called, but they have a pretty decent grasp of its capabilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=309590#post309590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's see,<br /> <br /> -Help Novalesk with the current Fae troubles<br /> -Learn how to make artifact armor<br /> -Make Shadow a veritable demigod<br /> -Perfect the art of fighting with Bastard Daiklaives<br /> -Maybe figure out what all this Dawn Caste Solar business is about<br /> -Indulge morbid (see what I did there?) curiosity of the Underworld<br /> -Complete the challenges of Helios' siblings<br /> <br /> Not quite as long, but I think it will get there eventually.</div> </div> </div> </div>No &quot;Help my bestest buddy Cinder move up in the world&quot;? For shame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","user":"Noodle","date":". 11-11-2014, 11:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T19:48:09-08:00","id":309768,"title":"","content":"Also, I find it rather odd that everyone seems to take it in stride that Origenes has magic that can, according to these reports, WIPE ENTIRE CITIES OFF THE MAP?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T20:17:25-08:00","id":309805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=309768#post309768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I find it rather odd that everyone seems to take it in stride that Origenes has magic that can, according to these reports, WIPE ENTIRE CITIES OFF THE MAP?</div> </div> </div> </div>I just assumed he called in several major favors with the bureau of nature and got some martial weather. Also, I haven't thought of a polite way to bring it up in conversation with him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T20:17:33-08:00","id":309806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a hre