se the meaning is approximately the same, so... Yeah.<br /> <br /> Remember, there's no SH or V in Old Realm!<br /> <br /> Also, I do get into a bit of an engrishy mindset when writing Old Realm. Context clues may be important to an accurate translation!</div> </div> </div> </div>Scion then? I had considered that but was expecting some sort of C. Curse you french spelling of germanic words due to a desire by English scribes to appear cultured to their Norman overlords!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 11-15-2014, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T07:59:12-08:00","id":312960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=312808#post312808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Scion then? I had considered that but was expecting some sort of C. Curse you french spelling of germanic words due to a desire by English scribes to appear cultured to their Norman overlords!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep! Everything is phonetic (kinda) to keep the number of characters to a minimum. <br /> <br /> As a speaker of both English and German, I feel your pain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T09:16:15-08:00","id":312980,"title":"","content":"That's neat stuff. I was able to find a High Realm translation tool, but nothing for Old Realm. What are you guys using to translate this stuff? I'm a closet language nut and constructed languages fascinate me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":1146,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","user":"Belkra","date":".  Proper punctuation is a writer's friend. 11-15-2014, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T09:44:46-08:00","id":312985,"title":"","content":"Old Realm script is in the Apendix of one of the Dreams of the First Age books. The syllabic system is the same as High Realm (assuming I remember High Realm correctly) so now that Exthalion's transcribed it, you should be able to help with the Translation.<br /> <br /> Edit: yep, the syllabic transliteration between English and Old Realm is the same as between English and High Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T12:16:34-08:00","id":313185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=311803#post311803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lay them on me! I'm always open to questions and suggestions about the game!</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Thanks ok so I'll begin with the basic things I want to know.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Can a dragon-blooded raise it's breeding background in game ?</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">How many people can you train at the same time using tiger training technique ?</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Is there an equivalent in war to the lore charm terrestrial edification program ?</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">What are the limits of what a terrestrial martial art can do ? </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T13:13:02-08:00","id":313216,"title":"","content":"In order:<br /> <br /> (1) Yes! A terrestrial can increase their Breeding! In canon, there is only one way to do this: the Presence Charm &quot;Purity Crucible Strike&quot; from Dreams of the First Age: Lords of Creation.<br /> <br /> It allows a Breeding 5 BD (or Eclipse) who learns it to burn away impurities in a Terrestrial's blood, increasing their Breeding. Failure on the roll (an Essence + Breeding Roll at a difficult of targets Breeding +1) results in Death, though. It can be learned by DBs with less than 5 Breeding, but they can only use it on themselves until they reach Breeding 5. Also, it requires Essence 6, Presence 6, and a significant investment into the Presence Charm tree, so there's that. <br /> <br /> Outside of canon, there could be other ways. Pacts with the Yozis to burn away impurities, blessings from the Elemental Dragons, bathing in the Blood of an appropriately aspected Greater Elemental Dragon, meditating for a season in the untamed energies of the appropriate Elemental Pole, using only your Exalted Essence as protection. They should be equally difficult and pose equal risk as the charm. <br /> <br /> (2) It gives no limit in Core or Errata, save that it must be a single military unit. So the question would be, how big of a military unit can you get?<br /> <br /> (3) Not in canon, but I suppose there could be? Maybe teaching TMA charms instead of Sorcery and Thaumaturgy?<br /> <br /> (4) If you have access to the Scroll of the Monk, I would suggest reading the opening to the TMA chapter. It goes into this far better than I can. But to sum up: TMAs are direct, and enhance naturally occurring human martial skills. They are simple and Direct. They rarely touch upon more esoteric or immaterial concepts, and if so, only at the capstone, and even then, in how those esoteric effects touch the real world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T13:56:59-08:00","id":313281,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the quick response.<br /> <br /> 1. Oh nice so it can be done we need more dragon-blooded, I had this idea of using powerful elemental manses with custom powers, as a base for the purification process and it could require rare elemental exotic ingredient to purify their blood with elemental essence. Of course this form of purification is expensive and dangerous but can be reproduced multiple times.<br /> <br /> 2. Well this makes things simpler.<br /> <br /> 3. I was thinking about something like that.<br /> <br /> 4. I have this idea for a TMA that is made for enlighten mortals. If an enlighten mortal learns this style in it's entirety they become Elemental God blooded but maybe it doesn't fit into a TMA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T16:20:18-08:00","id":313354,"title":"","content":"(1) The closest I'm likely to allow with manses helping in this regard is the Dragon's Nest canon manse power. Also, you'd need to get enough breeding stock to start a Terrestrial Line, and I'm curious as to how you're going to go about that. <br /> <br /> (2) Yep!<br /> <br /> (3) Hm. Yes. Some more tinkering may be required.<br /> <br /> (4) What purpose would there be to make an Enlightened Mortal into an Elemental-Blood? If you run with the implications of the Enlightened Essence Mutation in Compass: Wyld, they can already learn selected spirit charms, and they can already apotheosis into gods. <br /> <br /> That said, it is possible for that, I guess? It would depend on the thematic elements of the rest of the style, I think. <br /> <br /> If you want to mass-produce divinely-empowered mortals, sorcery, Wyld magic or demesne mutation may be easier ways to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T16:53:46-08:00","id":313360,"title":"","content":"1. That may be the hard part though I am sure some dragon blooded would happy to start is own house or lineage we just need to find them. <br /> <br /> 3. Can It still enlighten mortals ?<br /> <br /> 4. There are multiple reasons for that it could all be done with training charms and I think it could be a great boost for our reputation with the population and we obtain powerful followers at a cheap cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 11-15-2014, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T18:18:49-08:00","id":313380,"title":"","content":"Terrestrial edification program doesn't enlighten mortals, it just increases their essence score. If that's what you want, you need Soul Enlightening Benefice, which goes off of Essence Lending Method.<br /> <br /> Ah. Training Charm abuse. Let's keep that at Tiger Warrior Training for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T18:39:58-08:00","id":313401,"title":"","content":"I guess it is... Well tiger warriors are still incredibly good soldiers. Still when I see things like the legions of silence of the realm and the gunzosha commandos of lookshy I'm a bit envious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 11-15-2014, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T18:13:30-08:00","id":314978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=313401#post313401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess it is... Well tiger warriors are still incredibly good soldiers. Still when I see things like the legions of silence of the realm and the gunzosha commandos of lookshy I'm a bit envious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude. I'm all for you using your powers to their maximum. And look at it this way; Gunzosha and Silent Legionnaires are pretty powerful, but with her current stats, Amelia could create an army of Dex 5, Melee 5, War 4 soldiers. That's nothing to sneeze at!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T05:23:17-08:00","id":315285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=314978#post314978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dude. I'm all for you using your powers to their maximum. And look at it this way; Gunzosha and Silent Legionnaires are pretty powerful, but with her current stats, Amelia could create an army of Dex 5, Melee 5, War 4 soldiers. That's nothing to sneeze at!</div> </div> </div> </div>So very true, sometimes I forget that having an ability at 5 means your one of the best in the world since in exalted it's easy to have multiple stats at 5 early in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T17:14:26-08:00","id":315774,"title":"","content":"Exthalion- Not trying to squarsh your crafting abitions, but i would say such an Artifact would be rating four or five at least, well beyond the capacity of anyone in Novalesk right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T17:36:31-08:00","id":315785,"title":"","content":"Are the chieftains trying to send us a quest before we leave for Novalesk ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T17:43:31-08:00","id":315788,"title":"","content":"They're trying to tell you it may be an effective way to spend the time between now and when the Warband gathers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T18:31:57-08:00","id":315805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=315774#post315774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exthalion- Not trying to squarsh your crafting abitions, but i would say such an Artifact would be rating four or five at least, well beyond the capacity of anyone in Novalesk right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should see my plans for a spike of starmetal and the golden blood of a Zenith that trumps heavenly procedure regarding prayer delivery so all my requests go straight to the Unconquered Sun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That said, the evil artifact from the demon sounds like a fun quest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 11-18-2014, 10:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T18:42:13-08:00","id":315817,"title":"","content":"Who said anything about this artifact being evil? Or held by a demon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T19:54:09-08:00","id":315839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=315817#post315817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who said anything about this artifact being evil? Or held by a demon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Red sand and the chancellor wont let him mention some place. Its either politics or some sort of demonic temptation going on. (I am jumping on it either way)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T21:58:47-08:00","id":315915,"title":"","content":"The place has nothing to do with the artifact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T07:49:44-08:00","id":316279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=315839#post315839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Red sand and the chancellor wont let him mention some place. Its either politics or some sort of demonic temptation going on. (I am jumping on it either way)</div> </div> </div> </div>You should probably latch onto the Marble, too. That's important too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T09:02:06-08:00","id":316329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=316279#post316279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You should probably latch onto the Marble, too. That's important too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely! And don't forget its an altar, that's the most important piece of evidence of all!<br /> <br /> <br /> So are we really saying this isn't a chance to sell my soul to a heretical priest of Cecelyn who believes she and Adorjan were once one, and that the silent wind is the evaporated sea which once covered the ancient ocean bed that became Cecelyn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T09:04:51-08:00","id":316332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=316329#post316329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Definitely! And don't forget its an altar, that's the most important piece of evidence of all!<br /> <br /> <br /> So are we really saying this isn't a chance to sell my soul to a heretical priest of Cecelyn who believes she and Adorjan were once one, and that the silent wind is the evaporated sea which once covered the ancient ocean bed that became Cecelyn?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my headcanon now. Ancient Tethys is/was a Titan. Cool stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T09:44:07-08:00","id":316367,"title":"","content":"Wow...You guys do lose me sometimes. All this stuff sounds pretty cool, though. Tethys? Titan? What the howl? Is a Titan like a Behemoth? I have an idea what a Behemoth is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T09:50:49-08:00","id":316377,"title":"","content":"Titan, like the mythological forbears of the gods in classic myth. It's shorthand for Primordial/Yozi, since the Primordials are essentially the Titans, being cosmic over gods who are simultaneously people and entire worlds as well as the fallen makers of the world/the gods.<br /> <br /> What Dietaku is saying is that Tethys, an archaic Hellenic ocean Titan considered to be the mother of all rivers and the embodiment of all the world's waters, is a Primordial/Yozi in Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","user":"Noodle","date":". 11-19-2014, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T16:17:06-08:00","id":316607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=316329#post316329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So are we really saying this isn't a chance to sell my soul to a heretical priest of Cecelyn who believes she and Adorjan were once one, and that the silent wind is the evaporated sea which once covered the ancient ocean bed that became Cecelyn?</div> </div> </div> </div>While that is possible (I guess?) this certainly isn't it. According to Cecelyne's law, Hadad is a non-entity at best, and a terrible traitorous terrorist at worst.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T17:54:41-08:00","id":316734,"title":"","content":"So there are 2nd circle demons loose in Novalesk now ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T18:16:23-08:00","id":316787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=316734#post316734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there are 2nd circle demons loose in Novalesk now ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of? Hadad is the only one, and his circumstances are ... unique. You'll see as time goes on in the IC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T19:32:20-08:00","id":316875,"title":"","content":"So how's the Old Realm translation going? Keeping on trucking, or do you want me to tell you what it means?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T20:51:27-08:00","id":316902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=316787#post316787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kind of? Hadad is the only one, and his circumstances are ... unique. You'll see as time goes on in the IC.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a Sidereal greater astrology charm that turns demons into gods, and Luna has a servant who was once one. Also, it is speculated that the hidden judges of the secret flame were once priests of Cecelyne.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T21:21:34-08:00","id":316920,"title":"","content":"I know about Granalkin and &quot;An End To Darkness&quot; and the Hidden Judges. They're all pretty cool!<br /> <br /> I meant unique in terms of things you're likely to see. They're hardly unique on the cosmic scale!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T22:25:34-08:00","id":316949,"title":"","content":"I see now. Thanks for the explanation. I know about Primordials, in a vague sense and what I was able to gather from the Infernals hardcover.<br /> <br /> The Old Realm translation hasn't even been attempted. I would like some time to try it and maybe see if I could get it taken care of. I haven't accessed the computer with the correct files on it in a few days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T10:45:38-08:00","id":317552,"title":"","content":"The Titans/Primordials are a pretty neat aspect of the setting that lends itself well to all sorts of weird and wonderful ideas. Sadly, I seem to be in the minority in that I'd like to hear more about them, or at least the regulars here are just bitter and opinionated, whichever. Anyways, I found the Ink Monkeys' articles <i>On the Legends of the Titans</i> and <i>On Titans Less Spoken Of</i> to be helpful. That, and <i>Compass: Malfeas</i>. All good reads.They're more or less why any and all of our games get derailed whenever we get into Malfeas. The place is a huge hodgepodge of powerful beings and cool technology, all without the baggage of the Immaculate Dogma or the Bronze Faction's machinations to cock it all up. Of course, most beings wish you dead, but that's half the fun, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T16:12:26-08:00","id":317750,"title":"","content":"I have to admit that I am not that excited about Malfeas and all that comes from there. Behemoths I am somewhat excited about, but I am more excited about things like Juggernaut and the threat that guy represents. You see when it comes to Fantasy tropes I get really excited about paladin-type characters and the types of enemies they are most often seen facing or made to be really good against are undead. My wife can most likely tell you when I am playing a paladin in a game and I am fighting through a horde of skeletons. I am laughing maniacally.<br /> <br /> By extension I find myself having my second favorite type of character to play is a necromancer. The funny thing is that I generally don't like to play a necromancer whose abilities are tied inextricably to an animated servant. I like to be able to siphon life energy and use it for various purposes, or to level death itself in it's various forms at my opponents.<br /> <br /> All that to explain why I really get excited about all things Underworld when it comes to Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T16:31:08-08:00","id":317767,"title":"","content":"Ah man Yi gets to go to Malfeas some people get all the fun, seriously though it's on Amelia's list of place to conquer after she's done with heaven. <br /> <br /> Thanks for tips on Yozi\\Primordisl Dieyaku this will be useful for a game I'm prepping though I might have seen a bit too big for this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 11-20-2014, 07:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T16:37:54-08:00","id":317769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=317767#post317767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah man Yi gets to go to Malfeas some people get all the fun, seriously though it's on Amelia's list of place to conquer after she's done with heaven.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will endeavor to make your sojourn through the Wyld as engaging and awesome as a quest to Malfeas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T16:44:16-08:00","id":317772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=317750#post317750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to admit that I am not that excited about Malfeas and all that comes from there. Behemoths I am somewhat excited about, but I am more excited about things like Juggernaut and the threat that guy represents. You see when it comes to Fantasy tropes I get really excited about paladin-type characters and the types of enemies they are most often seen facing or made to be really good against are undead. My wife can most likely tell you when I am playing a paladin in a game and I am fighting through a horde of skeletons. I am laughing maniacally.<br /> <br /> By extension I find myself having my second favorite type of character to play is a necromancer. The funny thing is that I generally don't like to play a necromancer whose abilities are tied inextricably to an animated servant. I like to be able to siphon life energy and use it for various purposes, or to level death itself in it's various forms at my opponents.<br /> <br /> All that to explain why I really get excited about all things Underworld when it comes to Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see. It's cool. Different strokes and all that. Your excitement for being a holy warrior is one shared by my best friend, so I can totally see where you're coming from. <br /> <br /> As for being a necromancer, I'm pretty sure Exalted has your back in that, too. While I don't have White and Black Treatises on hand at the moment or as memorized as I'm sure others do, the ability to level Oblivion itself as a tool seems like a pretty great ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T17:05:25-08:00","id":317804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=317767#post317767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah man Yi gets to go to Malfeas some people get all the fun, seriously though it's on Amelia's list of place to conquer after she's done with heaven.<br /> <br /> Thanks for tips on Yozi\\Primordisl Dieyaku this will be useful for a game I'm prepping though I might have seen a bit too big for this one.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does delay my attaining the archonship though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Ext