tar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T19:53:18-08:00","id":377741,"title":"","content":"Does anybody know if there are celestial martial art that use swords and are compatible with armor ? I think it would be a good addition to Amelia's swordsmanship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T11:09:19-08:00","id":378221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=374493#post374493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they do resist, are they aware of &quot;Evil anathema mind control&quot;? Or is it just, &quot;Wow, that dirge almost mad me cry.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't know that it's magic unless you're using an obvious Charm. Given the fact that you're not hiding your nature, they may suspect magic is involved. But then again, they may suspect you're using magic even when you're not, so there's that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T11:10:23-08:00","id":378222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=377533#post377533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question, then, is what is the weapon stats for a thrown human body? Are we using Crack the Sky's stats for them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just roll (Strength + Athletics).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T11:15:55-08:00","id":378223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=377741#post377741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anybody know if there are celestial martial art that use swords and are compatible with armor ? I think it would be a good addition to Amelia's swordsmanship.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Eye of Heaven is compatible with Orichalcum Reaver Daiklaives. Otherwise, the only sword-based Celestial Style is Violet Bier of Sorrows, which isn't compatible. That doesn't prevent us from making one mind!<br /> <br /> The only issue I would have is that Amelia uses Glorious Solar Saber, which is a melee charm, as I understand it, that means It has to be used with the Melee ability, which would prevent usage of MA charms with it. At least RAW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T11:18:55-08:00","id":378231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=375893#post375893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This seems like the best solution though and here is Amelia roll for the distance to the bridge <a href=\"http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4754118/\" target=\"_blank\">4 sux</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's around eighty yards away, assuming your sense of perception is not being warped by the Wyld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T14:03:05-08:00","id":378371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=378223#post378223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Eye of Heaven is compatible with Orichalcum Reaver Daiklaives. Otherwise, the only sword-based Celestial Style is Violet Bier of Sorrows, which isn't compatible. That doesn't prevent us from making one mind!<br /> <br /> The only issue I would have is that Amelia uses Glorious Solar Saber, which is a melee charm, as I understand it, that means It has to be used with the Melee ability, which would prevent usage of MA charms with it. At least RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>This could be fun though what maybe someting along the line of a holy swordmaster style or the like, used to fight against creatures of darkness with high essence score. <br /> <br /> Hmm... That is true are their ways to go around that ? Like adding the martial keyword from the ink monkeys that would allow it's use with martial arts as it would count as both a melee charmand a martial art charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T15:30:53-08:00","id":378429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=378223#post378223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Eye of Heaven is compatible with Orichalcum Reaver Daiklaives. Otherwise, the only sword-based Celestial Style is Violet Bier of Sorrows, which isn't compatible. That doesn't prevent us from making one mind!<br /> <br /> The only issue I would have is that Amelia uses Glorious Solar Saber, which is a melee charm, as I understand it, that means It has to be used with the Melee ability, which would prevent usage of MA charms with it. At least RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was any Orichalcum blade? Although, what<i> I</i> really want is an iaijutsu-type quick draw sword style, which Shining Point in the Void has covered for Ex3. Sadly, there's nothing like that in MA, although both Sidereal and Solar melee have similar things, while Abyssal melee gives one a schwingy anime dash attack, too.<br /> <br /> I guess I shouldn't complain, though, considering how good swording is in general in Exalted, compared to, say, Thrown or Martial Arts itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T15:47:50-08:00","id":378437,"title":"","content":"There is a TMA that keys of the destiny background and lets you forge your own artifacts that is compatible with swords and armor.<br /> <br /> Edit: It is called path of the arbiter, you get to pick the form weapon when you learn a certain charm, it is compatible with armor that costs less than your MA rating (Artifacts are rating +3), and celestial exalts can't have the destiny background.<br /> <br /> Speaking of artifact costs, MoEP: DB has this to say <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Typically, non-military and minor artifacts have a value in Resources dots equal to their Artifact rating +1. This can<br /> include minor weapons and armor (daggers, bracers, light armor and the like), but typically, military artifacts and those with serious agricultural, industrial or construction applications are valued at the wonder\u2019s Artifact rating +2. Truly impressive and singular artifacts\u2014warstriders, First Age field artillery and other major artifacts\u2014can be rated as high as Artifact +3 (effectively placing most of them beyond the means of any single individual), but they are only very rarely on the market in the first place. </div> </div> </div>So probably rating + 2 for most moonsilver armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 01-22-2015, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T16:01:29-08:00","id":378441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=378429#post378429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought it was any Orichalcum blade? Although, what<i> I</i> really want is an iaijutsu-type quick draw sword style, which Shining Point in the Void has covered for Ex3. Sadly, there's nothing like that in MA, although both Sidereal and Solar melee have similar things, while Abyssal melee gives one a schwingy anime dash attack, too.<br /> <br /> I guess I shouldn't complain, though, considering how good swording is in general in Exalted, compared to, say, Thrown or Martial Arts itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true but I think a combination of martial arts and melee could be a great advantage in combat all thing considered but it seems that not a lot of martial art are compatible with armor which is a shame.<br /> <br /> I had considered learning the Eye of heaven style but it's a rare style in the age of sorrows. Still Exthalion's martial art that let you make artifact sounds interesting all thing considered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T15:42:03-08:00","id":379573,"title":"","content":"Hold it, Exthalion. Does that mean you have to have the Destiny background to take that TMA? If so, Amelia wouldn't be able to take that one. It also sounds interesting to me, but as I am gearing up to do crafting the hard way already, I might pass. I really only have MA so I can wreck fools if I somehow find myself unable to do the swording.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T15:50:29-08:00","id":379579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=379573#post379573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hold it, Exthalion. Does that mean you have to have the Destiny background to take that TMA? If so, Amelia wouldn't be able to take that one. It also sounds interesting to me, but as I am gearing up to do crafting the hard way already, I might pass. I really only have MA so I can wreck fools if I somehow find myself unable to do the swording.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the destiny background just makes it work better. I reread it, and you get an artifact and weapon of a rating equal to 1/2 of a particular virtue. You can add your destiny to one and only one of them for the purpose of the calculation. You can also get a second familiar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T10:05:18-08:00","id":380254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=379579#post379579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, the destiny background just makes it work better. I reread it, and you get an artifact and weapon of a rating equal to 1/2 of a particular virtue. You can add your destiny to one and only one of them for the purpose of the calculation. You can also get a second familiar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Second familiar? You mean, I could have TWO Shadows? Holy freakin' howl!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T13:44:50-08:00","id":382246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=380254#post380254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Second familiar? You mean, I could have TWO Shadows? Holy freakin' howl!</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on how the ST runs with it, you could not only have several familiars, but also behemoth familiars or even minor gods or demons as familiars, too. Of course, I've been limited in my circle to having one familiar for exactly that reason. &quot;Not letting you play Pokemon,&quot; my ass, Noodle. <br /> <br /> Now, when's our next game day?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T14:00:36-08:00","id":382292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=382246#post382246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depending on how the ST runs with it, you could not only have several familiars, but also behemoth familiars or even minor gods or demons as familiars, too. Of course, I've been limited in my circle to having one familiar for exactly that reason. &quot;Not letting you play Pokemon,&quot; my ass, Noodle.<br /> <br /> Now, when's our next game day?</div> </div> </div> </div>A: We have game days?<br /> <br /> B: You have to be a steampunk robot exalted to get minor gods as familiars. No one else is cool enough to have their own Cortana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T14:54:08-08:00","id":382340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=382292#post382292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A: We have game days?<br /> <br /> B: You have to be a steampunk robot exalted to get minor gods as familiars. No one else is cool enough to have their own Cortana.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first point is me being facetious, asking Noodle a question over an internet forum I could ask him right now, as he's currently less than ten feet away from me. <br /> <br /> It might've just been our group, but Noodle's predilection towards Sidereals more or less cemented for me that Siddies can have god BFFs, too. That the Ride tree lets you do this freely, too, makes it all the easier to imagine, too, although I suppose by RAW, you are correct, Exthalion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T15:26:38-08:00","id":382377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=382246#post382246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;Not letting you play Pokemon,&quot; my ass, Noodle.</div> </div> </div> </div>We did it once. It got like, hella crazy with all of them in EACH AND EVERY COMBAT OHMYGAWD. Granted it was super awesome, but things really difficult for me to keep track of. Remember how I kept forgetting Archer was present? Yeah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=382246#post382246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Now, when's our next game day?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tomorrow, remember? We went over this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","user":"Noodle","date":". 01-26-2015, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T15:29:14-08:00","id":382379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=382292#post382292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A: We have game days?<br /> <br /> B: You have to be a steampunk robot exalted to get minor gods as familiars. No one else is cool enough to have their own Cortana.</div> </div> </div> </div>A: Yeah, man. Didn't you get the memo? I'm pretty sure it was in the packet.<br /> <br /> B: Sidereals have an entire charm tree for that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T15:30:51-08:00","id":382381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=382340#post382340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first point is me being facetious, asking Noodle a question over an internet forum I could ask him right now, as he's currently less than ten feet away from me.<br /> <br /> It might've just been our group, but Noodle's predilection towards Sidereals more or less cemented for me that Siddies can have god BFFs, too. That the Ride tree lets you do this freely, too, makes it all the easier to imagine, too, although I suppose by RAW, you are correct, Exthalion.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is an actual written rule that Alchemicals are the coolest exalt type? Yay!<br /> <br /> Other familiars are cool, and I think you just need to get your graces forged to get your own Behemoth. (Though apparently you are supposed to let your lackeys attune it)<br /> <br /> Lets go on a metaphysical romp of transitioning into different splats to gain their familiars in our bid to collect them all! Who wants to have their exaltation warped by the Yozi first?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T15:31:06-08:00","id":382382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=380254#post380254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Second familiar? You mean, I could have TWO Shadows? Holy freakin' howl!</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall one brand of exalted (Alchemicals I think?) putting a cap of (Essence) on one's familiars. I tend to just run with that for all exalts. <br /> <br /> Anyway, that charm group would not only allow you to have two Shadows, but one of them would be the Shadow of your Soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T15:33:45-08:00","id":382386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=382381#post382381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is an actual written rule that Alchemicals are the coolest exalt type? Yay!</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Sidereals are the coolest type. Even the Core agrees!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T15:39:56-08:00","id":382390,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> What he's referring to is the Core of Autochthon, not the core rulebook. It's an in-joke in our game that the Core is this incredibly intelligent, but low common sense Deva who likes to screw with Creation through his Sorcerous Admin privileges that being Auto-kun's fetich grants him. This not only runs with us thinking the Viator is the cast-off remmnants of a truly terrifying former Deva, but also that the Core may be assisting Sidereals even now, because &quot;Vizier am Kung Fu Warrior. He am greetest.&quot;<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T18:35:55-08:00","id":382560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=382381#post382381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is an actual written rule that Alchemicals are the coolest exalt type? Yay!<br /> <br /> Other familiars are cool, and I think you just need to get your graces forged to get your own Behemoth. (Though apparently you are supposed to let your lackeys attune it)<br /> <br /> Lets go on a metaphysical romp of transitioning into different splats to gain their familiars in our bid to collect them all! Who wants to have their exaltation warped by the Yozi first?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was halfway considering going through the process of being Abyssalfied and then gaining redemption. (Cecil Harvey is one of my all time favorite dudes) However, I believe that is beyond the scope of this game anyway. I mean, redemption like that would take a significant effort on the part of the Abyssal. I feel that it would overshadow much of what would be going on with the other players and I want to star beside them not in front of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T20:02:27-08:00","id":382652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=382560#post382560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was halfway considering going through the process of being Abyssalfied and then gaining redemption. (Cecil Harvey is one of my all time favorite dudes) However, I believe that is beyond the scope of this game anyway. I mean, redemption like that would take a significant effort on the part of the Abyssal. I feel that it would overshadow much of what would be going on with the other players and I want to star beside them not in front of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, you just nick your Monstrance and have me reforge it into a grand daiklaive that can exalt the poor, mortal, shmuck who picks it up after your demise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T09:40:48-08:00","id":384290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=382560#post382560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was halfway considering going through the process of being Abyssalfied and then gaining redemption. (Cecil Harvey is one of my all time favorite dudes) However, I believe that is beyond the scope of this game anyway. I mean, redemption like that would take a significant effort on the part of the Abyssal. I feel that it would overshadow much of what would be going on with the other players and I want to star beside them not in front of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should ask Noodle for his Dark Knight Evil Wave charm he made, whereby the Abyssal launches a chunk of his soul, propelled by hate, at his foe. <br /> <br /> Also, you have some good taste, Cecil is a pretty good FF hero, although my personal favorite is Bartz. Carefree but hotblooded heroes who go for the crazy thing when the chips are down? That's some good stuff right there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T21:44:45-08:00","id":385830,"title":"","content":"Cecil Harvey is the type of hero that is in short supply in games these days. If you find a character like him, he (or she) is usually relegated to being one of the supporting cast. It's a darn shame really. I don't know how many more apathetic, immature jacktards I can put up with. I really didn't get into Bartz that much. It might be because I was doing a two-man playthrough on the PSOne remake and I wasn't focusing on the story too much. I was too busy worrying about how I was going to trick out my characters and what abilities I would learn next.<br /> <br /> As far as nicking the Monstrance goes, I'm not that tricky. Besides I was only halfway convinced that Abyssalfication was a good way to go. I would have to be fully convinced. I think what it would take for me to be fully convinced would be for me to be darn near guaranteed that I could return to being a Dawn.<br /> <br /> All that said, who is up for nicking monstrances anyway and trying to redeem the exaltations they have corrupted? Then we go after that wretched creature that houses the Infernal exaltations when they aren't hanging out with the Infernals.<br /> <br /> I don't know, I just have this image of a dude, unarmed and unarmored taking out Juggernaut...with a single hit. OP? Yep. Fun as anything? You bet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T15:00:08-08:00","id":394151,"title":"","content":"I highly suggest doing a normal run of FFV. It's definately my favorite mainline Final Fantasy game, and one of the main reasons for that is Bartz. While I'm apathetic to Cecil myself, I do agree that he's way better than the post-6 FF protags... Which is why I took those guys, blended them together, and chucked the result at you. I'm glad that he's had the intended result. <br /> <br /> I'm ready to facilitate an Abyssalification arc, though it would force me to move around some timetables. That's not the kind of thing I would ever force upon a player without a clear and decise YES as it being the direction you want to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T15:52:48-08:00","id":394185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=389229#post389229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something clicks for Jensven. Vellus was attempting to gain some measure of power through the current exchange. He had seen it back home when rival chieftans would visit and attempt to gain the services of some of the reavers by commending them and then subtly suggesting they should come over to their service.</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone's projecting, me thinks. Can't an honest and truthful guy do something nice without suspicion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T18:31:41-08:00","id":394337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=394185#post394185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Someone's projecting, me thinks. Can't an honest and truthful guy do something nice without suspicion?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Yes they can but we need to be careful about who we trust after all we still have the title of anathema over our head... for now at least.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T15:42:36-08:00","id":395520,"title":"","content":"Teamwork: is there anything it CAN'T make better?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T18:57:11-08:00","id":395750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=394151#post394151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I highly suggest doing a normal run of FFV. It's definately my favorite mainline Final Fantasy game, and one of the main reasons for that is Bartz. While I'm apathetic to Cecil myself, I do agree that he's way better than the post-6 FF protags... Which is why I took those guys, blended them together, and chucked the result at you. I'm glad that he's had the intended result.<br /> <br /> I'm ready to facilitate an Abyssalification arc, though it would force me to move around some timetables. That's not the kind of thing I would ever force upon a player without a clear and decise YES as it being the direction you want to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since I am about the biggest Paladin fanboy I know I can put up with Cecil being the way he is. I didn't get to play V (what little bit of it I did normally with a translated rom) until years later. One would have to keep in mind that I encountered FFIV at a time where I was looking for direction in my life. It (and therefore Cecil) made a definite impact on who I was and who I would become. Howl, recently I played through part of After Years and it was a kick of nostalgia right to my feels. Yeah, Cecil can be whiny sometimes. I think he is the freakin' man anyway.<br /> <br /> FFV was the end of an era. It was the last of the old school. You then had the transition period of VI and VII. Then there is the new school of everything after. Check the articles following this link for what I am talking about <a href=\"http://www.hardcoregaming101.net/finalfantasy/ff1/ff1-1.htm\" target=\"_blank\">here.</a><br /> <br /> I will have to think long and hard on whether I want to go that route. I know you are alright with me going Abyssal, but for me the real draw of being Abyssal would be the shot at Redemption. Are you willing to have me pull a Siegfried Schtauffen and go Nightmare and back?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=394185#post394185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Someone's projecting, me thinks. Can't an honest and truthful guy do something nice without suspicion?</div> </div> </div> </div>He reminds me, the player, of a freakin' serpent. Jensven is slightly lupine. He would catch onto that too. Not saying you can't ever trust such a person, but he needs to be won over at this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T22:04:37-08:00","id":395836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=395750#post395750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will have to think long and hard on whether I want to go that route. I know you are alright with me going Abyssal, but for me the real draw of being Abyssal would be the shot at Redemption. Are you willing to have me pull a Siegfried Schtauffen and go Nightmare and back?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be down, but I have tow primary concerns. One, how it would effect the group dynamic as a whole (though with the PCs basically doing their own things at this point, there's not much of a dynamic to speak of), and two, whether or not I'm a good enough ST to do an Abyssal redemption arc justice. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=395750#post395750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He reminds me, the player, of a freakin' serpent. Jensven is slightly lupine. He would catch onto that too. Not saying you can't ever trust such a person, but he needs to be won over at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's a serpent, then? Hm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle's Big Book o' Writeups</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Nikoloi Mari Vellus</b><br /> Motivation: Set an example for my nation as a just and honest man.<br /> Virtues: Compassion 3, Conviction 3, Temperance 4, Valor 2<br /> Relevant Intimacies: Novalesk (Patriotic Pride), Honesty (The Best Policy), Gens Nikoloi (Filial Duty)<br /> Relevant Abilities: Bureaucracy 3 (+2 Equitable Trades), Integrity 5 (+3 Being Honesty), Presence 3, Socialize 3<br /> Willpower 10<br /> Essence 2<br /> Charms<br /> Excellencies: First Presence, First Integrity, Second Bureaucracy<br /> Stoke The Flame- Limited to producing desire for Justice</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T09:13:39-08:00","id":397652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=395836#post395836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd be down, but I have tow primary concerns. One, how it would effect the group dynamic as a whole (though with the PCs basically doing their own things at this point, there's not much of a dynamic to speak of), and two, whether or not I'm a good enough ST to do an Abyssal redemption arc justice.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> He's a serpent, then? Hm.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Bah don't worry about it Noodle you are doing a very nice job as an ST (I also like Dietaku's style but no more gunstar game... sigh... so sad...) more than all of my IRL ST combined (I was lucky if we had one quest planned in advance) so for me this is paradise, I would not have problems with such an arc though I'm more of a fan of demonic damnation but I don't think you can come back from this one. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Ahahah nice one Noodle, though being that honest may have earned him some enemies he maybe in need of friends who shares his ideal to help him advance his motivation. <br /> <br /> And last you told me that we could make a martial art for Amelia though i'm not sure that what I want qualifies as a martial art.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T10:02:02-08:00","id":397729,"title":"","content":"I appreciate the complements!<br /> <br /> To be completely open, Vellus was deliberately crafted to set off your skeezeball sensors. And that write-up, while all true, is not exhaustive. The best lies, after all, are the ones that are true (Avoiding the Truth Technique FTW), so he could still be a master manipulator. If his write-up were that small, I wouldn't have bothered writing it up to begin with; the ones I do write up are generally for impressively magical people (Ba Rai, Baal-Hadad, Mejan Holof), plot relevant people (Larissa, Dero, Maia) or both (Padishah, Feiro, Esstrayaan). Hell, due to his position as the longest running and most occurring NPC, Dero has four writeups, with a fifth in the works. <br /> <br /> There's some pretty wonky MAs, both in Exalted and IRL. What exactly do you have in mind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T12:32:52-08:00","id":397894,"title":"","content":"Lets see:<br /> Motivation: Doesn't say he actually has to be just and honest, just to appear to be one so as to set an example<br /> Intimacies: Honesty (not the only policy), Gens Nikoloi (Ruthlessness in advancing), Novalesk (It is our duty to get rid of those undesirables)<br /> Abilities: Bureaucracy (If they walk away alive then it was obviously fair to them), Integrity (Honesty and Openness aren't the same thing. Enjoy all the misleading truths)<br /> Charms: Stoke the Flame (only for inciting mobs against those I don't like on flimsy legal grounds)<br /> <br /> The cynicism is strong with this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T12:49:12-08:00","id":397918,"title":"","content":"Heh.<br /> <br /> Anyways, it's been over a year since this game started! This has been the longest running Play-by-post game I've been in, let alone run, and has been just as long as my longest running IRL exalted game. <br /> <br /> So in celebration, I want to do something for you guys. Each of you can pick a single NPC, and I will write a short story (aiming for around 1000) words from their perspective. You can even request a particular topic or subject for them (Like &quot;Dero: a goofy adventure&quot; which I already know will be Dietaku's request). This gives you an opportunity to get a new perspective of both the game and NPCs, as well as allowing you to perhaps get some OOC knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T20:29:24-08:00","id":398333,"title":"","content":"It's great to have been a part of this. It is my first Exalted game ever and I hope I haven't been too much of a n00b for you guys.<br /> <br /> Vellus may be able to convince both myself and Jensven that he is honest and should be trusted. He just seems too much like slippery folks Jensven has met in the past. Of course, the information in your write-up wasn't available to me before so I stand by my decisions based on the information I had available. :P<br /> <br /> I have thought about the Abyssal thing and I would have to say that I will pass on that for now. I want to get to the point where I can play a Solar alright first and then maybe consider it. Of course, trying to recreate the Final Five of Final Fantasy Four (FFoFFF) in Exalted and doing a chronicle with them would own. (This has become a recent obsession with most games I am playing. Don't mind me.)<br /> <br /> As far as that offer of the Short Story goes, I don't think I have encountered any NPCs up to this point that would like to see a story about that badly. I will definitely attempt to cash that in after I find one that I feel merits that type of request.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T16:59:38-08:00","id":399568,"title":"","content":"I'd like to go with Alamass if you don't mind since he is my ally I think it would be a good idea to know the guy a bit, the topic will be the fall of the first age I'm a bit curious as to what you want to do with the character and I want to integrate better with the story.<br /> <br /> Also on a similar note does our characters first age incarnation matter in the game ? I want to expand Amelia's background by adding her first age incarnation story I have not wrote anything yet and have no specific ideas yet, if you already have ideas on the matter I'm interested in reading them since past incarnation are one of the many, many things I like in exalted.<br /> <br /> As for the martial art I only have a name and basic idea for now.<br /> <br /> Cosmic Dragon style<br /> A strange martial art style that allow one to master space and time by disrupting reality and tearing away pieces of the loom of fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T18:52:14-08:00","id":399718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=399568#post399568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to go with Alamass if you don't mind since he is my ally I think it would be a good idea to know the guy a bit, the topic will be the fall of the first age I'm a bit curious as to what you want to do with the character and I want to integrate better with the story.<br /> <br /> Also on a similar note does our characters first age incarnation matter in the game ? I want to expand Amelia's background by adding her first age incarnation story I have not wrote anything yet and have no specific ideas yet, if you already have ideas on the matter I'm interested in reading them since past incarnation are one of the many, many things I like in exalted.<br /> <br /> As for the martial art I only have a name and basic idea for now.<br /> <br /> Cosmic Dragon style<br /> A strange martial art style that allow one to master space and time by disrupting reality and tearing away pieces of the loom of fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a Sidereal style, they tend to be the crazy esoteric ones. The craziest cannon celestial style is only like that with the capstone that turns you into a dream-dragon who might dissolve into dreams if you stay in the form too long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T19:39:25-08:00","id":399814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=399718#post399718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds like a Sidereal style, they tend to be the crazy esoteric ones. The craziest cannon celestial style is only like that with the capstone that turns you into a dream-dragon who might dissolve into dreams if you stay in the form too long.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why oh why did they create sidereals and gave their own martial arts screwing with fate wasn't enough it seems. Still I think it could be a great style with some of the move I have in mind though some might be essence 5 or 6 charms, though if it's gonna be a sidereal style it's gonna stay in my head no way I'm gonna get my ass kicked with my own martial art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T13:48:30-08:00","id":400815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=397918#post397918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heh.<br /> (Like &quot;Dero: a goofy adventure&quot; which I already know will be Dietaku's request). .</div> </div> </div> </div>Dero's goofy adventu--SHIT.<br /> <br /> Alrighty, then, smart guy. How about Dero's origin story? What wacky hijinks did he get in before he met Tirien?<br /> <br /> As for Magnusar, well, that's because at their core, Sidereals are the wise badass old mentor Exalts. Look back at their mention in 1e core (Or take my word for it, because no one ought go back to 1e for anything.) where they're mentioned as being powerful and wise Exalts, often being sorcerers. Now, to Western eyes, the wise kung fu mentor character resonates with us, so Sidereals, being the Ben Kenobi to the Solar Luke Skywalker, got powerful martial arts to compensate for their lack of higher-end charms. Flash forward after several attempts to &quot;Balance&quot; this, and well, you get where we are. Personally, I'm of a mind that Sidereal MAs are fine as they are. Yes, they're overpowered, but look at their prerequisites; usually in excess of Essence 6, at which time, Solars can sword so hard, they can wield an infinite number of weapons, Terrestrials get access to crazy elemental typhoon blasts and Lunars can become monsters so large the Titan of HUGE gets a little peeved by their existence. So, yeah, Obsidian Shards of Infinity or Border of Kaleidoscopic Logic styles being able to make mincemeat of any reasonable Solar PCs? Well, DUH, they're the last resort weapons of creatures WAY out of their weight class.<br /> <br /> But, that's my two cents. You could probably have a &quot;Father Time&quot; style that uses swords, though. Maybe letting you do rerolls as you rewind time to do certain things. Sure, it dances around &quot;No time travel,&quot; but, so do many SWILIHN and Sidereal charms, so I see no foul here","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","user":"Dietaku","date":". 02-10-2015, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T14:29:38-08:00","id":400849,"title":"","content":"Since you guys are all so rad, I decided to start a new Exalted 2.5 game, this time set in the North. the link is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\"> here</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T11:29:24-08:00","id":402161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=399568#post399568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to go with Alamass if you don't mind since he is my ally I think it would be a good idea to know the guy a bit, the topic will be the fall of the first age I'm a bit curious as to what you want to do with the character and I want to integrate better with the story.<br /> <br /> Also on a similar note does our characters first age incarnation matter in the game ? I want to expand Amelia's background by adding her first age incarnation story I have not wrote anything yet and have no specific ideas yet, if you already have ideas on the matter I'm interested in reading them since past incarnation are one of the many, many things I like in exalted.<br /> <br /> As for the martial art I only have a name and basic idea for now.<br /> <br /> Cosmic Dragon style<br /> A strange martial art style that allow one to master space and time by disrupting reality and tearing away pieces of the loom of fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>(1) By the fall of the First Age, you you mean like, what he was doing during the Usurpation?<br /> <br /> (2) It matters as much as you want it to!<br /> <br /> (3) That sounds very much like an SMA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T11:31:22-08:00","id":402174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=400815#post400815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dero's goofy adventu--SHIT.<br /> <br /> Alrighty, then, smart guy. How about Dero's origin story? What wacky hijinks did he get in before he met Tirien?</div> </div> </div> </div>So I have:<br /> <br /> <br /> Dietaku: Dero's Origin Story.<br /> Magnusar: Alamass at the Fall of the First Age<br /> Belkra: Pass (as of present)<br /> Exthalion: ?<br /> <br /> I would like to point out that you need not have met these characters; you could ask about, say, the Bone Monarch. Or you could ask about Historical figures such as Myrinne or Midea, Odal Thousand-Fangs, the Three Founders, etc. If they've been mentioned IC or OOC, they're fair game!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T12:33:55-08:00","id":402252,"title":"","content":"For my story: Larissa or Artemia, having a normal day in the post Yi's arrival age of Novalesk. Your choice of which.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 02-11-2015, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T14:29:25-08:00","id":402462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=402161#post402161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (1) By the fall of the First Age, you you mean like, what he was doing during the Usurpation?<br /> <br /> (2) It matters as much as you want it to!<br /> <br /> (3) That sounds very much like an SMA.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Yes that is exactly what I meant<br /> <br /> 2. Nice this could also help you decide if the codex is acceptable<br /> <br /> 3. Oh... Well forget about it then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T18:07:00-08:00","id":402682,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Codicier of Final Repose sounds like a chap (or lass) I would like to hear more about as a player. They sound awesome as anything and I am excited to figure out what is going on with them. Maybe even figure out more about the Underworld in this region in the process.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conv