t.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T15:35:41-07:00","id":457363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=457279#post457279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm just messing with you Exthalion, I have no interest in ordon except to either converting or destroying them but I was wondering if I should spend my exp to get tiger warrior training technique right now or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Curse the internet and the lack of secondary communication! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If we are voting though, we are totally converting. That sweet, sweet infrastructure is begging to be repurposed by me.<br /> <br /> Edit: @Noodle<br /> <br /> Wow! Things like this are why you are the best ST I have yet had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 03-25-2015, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T18:28:06-07:00","id":457555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=457265#post457265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I figured they have known since Grey Ice. However, given that I could well be an invincible sword prince they probably want to get a proper Hunt together first, and that takes time, money, and dedicated Terrestrials. None of these are exactly in great supply. I am hoping that by the time they do get around to it that Jensven will have turned Novalesk's armed forces into tiger warriors and Origenes will be tots down with raining doom on them. (Arming said tiger warriors with gunzota armor and implosion bows is gravy)<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, should I expect something about the big to do Yi did or just start working on my next post?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tiger Warrior Training Technique is not something I picture Jensven taking for a LOOOONG time. There are better odds of him getting to a point that he is constructing the Gunzosha (sp?) armor first. Although, if he does make Shadow godlike, get decent armor, and do a Solar Wonder Twin thing with Amelia...They might be able to take a Wild Hunt by their lonesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T07:56:50-07:00","id":458059,"title":"","content":"@Exthalion: Amelia is not a savage of course we try to convert them at first, if we can't then we fight them.<br /> <br /> @Belkra; I can totally see that happening two dawn caste taking out an army. Training tiger warriors will give Amelia something to do except fighting when everyone are building things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T12:21:18-07:00","id":458239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=457363#post457363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: @Noodle<br /> <br /> Wow! Things like this are why you are the best ST I have yet had.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Nice to know you guys are enjoying yourselves. <br /> <br /> Though, what exactly are you referring to? (Just so I can try to do it more often.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=458059#post458059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Belkra; I can totally see that happening two dawn caste taking out an army. Training tiger warriors will give Amelia something to do except fighting when everyone are building things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tiger Warrior Training is a pretty damn awesome charm, and it will let you do stuff like that while the others are crafting! Downtime may not be as sedate as you're imagining, though. I fully expect downtime to be filled with the Circle going off in ones and twos to have their own awesome adventures. Fighting evil witches and wizards, saving kingdoms, seeking out the ancient masters of lost and forbidden martial secrets, getting all the money, killing princesses to save the monsters they've locked in a tower. <br /> <br /> You know, usual Exalt stuff. <br /> <br /> And, in the process of writing that I realized that's basically what's going on now. Huh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T16:23:41-07:00","id":458482,"title":"","content":"Saffron has been introduced! Also, Solars need to stop getting lost in the Wyld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T05:18:40-07:00","id":458819,"title":"","content":"Gotcha. I'll get on it when I get home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5005-heavenlythunder","name":"HeavenlyThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5005_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T09:01:14-07:00","id":466176,"title":"","content":"So Tirien thinks Saffron is Fair Folk? Let's see how long we can encourage that belief...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5005-heavenlythunder","name":"HeavenlyThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5005_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T15:39:02-07:00","id":467916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HeavenlyThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=466176#post466176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Tirien thinks Saffron is Fair Folk? Let's see how long we can encourage that belief...</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you blame her, though? Her master's master models herself as a Fae Princess, and her master is something of an intellectual in the vein of Wyld studies. Being from an intellectual background as well, I'd imagine that Tirien would naturally equate any garishly dressed, attractive newcomers as being of Fae origins, at least in her current environs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T20:10:39-07:00","id":468094,"title":"","content":"Fair! *rim-shot* They'll get along like a house on fire, I hope. Either in the spirit of the saying or as a house and fire actually would get along.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5005-heavenlythunder","name":"HeavenlyThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5005_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T05:07:33-07:00","id":481273,"title":"","content":"I'll be gone until the Monday after next Monday, in case replies are needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5005-heavenlythunder","name":"HeavenlyThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5005_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T10:22:31-07:00","id":505746,"title":"","content":"Anyone still around ? Just checking if we're gonna kick some fairfolks ass <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T17:18:25-07:00","id":506249,"title":"","content":"I'm lurking pretty much every day. I would like to join you in kicking those fair folk around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T18:16:33-07:00","id":506287,"title":"","content":"Same. Have 30 pages due next week, and other end of semester craziness, but still here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T05:59:33-07:00","id":506657,"title":"","content":"Belkra: And it would be fun if Jensven was in the wyld with us but he has to make sure that Yi comes back from the field trip to hell. I would have better liked to go to hell with you guys actually... (Sigh) I want to kill demons so let's hurry up and waste these fools so we can move on to other threats.<br /> <br /> Exthalion: Oh sounds rough hang in there <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Since your the only solar player with craft magitech for now, do you think it's possible to create a nation wide magitech infrastructure in Novalesk ? I think we might need an arsenal soon... Oh and I'm not talking first age infractructure but a factory cathedral or something like it, would help us a lot in the future I think. (If the Ess'tee let us of course <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 05-07-2015, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T07:37:43-07:00","id":506752,"title":"","content":"I'm around, I just don't think Saf has anything to do at the moment. Somebody else (Amelia?) is holding the floor I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5005-heavenlythunder","name":"HeavenlyThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5005_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T08:42:50-07:00","id":506887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HeavenlyThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=506752#post506752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm around, I just don't think Saf has anything to do at the moment. Somebody else (Amelia?) is holding the floor I think.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She is not really holding the floor but she does not want to waste time and she doesn't like fairfolks so for now Ishe is trying to get him to tell if he has Ciprus mind, so feel free to interact if Saf is a kind of thief/assassin he could help us find it and win some favors with us and it could help the characters to get each other more.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T09:29:35-07:00","id":506940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=506657#post506657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exthalion: Oh sounds rough hang in there <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Since your the only solar player with craft magitech for now, do you think it's possible to create a nation wide magitech infrastructure in Novalesk ? I think we might need an arsenal soon... Oh and I'm not talking first age infractructure but a factory cathedral or something like it, would help us a lot in the future I think. (If the Ess'tee let us of course <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)</div> </div> </div> </div>The answer is... sort of. Here's the problem. It takes a total of Craft+Lore+Occult=15 to design level 4 manses, and I have that. Level 5 manses require 20 dots so that is out of the picture for now and that is where Factory Cathedrals are.<br /> <br /> However, 4 dot powers include Atelier manses. These nice little things reduce the artifact creation roll by one step (seasons to months, divided by 9 for CNNT = 3.1 days). It also reduces the interval by one (or two for cheap items) for mundane items AND produces mundane items assembly line style. So once set up it could do things like crank out a suit of armor every hour.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, for building the thing: It would take 100 workers 8 years to build this thing at normal speed. Call it 800 man years. However, I have a custom charm that lets me apply CNNT to a workforce with a magnitude equal to my essence. The upper end of Magnitude 3 is 150. 150*9= effectively 1350 workers. 800/1350=0.59 years, or 248 days/35 weeks/8.8 months/3 seasons.<br /> <br /> Now if I save up for essence 4... it becomes 93 days. Which is not to say I couldn't summon up demons to reduce the time further. However, even going with the best, hopping puppeteers count as 10 mortals, summoned up one per night it only goes down to 158 days at E3 or 104 days at E4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T10:44:49-07:00","id":506981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=506940#post506940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The answer is... sort of. Here's the problem. It takes a total of Craft+Lore+Occult=15 to design level 4 manses, and I have that. Level 5 manses require 20 dots so that is out of the picture for now and that is where Factory Cathedrals are.<br /> <br /> However, 4 dot powers include Atelier manses. These nice little things reduce the artifact creation roll by one step (seasons to months, divided by 9 for CNNT = 3.1 days). It also reduces the interval by one (or two for cheap items) for mundane items AND produces mundane items assembly line style. So once set up it could do things like crank out a suit of armor every hour.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, for building the thing: It would take 100 workers 8 years to build this thing at normal speed. Call it 800 man years. However, I have a custom charm that lets me apply CNNT to a workforce with a magnitude equal to my essence. The upper end of Magnitude 3 is 150. 150*9= effectively 1350 workers. 800/1350=0.59 years, or 248 days/35 weeks/8.8 months/3 seasons.<br /> <br /> Now if I save up for essence 4... it becomes 93 days. Which is not to say I couldn't summon up demons to reduce the time further. However, even going with the best, hopping puppeteers count as 10 mortals, summoned up one per night it only goes down to 158 days at E3 or 104 days at E4.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I didn't know that athelier manse can reduce the interval for crafting artifacts, I did know that it is a production line for mundane item and thaumaturgical items, if you go to essence 4 you can get Wonder forging genius and the prerequisite to build the cathedral would drop by 3 and if you take a specialisation in manse building it could be possible. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I know I'm going for essence 4 as soon as the fairfolks are dealt with, legendary warrior curiculum will allow us to have a powerful military. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T11:03:40-07:00","id":507000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=506981#post506981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I didn't know that athelier manse can reduce the interval for crafting artifacts, I did know that it is a production line for mundane item and thaumaturgical items, if you go to essence 4 you can get Wonder forging genius and the prerequisite to build the cathedral would drop by 3 and if you take a specialisation in manse building it could be possible. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I know I'm going for essence 4 as soon as the fairfolks are dealt with, legendary warrior curiculum will allow us to have a powerful military. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I am going to start saving for E4 (DBL is the gold standard of crafting) but I just blew a lot of xp since I didn't think we would have the downtime to raise essence. Months off is kind of hard to schedule around a war.<br /> <br /> Edit: That, and my civic responsibilities are going to take up a lot of time as well. Hopefully I can delegate most of the job to the previous Archon while I spend the tax revenue on magic infrastructure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T15:23:42-07:00","id":507272,"title":"","content":"Meanwhile, I'm over here trying to think of ways to make a godlike Malamute knockoff. I don't think I will be going with the Medicine charms mentioned previously. That just doesn't seem to fit with what the character would do and how he would want to treat the animal. Never mind the fact that he has Medicine favored. I may have to go with custom Survival charms despite not favoring that Ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T16:02:45-07:00","id":507311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=506940#post506940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The answer is... sort of. Here's the problem. It takes a total of Craft+Lore+Occult=15 to design level 4 manses, and I have that. Level 5 manses require 20 dots so that is out of the picture for now and that is where Factory Cathedrals are.<br /> <br /> However, 4 dot powers include Atelier manses. These nice little things reduce the artifact creation roll by one step (seasons to months, divided by 9 for CNNT = 3.1 days). It also reduces the interval by one (or two for cheap items) for mundane items AND produces mundane items assembly line style. So once set up it could do things like crank out a suit of armor every hour.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, for building the thing: It would take 100 workers 8 years to build this thing at normal speed. Call it 800 man years. However, I have a custom charm that lets me apply CNNT to a workforce with a magnitude equal to my essence. The upper end of Magnitude 3 is 150. 150*9= effectively 1350 workers. 800/1350=0.59 years, or 248 days/35 weeks/8.8 months/3 seasons.<br /> <br /> Now if I save up for essence 4... it becomes 93 days. Which is not to say I couldn't summon up demons to reduce the time further. However, even going with the best, hopping puppeteers count as 10 mortals, summoned up one per night it only goes down to 158 days at E3 or 104 days at E4.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It would also require a rating 4 demesne, of which none are known to exist in Novalesk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T16:05:09-07:00","id":507332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=507000#post507000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am going to start saving for E4 (DBL is the gold standard of crafting) but I just blew a lot of xp since I didn't think we would have the downtime to raise essence. Months off is kind of hard to schedule around a war.<br /> <br /> Edit: That, and my civic responsibilities are going to take up a lot of time as well. Hopefully I can delegate most of the job to the previous Archon while I spend the tax revenue on magic infrastructure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Months of downtime is possible after the war though. <br /> <br /> Also, your current job is pretty small fries, and is basically you being a government sanctioned Scavenger Lord/tradesman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T16:11:48-07:00","id":507333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=507272#post507272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile, I'm over here trying to think of ways to make a godlike Malamute knockoff. I don't think I will be going with the Medicine charms mentioned previously. That just doesn't seem to fit with what the character would do and how he would want to treat the animal. Never mind the fact that he has Medicine favored. I may have to go with custom Survival charms despite not favoring that Ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are other paths. Sorcery, spiritual blessings, genesis, Wyld magic.<br /> <br /> Other people can work on making Shadow more awesome, too. There's an ex-PC genesis-specialist Solar running around, and Tirien's Lunar mentor makes entire species from scratch. Fae can be hard to deal with, but you have a few friendly(ish) fae on your team right now. Alopekis is the deity of the Novaleski Wolfhound, and is likely to know a few charms that may help Shadow get stronger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T16:14:46-07:00","id":507334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=507311#post507311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would also require a rating 4 demesne, of which none are known to exist in Novalesk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank Sol DBL lets me put it on top of a 3 dot demesne. Without that its either conquer the nearest 4 dot or wait years for geomancy to upgrade an existing one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=507332#post507332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Months of downtime is possible after the war though.<br /> <br /> Also, your current job is pretty small fries, and is basically you being a government sanctioned Scavenger Lord/tradesman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... I assume the social magic just needs more time to percolate. Or I need to invent New Fast Acting Social Nuke (tm).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T16:25:45-07:00","id":507339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=507334#post507334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank Sol DBL lets me put it on top of a 3 dot demesne. Without that its either conquer the nearest 4 dot or wait years for geomancy to upgrade an existing one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or destroy Esstrayaan's house and build it there. Or conquer Theros, raze Theros city and build it upon it's blasted ruins. Or build upon still-smoldering crater that was once Darumfel.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=507334#post507334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... I assume the social magic just needs more time to percolate. Or I need to invent New Fast Acting Social Nuke (tm).</div> </div> </div> </div>It does, in some cases. In others, you probably need to do something more concrete that make vague promises. Building the temple to Aesclepius is a step in that direction, and the trip to Hell is another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T18:58:40-07:00","id":507476,"title":"","content":"1. So Aurem is friendly ? I though it would be a bit more you know hostile. <br /> <br /> 2. Darumfel still exist ? Though not much if you say it is still smoldering. Interesting... (Might need more info on it later)<br /> <br /> 3. Exthalion I found this, could be useful if Ess'tee approves it. <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Dragon-Line Architect</span></b><br /> Cost: 20m, 1wp; Mins: Lore 5, Essence 4; Type: Simple (Dramatic Action)<br /> Keywords: Combo-OK, Obvious, Shaping<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Wyld-Shaping Technique <br /> The Lawgivers were tasked with the maintenance of Creation as well as the expansion of its borders. <br /> Using Dragon-Line Architect is an extended dramatic action. The dice pool used equals (Intelligence + Lore). Each roll requires five hours of effort, and the character pays the Charm's cost with each roll. This roll has a base difficulty of (1 + demesne rating). This technique has no effect on a demesne capped with a Manse. <br /> The Lawgiver can spend accumulated successes at any point to complete part of her construction. This functions as follow. <br /> <br /> Improving Demesne: A Solar can cleanse and strengthen the flow of Essence to a region and increase the rating of a demesne by one. This requires a number of successes equal to the new rating times five. Additionally, a sacrifice of resources equal to the new rating (new rating +2 for celestially aspect demesnes) is also required. Artifacts can also be substituted with the rating and type of artifact governing what the new demesne will be raised to. Increasing a demesne cannot change its aspect. If the new rating puts resources into a N/A state (6+) then the storyteller is obligated to tell the Solar what item(s) must be gathered to increase the rating. These will always be exotic and should involve a significant quest or deed to achieve. <br /> Changing Demesne: A demesne may be changed in a similar method requiring sacrifices equal to current rating of the demesne (rating +2 for Celestial aspect) and five successes are required. It is also possible to change demesne aspects over a course of months by simply expending at least 10 motes of essence times the demesne's rating for a number of months equal to 2x the demesne's rating. Sorcery can also be used to change aspects. If the resource cost of a conversion is in excess of 5 then a special sacrifice is required. Each sacrifice lowers the resource requirement by 1. These sacrifices are up to the ST but should typically be a quest worthy item, taming a raging fire elemental, converting a fluid Fair Folk into a diamond for Earth and the like. <br /> <br /> Create Demesne: The Lawgiver can even create a demesne in the most desolate of locations. Realistically, however, it is best to create demesne near their elemental poles. The difficulty for establishing a new demesne is 1 if near their respective pole, 5, if approximately half way across creation, or 10 if at the opposite side of creation. Five successes are required. Celestial demesne require 10 successes and are at a difficulty of 5 to establish anywhere in creation. <br /> <br /> Dragon Line: A Solar can also increase or decrease the potency of a dragon line and thus increase or decrease the flow of essence to a region. This process is considerably more complicated and can be used to affect up to the Solar's Essence in demesne per use. This technique is mainly used to repair the pattern of creation. Increasing the flow of essence to the region surrounding a shadow land will cause it to shrink. Decreasing the flow of essence to a region will cause a freehold to collapse upon itself. Each success expended for this use will reduce the size of one of these regions by one mile. The regions must be surrounded to be affected and larger areas may require several Lawgivers to work in tandem to achieve their effect. <br /> <br /> This technique was used to repair and maintain creation and Lawgivers who demonstrate knowledge of it would be among the first targets of the Deathlords and Fae Princes. It is for this reason that Mask of Winters has expended considerable effort to cap every demesne near to Thorns to prevent the resurgent Lawgivers from easily collapsing his newfound empire</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T20:14:48-07:00","id":507559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=507476#post507476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Exthalion I found this, could be useful if Ess'tee approves it.<br /> [snip]</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for that. I have used this cascade from the Ever-Cascading Torrent of Glory:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Feeling the Dragon\u2019s Path<br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Occult 2, Essence 2; Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Any Occult Excellency<br /> Placing his hand upon the soil, the Solar can feel the currents<br /> of essence that flow through it, the dragon lines that weave<br /> together the geomancy of Creation. This Charm allows the Solar<br /> to sense all dragon lines and demesnes within (Occult x 10)<br /> miles, and all manses within half that range. If the Exalt holds<br /> the hearthstone of a manse, he may instead detect it with the full<br /> range of this Charm. The Solar automatically discerns the aspect<br /> of any demesne or manse revealed by this Charm.<br /> <br /> Bending the Dragon\u2019s Flow<br /> Cost: 20m; Mins: Occult 5, Essence 4; Type: Simple (Dramatic<br /> Action)<br /> Keywords: Combo-Basic<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Feeling the Dragon\u2019s Path<br /> The wise scholars of the Solar Exalted reshape the world itself,<br /> ordering the geomancy of its dragon lines in auspicious<br /> harmony. This Charm is a dramatic action to create a demesne,<br /> with an interval of a single season. The Solar must spend that<br /> time meditating in the center of the region he wishes to enrich<br /> with geomantic perfection, practicing enlightened yoga, maintaining<br /> essence-channeling rock gardens, or wrangling dragon<br /> lines into place with his bare hands. He rolls (Intelligence +<br /> Occult) at difficulty one, and, if he succeeds, a new demesne<br /> manifests, up to (Essence x 1000) square yards in size. The Solar<br /> may determine the aspect of the demesne he creates, and is automatically<br /> attuned to it. Demesnes created by this Charm always<br /> have a rating of one.<br /> It is also possible to increase the rating of existing demesnes<br /> using this Charm. Doing so increases the interval of this Charm<br /> to a number of seasons equal to the rating the Solar is attempting<br /> to raise the demesne to, and requires even more extensive<br /> geomantic alterations. Once he has completed this extended<br /> activation, he must succeed on an (Intelligence + Occult) roll<br /> with a difficulty equal to the rating he is attempting to raise the<br /> demesne to. Each activation may only raise the demesne\u2019s rating<br /> by one dot. Altering existing demesnes is far easier\u2014by spending<br /> a season in geomantic meditation and succeeding on an (Intelligence<br /> + Occult) roll at the difficulty of an attuned demesne,<br /> the Solar may alter its aspect.<br /> It is also possible to use this essence-channeling technique<br /> to destroy demesnes, though doing so is fraught with risk even<br /> for the Solar Exalted. Rather than the meticulous sculpting of<br /> dragon lines needed to create or alter a manse, this technique<br /> simply warps and cracks the geomancy of a demesne until it cannot<br /> maintain its integrity. Activated in this way, this Charm has<br /> an interval of one day. The Solar rolls (Intelligence + Occult) at a<br /> difficulty of the demesnes\u2019s rating, banking all threshold successes.<br /> He must re-activate this Charm on the next day to continue<br /> the process, and must continue doing so until he has accumulated<br /> (5 + [Demesne Rating x 5]) successes, at which point essence<br /> build-up begins. If the Solar does not maintain this process, the<br /> geomantic damage is undone, the maimed dragon lines shifting<br /> back into place. This Charm cannot enrich, alter, or destroy<br /> demesnes that have been capped with a manse.<br /> <br /> Dragon-and-Pearl Meditation<br /> Cost: \u2014; Mins: Occult 6, Essence 6; Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Bending the Dragon\u2019s Flow<br /> Elder geomancy techniques allowed the Solars of the First<br /> Age to reshape the face of Creation itself. This Charm upgrades<br /> Bending the Dragon\u2019s Flow. When used to create, enhance, or<br /> alter demesnes, its interval is reduced to weeks, rather than seasons.<br /> In addition, the Solar may now create demesnes with a<br /> rating higher than one. Doing so increases the difficulty of the<br /> (Intelligence + Occult) roll to the rating of demesne he wishes<br /> to create, and takes a number of weeks equal to the rating. Likewise,<br /> he may now raise the rating of demesnes by more than one<br /> dot. At Essence 7++, the interval for geomantic alterations is<br /> further reduced to days.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Personally, I hope there is some sort of cap/area so that an ever increasing geomantic network actually needs to start covering territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 05-07-2015, 11:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date: