sive<br /> geomantic alterations. Once he has completed this extended<br /> activation, he must succeed on an (Intelligence + Occult) roll<br /> with a difficulty equal to the rating he is attempting to raise the<br /> demesne to. Each activation may only raise the demesne\u2019s rating<br /> by one dot. Altering existing demesnes is far easier\u2014by spending<br /> a season in geomantic meditation and succeeding on an (Intelligence<br /> + Occult) roll at the difficulty of an attuned demesne,<br /> the Solar may alter its aspect.<br /> It is also possible to use this essence-channeling technique<br /> to destroy demesnes, though doing so is fraught with risk even<br /> for the Solar Exalted. Rather than the meticulous sculpting of<br /> dragon lines needed to create or alter a manse, this technique<br /> simply warps and cracks the geomancy of a demesne until it cannot<br /> maintain its integrity. Activated in this way, this Charm has<br /> an interval of one day. The Solar rolls (Intelligence + Occult) at a<br /> difficulty of the demesnes\u2019s rating, banking all threshold successes.<br /> He must re-activate this Charm on the next day to continue<br /> the process, and must continue doing so until he has accumulated<br /> (5 + [Demesne Rating x 5]) successes, at which point essence<br /> build-up begins. If the Solar does not maintain this process, the<br /> geomantic damage is undone, the maimed dragon lines shifting<br /> back into place. This Charm cannot enrich, alter, or destroy<br /> demesnes that have been capped with a manse.<br /> <br /> Dragon-and-Pearl Meditation<br /> Cost: \u2014; Mins: Occult 6, Essence 6; Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Bending the Dragon\u2019s Flow<br /> Elder geomancy techniques allowed the Solars of the First<br /> Age to reshape the face of Creation itself. This Charm upgrades<br /> Bending the Dragon\u2019s Flow. When used to create, enhance, or<br /> alter demesnes, its interval is reduced to weeks, rather than seasons.<br /> In addition, the Solar may now create demesnes with a<br /> rating higher than one. Doing so increases the difficulty of the<br /> (Intelligence + Occult) roll to the rating of demesne he wishes<br /> to create, and takes a number of weeks equal to the rating. Likewise,<br /> he may now raise the rating of demesnes by more than one<br /> dot. At Essence 7++, the interval for geomantic alterations is<br /> further reduced to days.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Personally, I hope there is some sort of cap/area so that an ever increasing geomantic network actually needs to start covering territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there are one actually from what I read about Denandsor, it says that there are a dozen factory cathedral in the city. I assume that if you do it correctly we could have a least three high level manse in a city in the second age. We will need to expand the network carefully it could be a incentive to join us. The geomantic work is not what I think will be the problem it's the magical material while certain can be manufactured with thaumaturgy others cannot and it will take a lot of it.<br /> <br /> Can we make jade ? like Orichalcum is made from gold, sunlight and lava.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T09:27:12-07:00","id":508147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=507476#post507476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. So Aurem is friendly ? I though it would be a bit more you know hostile. <br /> <br /> 2. Darumfel still exist ? Though not much if you say it is still smoldering. Interesting... (Might need more info on it later)</div> </div> </div> </div>1- Aurem appears to be friendly. Whether or not he actually is has yet to be seen.<br /> <br /> 2- Darumfel exists, as a Necropolis, in the Underworld. The earthly remnants of the city were blasted into a crater. The walls of the city, however, were a powerful fortress-manse (turns out you can get a ton of neet perks if you minimize Habitability and Hearthstone). The only things keeping the demesne unclaimed are the descendants of Darumfel's survivors, the Vicruith Geherin being relatively close, and the fact that any breach into the Underworld would put you inside a very angry, very militant Necropolis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T09:34:24-07:00","id":508160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=507977#post507977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think there are one actually from what I read about Denandsor, it says that there are a dozen factory cathedral in the city. I assume that if you do it correctly we could have a least three high level manse in a city in the second age. We will need to expand the network carefully it could be a incentive to join us. The geomantic work is not what I think will be the problem it's the magical material while certain can be manufactured with thaumaturgy others cannot and it will take a lot of it.<br /> <br /> Can we make jade ? like Orichalcum is made from gold, sunlight and lava.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recall it ever being said that Denandsor had a dozen factory cathedrals. Lookshy, on the other hand, has three five-dot manses, and that was said to be a wealth of magical power, even in the first age. <br /> <br /> Making Jade would require finding a way to concentrate elemental essence into the corresponding Jade color. It would likely be time consuming and require a demesne of whatever element Jade you're trying to make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T10:32:49-07:00","id":508187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=508160#post508160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't recall it ever being said that Denandsor had a dozen factory cathedrals. Lookshy, on the other hand, has three five-dot manses, and that was said to be a wealth of magical power, even in the first age.<br /> <br /> Making Jade would require finding a way to concentrate elemental essence into the corresponding Jade color. It would likely be time consuming and require a demesne of whatever element Jade you're trying to make.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, seems I spoke too fast they don't mention number but they do says that there are factory-cathedrals in Denandsor and first age geomancy was something else in those days so it <b><i>could</i></b> have a dozen around the city.<br /> <br /> Beside even if it is impossible, for a solar this concept doesn't exist.<br /> <br /> So it's easier to make orichalcum than jade ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 05-08-2015, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T11:22:56-07:00","id":508210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=508187#post508187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, seems I spoke too fast they don't mention number but they do says that there are factory-cathedrals in Denandsor and first age geomancy was something else in those days so it <b><i>could</i></b> have a dozen around the city.<br /> <br /> Beside even if it is impossible, for a solar this concept doesn't exist.<br /> <br /> So it's easier to make orichalcum than jade ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Much. The standard method is to use the art of alchemy (either the crucible of tarim or a room full of thaumaturges) to turn base metals into gold and then refine it. Giant bombs can be used to blow a hole in the ground if you lack a volcano of your own.<br /> <br /> The thing with Jade is that it is obscenely common in some places. The Imperial Mountain has jade deposits the size of cities, and apparently the seafloor is black jade near the poll of water. If you have the right mining infrastructure in places its cheaper than wyldshaping it.<br /> <br /> Wyld shaping is incidentally the way most &quot;Set The Craft Skill On Fire Until You Can Rebuild The First Age In A Cave With A Box Of Scraps&quot; plans deal with the lack of resources.<br /> <br /> STCSOFUYCRTFAIACWABOS plans also enjoy using a Rod of Verdant Minerals to make lots of mundane material (works best if an integrated utility artifact for a manse) and mass summoning of demons to melt into Calcanth to use as exotic material components. Factory Cathedrals are of course not optional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T11:53:42-07:00","id":508229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=508210#post508210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Much. The standard method is to use the art of alchemy (either the crucible of tarim or a room full of thaumaturges) to turn base metals into gold and then refine it. Giant bombs can be used to blow a hole in the ground if you lack a volcano of your own.<br /> <br /> The thing with Jade is that it is obscenely common in some places. The Imperial Mountain has jade deposits the size of cities, and apparently the seafloor is black jade near the poll of water. If you have the right mining infrastructure in places its cheaper than wyldshaping it.<br /> <br /> Wyld shaping is incidentally the way most &quot;Set The Craft Skill On Fire Until You Can Rebuild The First Age In A Cave With A Box Of Scraps&quot; plans deal with the lack of resources.<br /> <br /> STCSOFUYCRTFAIACWABOS plans also enjoy using a Rod of Verdant Minerals to make lots of mundane material (works best if an integrated utility artifact for a manse) and mass summoning of demons to melt into Calcanth to use as exotic material components. Factory Cathedrals are of course not optional.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, the thing I noticed is that some ST (I don't count Noodle or Dietaku in this) do not want to have factory-cathedrals in their game I was told that it is a game breaker and that is was ridiculus to mass produce artifacts, hell one banned magitech from is game. I mean what's the point of the craft skill and being a godking if you can't build awesome things quickly while the rest of creation have magitech or necrotech infrastructures huge armies and other less savory stuff.<br /> <br /> Sorry this is a bitter feeling of mine when people tell you that there is cool stuff but you can't have it.<br /> <br /> Still we could take a stroll to the elemetal pole of wood to stock up on jade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 05-08-2015, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T12:58:57-07:00","id":508344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=508229#post508229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, the thing I noticed is that some ST (I don't count Noodle or Dietaku in this) do not want to have factory-cathedrals in their game I was told that it is a game breaker and that is was ridiculus to mass produce artifacts, hell one banned magitech from is game. I mean what's the point of the craft skill and being a godking if you can't build awesome things quickly while the rest of creation have magitech or necrotech infrastructures huge armies and other less savory stuff.<br /> <br /> Sorry this is a bitter feeling of mine when people tell you that there is cool stuff but you can't have it.<br /> <br /> Still we could take a stroll to the elemetal pole of wood to stock up on jade.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing everyone, especially the super craft advocates, seem to forget is that a factory cathedral by itself is an empty building. You need a massive infrastructure in place to support one at anything like full capacity. Even assuming you used that trick with melting demons, they still have a cap on the level of artifact they can be used for. So assuming you have an optimized Calcanth making manse you are still going to need to assemble higher level artifacts out of lower level artifacts. All of which needs to be done in identical batches since factory cathedrals only make identical copies. They also make higher levels in much smaller units than lower, such that you can only make one five dot or 10 four dots at a time. The real heavy stuff like Dawning Suns take a lot of component artifacts to make. Even then the fact cath is not benefiting from all your Solar charms. So it doesn't CNNT to reduce time further or HMU to halve required successes. So it rolls, at your dicepool, once a month to make artifacts.<br /> <br /> Assuming you don't want to use demons (it is certain to go wrong at some point) you need exotic material components from somewhere. I am not certain that it is actually possible to make a reality engine as an integrated utility artifact, and even if it was, the manse certainly can't use a Hand of the Great Maker since it does not know Solar charms. A sane ST will require someone to go hunting for them, which means a sane solar will set up a production infrastructure for them that does not require personally traipsing to the wyld every time a new apartment building goes up. Which means infrastructure <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Glorious, territory covering, vulnerable to geopolitical considerations and war, infrastructure!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T20:10:37-07:00","id":508659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=507333#post507333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are other paths. Sorcery, spiritual blessings, genesis, Wyld magic.<br /> <br /> Other people can work on making Shadow more awesome, too. There's an ex-PC genesis-specialist Solar running around, and Tirien's Lunar mentor makes entire species from scratch. Fae can be hard to deal with, but you have a few friendly(ish) fae on your team right now. Alopekis is the deity of the Novaleski Wolfhound, and is likely to know a few charms that may help Shadow get stronger.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one thing I am really starting to learn about this game. You have multiple paths to getting whatever you want to do. I guess anything that is more like training the dog as opposed to making stuff happen to him would be the best option in my book. Other options may be acceptable as long as they aren't invasive.<br /> <br /> Also, it seems like there are thaumaturgical processes that allow for the creation of magical materials. I'm not sure what the requirements for that are, but with enough effort most exalted can do things considered impossible by most mortals in the setting.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T20:35:06-07:00","id":508671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=508659#post508659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's one thing I am really starting to learn about this game. You have multiple paths to getting whatever you want to do. I guess anything that is more like training the dog as opposed to making stuff happen to him would be the best option in my book. Other options may be acceptable as long as they aren't invasive.<br /> <br /> Also, it seems like there are thaumaturgical processes that allow for the creation of magical materials. I'm not sure what the requirements for that are, but with enough effort most exalted can do things considered impossible by most mortals in the setting.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Would replacing his entire body except for his brain with orichalcum prosthetics count as making stuff happen to him? Because I think I could manage that one if you would like.<br /> <br /> If you are unsure, we can totally go with a trial period. Cyborg killbot wolf should be a reasonable middle ground while you get a feel for it don't you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T06:11:43-07:00","id":508876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=508344#post508344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing everyone, especially the super craft advocates, seem to forget is that a factory cathedral by itself is an empty building. You need a massive infrastructure in place to support one at anything like full capacity. Even assuming you used that trick with melting demons, they still have a cap on the level of artifact they can be used for. So assuming you have an optimized Calcanth making manse you are still going to need to assemble higher level artifacts out of lower level artifacts. All of which needs to be done in identical batches since factory cathedrals only make identical copies. They also make higher levels in much smaller units than lower, such that you can only make one five dot or 10 four dots at a time. The real heavy stuff like Dawning Suns take a lot of component artifacts to make. Even then the fact cath is not benefiting from all your Solar charms. So it doesn't CNNT to reduce time further or HMU to halve required successes. So it rolls, at your dicepool, once a month to make artifacts.<br /> <br /> Assuming you don't want to use demons (it is certain to go wrong at some point) you need exotic material components from somewhere. I am not certain that it is actually possible to make a reality engine as an integrated utility artifact, and even if it was, the manse certainly can't use a Hand of the Great Maker since it does not know Solar charms. A sane ST will require someone to go hunting for them, which means a sane solar will set up a production infrastructure for them that does not require personally traipsing to the wyld every time a new apartment building goes up. Which means infrastructure <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Glorious, territory covering, vulnerable to geopolitical considerations and war, infrastructure!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh that I know but such an infrartructure is not out of reach from a solar with the right training charms. I can train relevant craft with legendary warrior curriculum but not the orther abilities such as lore or occult but it's a start. I trust you with the political stuff I hope you can trust me, Belkra and Tirien with warfare. We'll keep you're infrastructure safe, no one will want to go to war with us once we are done with our enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 05-09-2015, 09:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T09:17:36-07:00","id":509042,"title":"","content":"Regarding Factory Cathedrals:<br /> <br /> While I lack the objective view as to comment on the degree of my own sanity, I agree whole heartedly with Exthalion up there. Only lazy or thoughtless STs allow factory cathedrals to be used that way. And STs who spent several years and a ton of money to get a degree in Political Science definitely won't allow it. Geopolitical considerations are fun!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T09:18:43-07:00","id":509045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=508671#post508671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would replacing his entire body except for his brain with orichalcum prosthetics count as making stuff happen to him? Because I think I could manage that one if you would like.<br /> <br /> If you are unsure, we can totally go with a trial period. Cyborg killbot wolf should be a reasonable middle ground while you get a feel for it don't you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Going the Proto Puma Prime path, I see. <br /> <br /> You'd fit in well with my IRL group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T09:20:05-07:00","id":509047,"title":"","content":"While formulating a response to Magnusar, I noticed that Aurem made reference to both a scepter and a crown. This is in error, and has been fixed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T10:32:43-07:00","id":509091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=508671#post508671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would replacing his entire body except for his brain with orichalcum prosthetics count as making stuff happen to him? Because I think I could manage that one if you would like.<br /> <br /> If you are unsure, we can totally go with a trial period. Cyborg killbot wolf should be a reasonable middle ground while you get a feel for it don't you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>This definitely counts as making stuff happen to him. Were I playing an Alchemical this would sound pretty fricken sweet. What I would really like to do is see if I can't get him charms almost as if he were a solar godblood, albeit one that is tied metaphysically to a full on Solar. I guess what I am looking for is things that would make him rock and enhance the dog while enhancing the bond between the two. Perhaps finding a way to raise his Familiar dots to N/A (6+) would be what I am looking for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T11:46:13-07:00","id":509155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=509091#post509091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This definitely counts as making stuff happen to him. Were I playing an Alchemical this would sound pretty fricken sweet. What I would really like to do is see if I can't get him charms almost as if he were a solar godblood, albeit one that is tied metaphysically to a full on Solar. I guess what I am looking for is things that would make him rock and enhance the dog while enhancing the bond between the two. Perhaps finding a way to raise his Familiar dots to N/A (6+) would be what I am looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, if that's all then your in luck.<br /> <br /> First, learn Bestial Traits Technique (core 210) and train Shadow to adult human intelligence (aka, now an ata-beast)<br /> <br /> Then tag him with power awarding prana and watch as he sudden grows to E2, gets a mote pool, and can learn solar charms. (You could go with soul-enlightening beneficence instead, but I don't think that lets him learn solar charms)<br /> <br /> Voila! You now have a young solar exalted ally as your familiar. I suggest skin mount amulets to increase his essence pool and a focus on permanent or long duration charms","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T15:04:48-07:00","id":511194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=509155#post509155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, if that's all then your in luck.<br /> <br /> First, learn Bestial Traits Technique (core 210) and train Shadow to adult human intelligence (aka, now an ata-beast)<br /> <br /> Then tag him with power awarding prana and watch as he sudden grows to E2, gets a mote pool, and can learn solar charms. (You could go with soul-enlightening beneficence instead, but I don't think that lets him learn solar charms)<br /> <br /> Voila! You now have a young solar exalted ally as your familiar. I suggest skin mount amulets to increase his essence pool and a focus on permanent or long duration charms</div> </div> </div> </div>Soul-Enlightening Benefice would prevent Shadow from learning Solar charms. He would be able to learn certain spirit charms and TMAs though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T15:18:51-07:00","id":511211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=509091#post509091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This definitely counts as making stuff happen to him. Were I playing an Alchemical this would sound pretty fricken sweet. What I would really like to do is see if I can't get him charms almost as if he were a solar godblood, albeit one that is tied metaphysically to a full on Solar. I guess what I am looking for is things that would make him rock and enhance the dog while enhancing the bond between the two. Perhaps finding a way to raise his Familiar dots to N/A (6+) would be what I am looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>By Solar godblood do you mean a Solar half-caste? 'Cause Solar godblood to me means the scion of a solar-aspected deity, like Little Beam or the Golden Lord. <br /> <br /> Survival charms could, I suppose, allow Shadow to access analogs to Solar charms, particularly those in Athletics, Survival, and Resistance. Getting other abilities could be a stretch. <br /> <br /> However. I have never really be one to let the rules get in the way of awesomeness. And I believe I made it clear that backgrounds can be upgraded through both play and roleplay. If the direction the game goes makes sense for Shadow to become a fluffy canine god-beast through sharing in his Solar master's heroic legend, then your Familiar dots will probably increase, and Shadow will get very interesting. <br /> <br /> Now, if you want to build on that yourself, by all means! But you having expressed interest in Shadow's apotheosis to fuzzy demigod means that I'm going to be looking out for opportunities to make that happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T22:16:49-07:00","id":512558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=511211#post511211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By Solar godblood do you mean a Solar half-caste? 'Cause Solar godblood to me means the scion of a solar-aspected deity, like Little Beam or the Golden Lord.<br /> <br /> Survival charms could, I suppose, allow Shadow to access analogs to Solar charms, particularly those in Athletics, Survival, and Resistance. Getting other abilities could be a stretch.<br /> <br /> However. I have never really be one to let the rules get in the way of awesomeness. And I believe I made it clear that backgrounds can be upgraded through both play and roleplay. If the direction the game goes makes sense for Shadow to become a fluffy canine god-beast through sharing in his Solar master's heroic legend, then your Familiar dots will probably increase, and Shadow will get very interesting.<br /> <br /> Now, if you want to build on that yourself, by all means! But you having expressed interest in Shadow's apotheosis to fuzzy demigod means that I'm going to be looking out for opportunities to make that happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Woot! Puppy demigod!<br /> <br /> In all seriousness, though. I am looking to go the route of increasing Familiar and eventually getting into custom Survival charms as the route to getting Shadow to be awesome. These seem the most in line with what the dawn and his canine companion would want.<br /> <br /> Also, I am picturing Shadow with some of the Solar Athletics charms that allow for running really freakin' fast. That just seems epic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T15:32:37-07:00","id":514573,"title":"","content":"Something else, hopefully also awesome!<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">It was a beautiful summer Saturnday morning. The sun had just begun to set the east ablaze, but Greheis lacked the usual pre-dawn flurry of activity. By Novaleski tradition, Saturnday was a day of rest and relaxation. Though many in the outlying homesteads still had their daily activities to attend to, in the city, businesses would be left shut, trading paused, and the temples closed. It was a time for the populace to engage in their hobbies. It was a time for family. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Which is why Ptreas Artemeon Derontikles, direct descendant of Ptreas, scion of wealth and privilege, was busy climbing over the walls of his family\u2019s compound. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The walls were short and made of roughly hewn stone, making it easy for the scrawny fourteen-year-old to find handholds and pull himself over the short wall. The wall was little more than a stone fence, serving the sole purpose of delineating the property of the Ptreas household from the rest of the city and the Gens. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">His escape was timed perfectly. The small handful of guards on duty had passed by in their rounds and wouldn\u2019t be back in at least a minute. Plenty of time for him to get over the wall and hide in the recesses of the nearby meeting-hall. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">She won\u2019t get me this time, </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dero thought as he cleared the edge of the wall and fell onto the streets below. </span></span></span><br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The sun sat at it\u2019s zenith as Dero munched on his breakfast. He\u2019d had a couple of close calls throughout the morning. Belisana and her dogs had almost caught him at the public baths, but luckily he\u2019d not counted on somewhat prudish Novaleski social norms to keep her out of the men\u2019s baths. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">After ducking into the private staff area, applying liberal amounts of mildly caustic soap and changing into a spare suit of low-class clothing that he had dirtied up for such an occasion, the dogs had lost his scent. From there he\u2019d made his way to his current perch on a massive warehouse on the waterfront, pilfering a bag of soft cheese and a roll of flatbread along the way. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">There\u2019s nothing right about stealing, </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dero thought,</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Not ever. </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">He\u2019d left a half-dozen sesterces behind, slipped innocuously into the pockets of those he\u2019d robbed. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">I\u2019m not here to make a quick dinar.</span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dero finished his meal and laid back on the sun-warmed brick roofing. As strange as it was, Dero kind of enjoyed these days. Sure, Belisana tried to chase him down, but over the course of the past couple of years, it had become something of a game. And while his older sister </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">hated </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">him getting away, she took her defeats with grace and poise. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dero snapped his head to the side as something caught his eye. A glint of light, a flashing mote reflected from the hills just north of town. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The abandoned quarries? </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dero thought. Those once-rich veins of stone were part of the reason that Greheis was located where it was. But they\u2019d run dry years ago, and were now crawling with beastial earth elementals. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">There it is again, </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dero thought as the glinting returned, </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Something\u2019s going on up there. And I\u2019m going to find out what. </span></i></span></span><br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Getting out of the city was much more difficult that getting out of the compound. Belisana would be watching the gate, and there was no going over the walls. Unlike the compound walls, these were built by the finest engineers in the nation to fend off roving barbarian tribes and small armies. Dero could find no purchase there. So he had circumvented the issue by slipping into the river and swimming upstream. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">My second bath today, </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dero thought as he dredged himself from the muddy banks of the river, </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">I\u2019ll need at least one more before this is through.</span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">It was less than a mile from the city wall to the quarries, but Dero crept there slowly, not wanting to catch the attention of the local wildlife, the local elementals, or whomever or whatever was up there. Staying close to cover as he did, it took him the better part of an hour to make it that far. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Reaching the edge of the quarries, Dero spotted movement. A large shape, blackish, was coming in his direction. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">A bear?, </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">he thought, hiding in an instant. Two more shapes appeared, and as the drew closer, Dero saw they were men. Heavyset men, wearing dark shades of blue, green or grey. Each one was armed with a broad, short blade. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Guards,</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Dero thought, </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Something\u2019s not right here. I\u2019m going to have to sneak around. </span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dero crept behind the trio slowly as they made their circuit East. They passed a few checkpoints, each one with a handful of similarly outfitted muscle-bound individuals scanning the landscape. Dero narrowly avoided detection several times, but his skill, paranoia and thick coating of mud served to keep him out of sight. Another patrol passed them making a clockwise circuit, and Dero knew he had his opportunity. Mere moments after the second patrol passed, he ducked past the perimeter and into the quarries. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Amateurs, </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dero thought, </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">they should be more careful</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">. </span></span></span><br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dero lay prone atop an artificial cliff, a brambly bush keeping the blazing sun off of his back. Despite his grandfather\u2019s wishes, Dero, his cousins and his sisters had spent a great deal of time hiding and playing in these hills. This spot was one of his favorites; the path up looked too steep to climb easily, and the brambles looked deceptively thick. More to the point, it had a good view of the area, including an easy line-of-sight on the only path up. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">And a good view of the proceedings taking place below him.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Two parties were gathered below him. The first was composed primarily of the dark-clothed meatheads he\u2019d slipped by earlier. The second group looked to be made of Novaleski citizen-soldiers. The first group was handing off a number of large crates to the second, and several of the Novaleskis just cracked open one of them to examine the contents. A hooded and robed man reached into the crate and withdrew a short silver-grey blade. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Therian weapons!?, </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dero thought. Iron-steel weapons were valuable in Novalesk, if only for the value of their metal. So why were they just being handed over, without payment? Had he missed an exchange of currency? Or were there other considerations?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Black Cowl, </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dero thought. It explained their peculiar dress, and their easy access to Therian weapons. And the Novaleskis were cultists themselves, survivors of the rebellion Dero\u2019s Uncle Vadik put down a little less than a year ago. Uncle Vadik, who was knifed in a barroom brawl just six weeks ago...</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dero\u2019s eyes flashed. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">I have to let the authorities know, </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">he thought, </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> The city\u2019s in danger. </span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dero began to climb down from his hiding-spot, but his mind was racing, considering all of the possibilities, all of the implications. Focused on the future, Dero misplaced his foot. He tried to catch himself too late, and lost his already tenuous grip. Dero tumbled down the cliff and passed into unconsciousness. </span></span></span><br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dero awoke to a powerful, throbbing pain in his arms and side. He winced as he tried to roll over onto his left side, a hot stab of pain piercing him from hip to fingers. His vision, already hazy from the shock, swam. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Ribs, cracked. Left arm, broken. Shoulder dislocated, </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dero thought, running through his list of injuries, </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">This is serious-</span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">A hand reached out and firmly pushed Dero to the ground. He saw a dark figure leaning above him, and he registered the sickly-sweet stench of blood and excrement. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Oh, damnation, </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dero thought, </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">They\u2019re going to kill me. </span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dero\u2019s vision came into focus, and he got a good look at the familiar face of the robed figure leaning in above him. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">OH DAMNATION, </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dero thought, </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">HE\u2019S going kill me!</span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cYou tumbled into something very dangerous, young man,\u201d the figure said, \u201cbut luckily for you, we got what we came for.\u201d Dero\u2019s confusion must have shown in his eyes or expression, as the figure continued, \u201cNo, not the weapons. That was just a pleasant bonus. We now have definitive proof the head of House Aloia and her heir are both members of the Black Cowl.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dero winced, both in pain and in anger at his own stupidity, as he tried to sit up. House Aloia was the most powerful family in the northern Therian territories, the closest thing Gens Ptreas had to blood rivals. If that information became public in Theros, the House would tear itself apart. The resulting power vacuum would quickly settle, but during the chaos, Novalesk would gain a powerful advantage in the north...</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The figure reached out again and pushed Dero back down, \u201cYou understand. Good. Now, one of my men will patch you up well enough to move. Then, you, your Grandfather and I will sit down for a nice long chat. Understood?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dero could only nod as Ptreas Artemeon Ilias, Scavenger Lord and Spymaster of Gens Ptreas, called over a Novaleski soldier to tend to his son\u2019s wounds. </span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1JRgroW2zTMLc7ClLZy_tn59ac_DuGyhpBpA82JsAtEE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A link to the original</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T19:27:45-07:00","id":514728,"title":"","content":"Also, Dero's internal monologue should be read in the voice of David Hayter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T17:40:03-07:00","id":515630,"title":"","content":"Wow, great! Also, I had to listen to the MGS2 soundtrack while reading it. Definitely worth the wait.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, Orchid makes a return in Emerald Labyrinth. She hasn't appeared lately, has she?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T16:14:24-07:00","id":532468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=515630#post515630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Orchid makes a return in Emerald Labyrinth. She hasn't appeared lately, has she?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not since just after Exthalion joined the game. So, yeah, it's been a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T20:29:40-07:00","id":535149,"title":"","content":"It's been a while, but the Rumor Mill turns again!<br />