d by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=558279#post558279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't be silly, that would be a horrible perversion of all that Yi and the Solar Exalted stand for.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Besides, where would I find the parts in this backwater...</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure that either the Monarch Raised Upon The Bones Of Trees and/or the Codicer Of Final Repose would be happy to supply you with the materials. The Dowager is not too far away either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T14:02:59-07:00","id":558665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=558342#post558342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of climates and such. I had envisioned a river-riven <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Subarctic_climate\" target=\"_blank\">Subarctic</a> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taiga\" target=\"_blank\">Taiga</a> as the homeland of both Jensven and Shadow. I'm reasonably sure that we can find that type of area on the map. Especially, if we are looking at the revisions made for 2.5/Ex3.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking it would probably be one of the rivers that feeds into the Avarice from the north.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T07:07:00-07:00","id":560784,"title":"","content":"Would a presence roll help in this situation ?<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh almost forgot how rare are dragon-blooded in creation ? If we wish to recruit more how hard would they be to find ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 06-19-2015, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T10:50:28-07:00","id":560934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=560784#post560784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a presence roll help in this situation ?<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh almost forgot how rare are dragon-blooded in creation ? If we wish to recruit more how hard would they be to find ?</div> </div> </div> </div>An astrological direction is 100,000,000 and there are five so Creation's pop is half a billion give or take.<br /> <br /> Assuming the commonly thrown around number of 10,000 dragons is roughly accurate, there is one Terrestrial per 50,000 people. (Insert cracks about them not being one in a million here)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T11:09:15-07:00","id":560947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=560934#post560934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An astrological direction is 100,000,000 and there are five so Creation's pop is half a billion give or take.<br /> <br /> Assuming the commonly thrown around number of 10,000 dragons is roughly accurate, there is one Terrestrial per 50,000 people. (Insert cracks about them not being one in a million here)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if that is a lot or not for terrrestrial exalted, how many would we need if we wanted to build a dragon-blooded Gens ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T11:18:28-07:00","id":560954,"title":"","content":"That depends, really. If you want to rebuild a First Age Gens at that level of blood purity, you'd need time, patience, and a certain lack of squeamishness about incest, as unlike in real life, it seems to IMPROVE the child's power in regards to the purity of their blood rather than detract from it. Hoenstly, though? You could rebuild one with one DB and a series of Neomahs or elementals, as if they're essence 4 or above, the Blood of Dragons takes over, and all children, if they are conceived, then they do gain the blood. On top of that, the children gain additional bonuses to exalting, as both parents have high essence, and in the case of Elementals, a circumstantial bonus because of their elemental nature.<br /> <br /> Noodle and I looked quite a bit into this because we've wondered why the Lunars in the Second Age never pulled a Bronze Faction, and tried to rebuild the Genses using their breeding charms to produce cadres of Beastmen DBs. Heck, Mejan Holof is partially based off this conceit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T11:30:51-07:00","id":560956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=560954#post560954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That depends, really. If you want to rebuild a First Age Gens at that level of blood purity, you'd need time, patience, and a certain lack of squeamishness about incest, as unlike in real life, it seems to IMPROVE the child's power in regards to the purity of their blood rather than detract from it. Hoenstly, though? You could rebuild one with one DB and a series of Neomahs or elementals, as if they're essence 4 or above, the Blood of Dragons takes over, and all children, if they are conceived, then they do gain the blood. On top of that, the children gain additional bonuses to exalting, as both parents have high essence, and in the case of Elementals, a circumstantial bonus because of their elemental nature.<br /> <br /> Noodle and I looked quite a bit into this because we've wondered why the Lunars in the Second Age never pulled a Bronze Faction, and tried to rebuild the Genses using their breeding charms to produce cadres of Beastmen DBs. Heck, Mejan Holof is partially based off this conceit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it would be overkill and LONG LIVE THE EMPIRE OF THE MOON !!! Joking aside even though a lot of them will probably try to kill us I still think that having a dragon-blooded Gens will help provide additionnal exalted to our cause and allow us to expand more easily.<br /> <br /> Let's say Amelia as a child with a dragon-blooded what are the chances that the child exalt as a dragon-blooded ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 06-19-2015, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T11:44:02-07:00","id":560980,"title":"","content":"Depends, what is your relative essence level. If you are the same or higher the chance is zero, since they will be Solar half castes. Their descendants will have a decent chance though. Better if this theoretical DB uses purity crucible strike to increase their own breeding. You can probably find Thoth's manse concepts that let you crank out first age legions by the day. These are generally taken as proof that something is wrong with the manse or breeding rules and possibly both.<br /> <br /> However, the general consensus on the forum is that trying to do this rapidly is almost certainly going to blow up in your face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T11:49:38-07:00","id":560996,"title":"","content":"I forget, which book are the breeding rules in, Exthalion? I've pored over my copy of MoEP: DBs, and I can't find it. Is it in Oedanael's Codex, with the Dragon Nest Manse, or what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T12:02:20-07:00","id":561001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=560980#post560980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends, what is your relative essence level. If you are the same or higher the chance is zero, since they will be Solar half castes. Their descendants will have a decent chance though. Better if this theoretical DB uses purity crucible strike to increase their own breeding. You can probably find Thoth's manse concepts that let you crank out first age legions by the day. These are generally taken as proof that something is wrong with the manse or breeding rules and possibly both.<br /> <br /> However, the general consensus on the forum is that trying to do this rapidly is almost certainly going to blow up in your face.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I saw those they are nice but too powerful for my taste. Oh dont worry I'm not gonna rush something like that. Really solars + DB = Solar HC I would have thought that both of them being exalted would have helped for having a DB child instead","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T12:07:18-07:00","id":561017,"title":"","content":"Half Castes are Scroll of Heroes p. 110. The Legendary Breeding and Terrestrial Bloodline merits are also in that book.<br /> <br /> Conveniently, while looking up the Terrestrial Bloodline merit it gave the reference to the breeding rules: MoEP DB p. 105-106. I had actually forgotten and was going to have to go hunting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T12:35:25-07:00","id":561049,"title":"","content":"Ah, thanks. I completely forgot about that merit, considering that my IRL group basically has ruled that all humans have a chance of exalting as a DB, however small that may be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T12:58:28-07:00","id":561065,"title":"","content":"As I recall, there are about 10,000 DBs in the Scarlet Dynasty, with about two or three thousand more Outcastes and members of the Cadet families. That number is about half of the DBs currently alive. The remaining numbers are spread about the other directions, with a heavy bias for the East, due to both the size of the population and the presence of Shogunate successor states like Lookshy and Port Calin. <br /> <br /> Since I'm the ST, that's the number we'll run with. <br /> <br /> In the immediate vicinity of Novalesk, there are 6 known DBs in Novalesk, about 60 or so in Theros, and maybe three or four among the Vicruith Geherin. There may be as many as ten among the steppes barbarians, with a strong bias towards those tribes descended from Darumfelian refugees (While the eradication of Darumfel's royal bloodline was rather complete, killing all of their bastards was outside the realm of the possible).<br /> <br /> To restart a stable Terrestrial bloodline, you'd need to get about as many as Theros has, with a significantally large number of un-exalted mortals with the dragons' blood to act as additional stock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T13:14:48-07:00","id":561073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=561065#post561065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I recall, there are about 10,000 DBs in the Scarlet Dynasty, with about two or three thousand more Outcastes and members of the Cadet families. That number is about half of the DBs currently alive. The remaining numbers are spread about the other directions, with a heavy bias for the East, due to both the size of the population and the presence of Shogunate successor states like Lookshy and Port Calin.<br /> <br /> Since I'm the ST, that's the number we'll run with.<br /> <br /> In the immediate vicinity of Novalesk, there are 6 known DBs in Novalesk, about 60 or so in Theros, and maybe three or four among the Vicruith Geherin. There may be as many as ten among the steppes barbarians, with a strong bias towards those tribes descended from Darumfelian refugees (While the eradication of Darumfel's royal bloodline was rather complete, killing all of their bastards was outside the realm of the possible).<br /> <br /> To restart a stable Terrestrial bloodline, you'd need to get about as many as Theros has, with a significantally large number of un-exalted mortals with the dragons' blood to act as additional stock.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. I'm guessing that recruiting Dragon-Blooded isn't easy, how many in theros are realm scion ?<br /> <br /> 2. Does breeding with elemental half-caste help the odds ?<br /> <br /> 3. Without using methods like Thoth's manse, are there ways to help ensure almost all children exalt as dragon-blooded<br /> ?<br /> <br /> Also what is that roll to see if the child exalt ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 06-19-2015, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T15:32:51-07:00","id":561279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=561073#post561073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. I'm guessing that recruiting Dragon-Blooded isn't easy, how many in theros are realm scion ?<br /> <br /> 2. Does breeding with elemental half-caste help the odds ?<br /> <br /> 3. Without using methods like Thoth's manse, are there ways to help ensure almost all children exalt as dragon-blooded<br /> ?<br /> <br /> Also what is that roll to see if the child exalt ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Purity crucible strike from both terrestrial parents pushes their breeding to five. That ensures all children will Exalt. PCS can kill the user, so channeling a virtue is suggested.<br /> <br /> Apparent the rules didn't actually make it into the book...<br /> <br /> Here they are:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">The rules for determining if a Dragon-Blooded child exalts involve rolling a single 10-sided die. If both parents are patricians of proper breeding with numerous Dragon-Blooded relatives, the child Exalts on a roll of 1-2. If one parent's a Dragon-Blood and the other is a mortal of poor breeding, the child will Exalt on a roll of 1-3. If one parent's a Dragon-Blood and the other's a patrician of good stock with Dragon-Blooded relatives, the child Exalts on a roll of 1-4. If both parents are Dragon-Bloods, the child Exalts on a roll of 1-6.The Breeding Background adds to the number that must be rolled, and it applies from both parents if both have high enough Breeding. Thus, if two Dragon-Bloods, one with Breeding 4 and one with Breeding 5, have a child, the child will Exalt on a roll of 1-9 (the normal 1-6 for the child of two Terrestrials, plus 1 for the Breeding 4 parent, plus another 2 for the Breeding 5 parent).</span></span> </div> </div> </div>From that we can infer that:<br /> Poor breeding mortal: +0<br /> Good breeding mortal: +1<br /> Terrestrial: +3 or Breeding background, whichever is higher.<br /> <br /> The Dragon's Nest manse power adds +1 to the roll if the child is conceived in the manse, and +2 if the child is brought to term in it.<br /> <br /> Finally, there is a rule somewhere (I don't remember where) that if one of the parents is an elemental and the other a terrestrial exalted then the child will exalt no matter how poor the breeding. I disagree strongly with this rule and think it should do nothing but dilute the blood. That might just be me though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 06-19-2015, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T16:11:54-07:00","id":561304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=561279#post561279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Purity crucible strike from both terrestrial parents pushes their breeding to five. That ensures all children will Exalt. PCS can kill the user, so channeling a virtue is suggested.<br /> <br /> Apparent the rules didn't actually make it into the book...<br /> <br /> Here they are:<br /> <br /> <br /> From that we can infer that:<br /> Poor breeding mortal: +0<br /> Good breeding mortal: +1<br /> Terrestrial: +3<br /> <br /> The Dragon's Nest manse power adds +1 to the roll if the child is conceived in the manse, and +2 if the child is brought to term in it.<br /> <br /> Finally, there is a rule somewhere (I don't remember where) that if one of the parents is an elemental and the other a terrestrial exalted then the child will exalt no matter how poor the breeding. I disagree strongly with this rule and think it should do nothing but dilute the blood. That might just be me though.</div> </div> </div> </div>If all the right circumstance can be reunited restarting a strong dragon-blooded gens and ensuring a good rate of exalted children is possible in theory, I still think recruiting 60 dragon-blooded augmenting their breeding to maximum and having them mate in a dragon crucible manse will not be an easy task. <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Breeding with an elemental could help reinforced and purify the dragon-blood</span></span></span> but only for a single generation. Ex: If the dragon-blooded daughter of an elemental would have a child with another elemental it would decrease the breeding and the chance of her child to exalt and so on. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T10:06:26-07:00","id":562058,"title":"","content":"All this talk of a breeding program makes me wonder if we aren't stepping into the territory of forcing people, especially the mortal stock (which can be created by breeding dragon-bloods with normal people if you think about it), to do things they may not be okay with in the interest of increasing the strength of the nation. Jensven wouldn't be cool with that.<br /> <br /> Of course, there are ways to convince people that they really want to do something even if they wouldn't normally do it under the same circumstances. Natural Mental Influence is a great thing here. If the terrestrials and the mortals are feeling very patriotic and decide to do this, it would work rather well. Even better than if they were coerced. Let's keep in mind that I am not accusing anyone of saying we should use coercion. I am just stating my thoughts and concerns on the issue. More relevant, though is how I believe my character would react to such.<br /> <br /> Finally, I think it would be a very potent story element for us to employ if one of the NPCs involved in the breeding program were engaging in it because they were enamored with one of the PCs and were willing to even shack up/marry/knock up/be knocked up by others in an effort to seek the approval of that character. I have a feeling that it would be very tragic. If handled maturely and responsibly it could make for a very compelling story.<br /> <br /> That's my two dinar on the matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T12:52:04-07:00","id":562154,"title":"","content":"Oh no, that would blow up in our face really fast. Better to transform neomah into gestation tanks to grow out new terrestrials in than try mass forced programs. Or just use neomah, but for some reason it feels as though the setting can only be improved by fields of neomah tanks.<br /> <br /> (Or this is another Dune reference and I am enjoying the running joke)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T13:02:30-07:00","id":562167,"title":"","content":"Let's keep the &quot;I use demons for everything&quot; to a minimum please (joking ?) but I have to ask why Neomah ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T13:48:26-07:00","id":562180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=562167#post562167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's keep the &quot;I use demons for everything&quot; to a minimum please (joking ?) but I have to ask why Neomah ?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://dune.wikia.com/wiki/Axlotl_Tanks\" target=\"_blank\">http://dune.wikia.com/wiki/Axlotl_Tanks</a><br /> <br /> (It was totally a Dune reference)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 06-20-2015, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T18:00:25-07:00","id":562418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=562180#post562180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://dune.wikia.com/wiki/Axlotl_Tanks\" target=\"_blank\">http://dune.wikia.com/wiki/Axlotl_Tanks</a><br /> <br /> (It was totally a Dune reference)</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't watched Dune yet so didn't get that part <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T20:01:13-07:00","id":562525,"title":"","content":"Since the others were answered...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=561073#post561073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. I'm guessing that recruiting Dragon-Blooded isn't easy, how many in theros are realm scion ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you refering to the handful of officers commanding the local garrison, a thousand scales bureaucrat and a mid-ranking immaculate monk that are members of the Great Houses? Or the anywhere from zero to some who are rumored to be the bastards of the great houses? <br /> <br /> The Realm natives weren't included in the initial count of Therian terrestrials. The later were, in the event that they actually exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T20:05:54-07:00","id":562527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=562167#post562167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's keep the &quot;I use demons for everything&quot; to a minimum please (joking ?) but I have to ask why Neomah ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Neomah are flesh-weavers, and can take a pound of flesh from two or more people to make offspring in a manner of hours, instead of three seasons. Also they have a power that improves the chances of the offspring of a Terrestrial inheriting Exaltation. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T20:08:43-07:00","id":562530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=562418#post562418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I haven't watched Dune yet so didn't get that part <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>If you're planning on <i>watching </i>Dune, go with the 1984 film. Otherwise, I suggest reading from <i>Dune </i>to <i>God-Emperor of Dune</i> and stopping there. After that it starts to get really weird (and given the weirdness of the first four books of the series, that's saying something).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T20:11:22-07:00","id":562532,"title":"","content":"Umm... Exthalion? Are you trying to summon a Lesser Elemental Dragon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T20:32:13-07:00","id":562543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=562532#post562532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Umm... Exthalion? Are you trying to summon a Lesser Elemental Dragon?</div> </div> </div> </div>While that was not my intention, I am totally down for that if it makes for a better story. I assumed some of them below that level know the Terrestrial spell Ritual of Elemental Empowerment. (The name is taken from the elemental lover of a previous character of mine. She was a spirit of an oasis in the South and he was just coming back from one of those banished into the desert to die sorts of things.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T20:37:38-07:00","id":562548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=562543#post562543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While that was not my intention, I am totally down for that if it makes for a better story. I assumed some of them below that level know the Terrestrial spell Ritual of Elemental Empowerment. (The name is taken from the elemental lover of a previous character of mine. She was a spirit of an oasis in the South and he was just coming back from one of those banished into the desert to die sorts of things.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay. I just wanted to know what level of essence to give her, should she desire to resist. Also, whether or not she likely would. And I could totally see Yi trying to pull something like that. <br /> <br /> I suppose it would likely be, given your brief description of her and her deeds, that she would be a high- ranking spirit in her court, likely only one or two steps from the very top.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T00:30:57-07:00","id":570021,"title":"","content":"On account of sudden family obligations (of which there seem to be many) I'll be unable to post til the 4th","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5005-heavenlythunder","name":"HeavenlyThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5005_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T11:33:33-07:00","id":572971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HeavenlyThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=570021#post570021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On account of sudden family obligations (of which there seem to be many) I'll be unable to post til the 4th</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know that feeling. Hope everything's alright.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T10:37:23-07:00","id":574099,"title":"","content":"Yeah, they just like traveling and decided Paris in 90-105 degree weather was a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5005-heavenlythunder","name":"HeavenlyThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5005_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T11:41:17-07:00","id":576639,"title":"","content":"What does two dots in lore gives you in terms of education ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T11:28:35-07:00","id":577547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=576639#post576639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does two dots in lore gives you in terms of education ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Basic mathematics, some algebra and geometry. Maybe some basic physics. Rough history of your nation, nation's religion and such.<br /> <br /> Since Amelia is from Greyfalls, that would include Realm history 101, Greyfalls History 101, and Introduction to the Immaculate Religion for Secular Life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T11:46:40-07:00","id":577561,"title":"","content":"So, I wrote up the entirety of Moxe-Ulto's creation myth, before I realized that the young woman in question would probably just summarize it. Anyways, here's the unabridged myth, since I didn't want that work to go to waste. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Before there was the World, there was nothing. Then Pei-Seth said, Let There Be Me, and He Was. With Pei-Seth's divine primogenesis, so to was birthed the Eternal Chaos. The Chaos was anathema to Pei-Seth, who was Order. So Pei-Set said, Let Events Unfold As They Will, and There Was Time. And with Time, Order was imposed upon the Chaos. Then Pei-Set said, Let Myself Have Form Eternal, and then was birthed the Land, that was His Flesh But Also Not. And then Pei-Seth slept, for further action would be to upset the Order That Was. Thus was the First Age of the World Born, When Pei-Seth slept after its Creation.<br /> <br /> The Second Age of the World was Birthed with the Second Divinity. Pei-Seth awoke after slumbering countless millennia away. And when He Awoke, the Urge To Create once more was upon Him. And so Pei-Seth said, Let There Be Another, Who is Like Me But Not. And Marle Who Was The Sky was Born. Marle was Like Pei-Seth, for She too Was of Order. But She was Not, for Her Order was one of Motion and Patterns Within Patterns, where Pei-Seth\u2019s was an Order of Stillness. Content, Pei-Seth returned to His Slumber, while Marle roiled above. So passed the Second Age.<br /> <br /> The Third Age of the World came when was Birthed the Third Divinity. Dannu was Birthed along with her Sister by Pei-Seth at the Dawn of the Second Age. But Her Nature was more Fluid that the Others, and so was merely Birthed as a Potentiality. But some of the Power of the Chaos Eternal bleed into the Creation of Pei-Seth, and it merged with the Potentiality of Dannu making Her Dannu Who Was The Sea. Her Nature was both the Order of Pei-Seth and the Order of Marle. And Dannu broke against both Land and Sky and Changed their Order to fit her own.<br /> <br /> The Fourth Age came when Pei-Seth Awoke Once More. Seeing Dannu, Passion and Lust came upon Him and He lway with Her, and from their Union was Born Shef-Joryis Who Was the Life. His Order was one of a Thousand-Thousand little Orders. And the Four Divinities were content with One Another, and Sat Together, Awake and In Peace.<br /> <br /> The Fifth Age came with the Arrival of Hei-Seth Who Was the Destroyer. Hei-Seth was Born too with Pei-Seth in the Formless Nothing. But Pei-Seth was an Order of Creation, while Hei-Seth was an Order of Destruction, and so had Ignored His Brother in the Creation of That Which Was. This caused Rage and Anger to boil in His Heart. So Hei-Seth came to the World That Was and Burned It To Ash and Waged War upon Pei-Seth and Marle and Dannu and Shef-Joryis. The War Lasted for Time Uncounted, for Time Itself was a casualty of the War. But while Hei-Seth was Mighty, the others were both Mighty and Many, and Threw Him Down. But in so doing, they learned that Hei-Seth\u2019s hatred grew from Loneliness and Sorrow from being Excluded by His Siblings. And so They Raised Him Up into the Embrace of Marle and Hei-Seth Who Was The Devourer Became Hei-Seth Who Is The Flame. And Hei-Seth cleared the way for others to rebuild and build anew, passing the Ages from the Fifth to the Sixth.<br /> <br /> In the Sixth Age, the Five Divinities rebuilt the World and the Life from the cinders that Hei-Seth had burned it to. They birthed from themselves Twenty-Four and One lesser Divinities Of Themselves, and Uncounted Many Least divinities to govern and steward their Creation. And they took Beasts and gave them the Souls Of Gods to See the Order They Would Make with Divine Vision but not the Reach to Grasp It. And They Were Pleased.<br /> <br /> And the Sixth Age Passed into the Seventh with the Coming of another War. Those who dwelled in the Chaos Eternal Wished to cast Down The Creation of the Divine, to return all to to Formless Nothing. They Rallied Against Creation, and the Five Divinities Did Battle with the Brazen Imperator, and the Eternal Wasteland, and the Sea That Drowned, and the Invincible Beast, and the Eternal Tower who were each their equals. And the Twenty-Four and One Lesser Divinities made war with their Servants, the Shadow Serpent, and the Seven-Winged Peacock, and the Emerald Pyre-Sun, and the Demon-Wind, and the Eye of the Heavens, and the Silver City, and Twenty More who were each their equals. And the hordes of Least Divinites clashed with the hordes of the Least Servants of Chaos and were met as Equals. And a Stalemate was reached. And for an Age the War raged, until the Five Great Divinities took some of the Beasts that had Souls of Gods and Burned Their Divine Power into the Beasts\u2019 blood. And this new force tipped the Balance in the favor of the Gods, who took mercy upon their fallen Foes, exiling them in a world of their own devising. So passed the Seventh Age unto the Eighth.<br /> <br /> The Eighth Age was a time of golden prosperity. The Divinities made for themselves a Golden City and passed the world unto those who had inherited their Divine Fire within their Blood. Civilization prospered and Wonders were there for any with but the Will To Reach For Them. It would have been a paradise that lasted forever, but for the Hubris of Man. Some few of those with the Divine-blood sought out their fallen enemies to learn their secrets, and so learned the power to amplify their Divine spark. Twenty-Four by Twelve were the number of those who used this Power. At First, this power made them Great, and they were lauded as Kings, for their wonders were without peer and their Wisdom knew No Bounds. But the Brazen Imperator knew the Secrets of the World and of Their Heart, and Placed a Curse upon that Power. While It amplified all facets of their power, the sorceries of the Imperator stoked the smouldering spark of the Great Devourer that slumbered within. Wisdom grew to Tyranny and Wonders to Horrors, and they began to burn with the Gilded Fire of the Devourer. Seeing their Corruption, those of the Blood cast down their fallen Kings, turning the age from the Eighth to the Ninth.<br /> <br /> The Ninth Age was also one of Wonders and Prosperity, for there were many of the Divine Blood. Many declared it lesser than the Eighth, but they were fools, for those wonders came at the price of the yoke of the mad golden kings. But it was also a time of War, for the Powers of the Gilded Kings thrummed in their Souls, drawing them back to the flesh each time they were killed like Iron to a Lodestone. Over time, the world was lessened by this onslaught, and the Gilded Kings fled unto the Brazen Realms. It was not long after, though, that a Sickness fell over the World, so mighty that the Five Divinities took it unto themselves so to Save their countless children. They sleep now in the Golden City, healing themselves for the Great Disease. But the forces of Chaos saw their temporary weakness and struck. They failed to release their God-Titans, but shattered the world before they were thrown back by what few Divinities and Blooded Ones Remained. So passed the Ages from the Ninth to the Tenth.<br /> <br /> The Tenth Age was the Shortest to yet, numbering a mere Twenty-Four-by-Fifteen Years. Three of the Lesser Divinities, Children of the Five, sacrificed themselves to build a glorious citadel, Moxe-Ulto. So long as that Citadel stood, the Forces of the Chaos Eternal could not break the shattered World. But the Tenth Age was an age of Peace, as the World Healed itself from the ravages of the Chaos. Now it is the Eleventh Age, when the Hosts of Chaos, themselves lessened by their failure, attempt to break that bulwark to finish what they had started in the Ninth. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"than