nges a few tactic I thought about though I won't complain I did start with a rank 5 magitech artifact which are supposed to super rare, some people might try to kill me for it I assume (if being a solar wasn't enough).</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 09-29-2015, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T14:56:07-07:00","id":683571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=682066#post682066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That is also what I thought but if its not it changes a few tactic I thought about though I won't complain I did start with a rank 5 magitech artifact which are supposed to super rare, some people might try to kill me for it I assume (if being a solar wasn't enough).</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Major kingdoms will declare war, expend all the prosperity and treasure built up over the course of a mighty dynasty, and sacrifice a generation of their young men for a five dot artifact. Being magitech is window dressing at that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T15:36:59-07:00","id":683608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=683571#post683571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Major kingdoms will declare war, expend all the prosperity and treasure built up over the course of a mighty dynasty, and sacrifice a generation of their young men for a five dot artifact. Being magitech is window dressing at that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>True but does the average Joe know what a celestial battle armor is, now that I think about who could recognize it for what it is ? Few ever saw one that is for sure and fewer even know they existed no ? I think even Yi will have trouble knowing what it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 09-30-2015, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T11:59:36-07:00","id":690002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=683608#post683608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True but does the average Joe know what a celestial battle armor is, now that I think about who could recognize it for what it is ? Few ever saw one that is for sure and fewer even know they existed no ? I think even Yi will have trouble knowing what it is.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>The ... mutant things kept pushing against our lines. Scuttling, horned chitinous things that might have been human once, centuries ago. Damn, we were the light foot! Skirmishers! We're weren't supposed to stand down foes, even undisciplined ones! And they kept pushing us, in their never-ending waves. Sure, we cut them down like wheat before the scythe. But every so often, one would slip behind the bodies and grab one of our men. The lucky ones were those that they just shredded. The unlucky ones got pulled away from the lines into that dark, chitinous sea.<br /> <br /> It seemed like we were making headway. We pushed them over Burroshil and into the valley. Step-by-bloody-step we advanced, the Lookshy medium foot on our right flank, and the Albian heavies on our left. Our captain stood at the van, sling in one hand, and spear in the other. Some said he was the son of the Shield of a Different Day. Others, that he was a deserter of Sunipa's war-staff. But one thing was certain, he was a god. Each time he struck one of those monsters with his spear it burned to a cinder from the inside out. Each time he fired his sling, a dozen of them fell from the bullet. We pushed them back toward Madorai, where the natives had blockaded their city-bridge. With their back to the rivers and caught between the Confed forces on one flank, and the fortified City Upon The Bridge on the other, the enemy was screwed, and they knew it.<br /> <br /> At least, until their god-monster rallied them forward. It was a terrible protean monster, standing nearly fifteen feet tall with blood-dripping matted fur and a long horn and no eyes. It could see somehow, though, since it singled out the captain and ripped him limb from limb. I think it knew we were the weakest link in the Confederation's line of battle, cause it then started cutting though our line. It was about the grab me, when a gilded fist came out of nowhere and sent it flying. My savior was garbed in gilded armor from head to toe, arcane sigils all over it. Strange rosy-gold fins stretched from the back, almost as wings. It was as if one of the dread Solar Anathema of Old came down before me, until I caught a whiff of smoky incense. I had smelt it before, when the Prince of the Earth commanding the Lookshan detachment had wrestled the captain.<br /> <br /> The Prince of the Earth grabbed the god-monster's hair and smashed his fist into its face. Again and again, the gilded fist fell, and his grip remained firm. I just couldn't understand it. The Lookshan got thrown by the captain two times out three, but here he was, smacking the shit out of the monster that ripped the cap in half?<br /> <br /> The Lookshan killed the monster, and the mutants routed after that. The Lookshans put that strange gilded armor back into that Jade Casket they were carrying around, and I knew why those Gunzosha were guarding it rather taking part in the battle.<br /> <br /> -Taken from the Journal of Hei Dai Nao, Great Forks citizen-soldier, regarding events circa 543 Post-Contagion. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","user":"Noodle","date":". 10-08-2015, 10:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T16:41:56-07:00","id":690595,"title":"","content":"Nice story , and nice reference to the Horned Nightstalker we had talked about earlier. I've posted, apologies to all; work has been slapping my shut these past few weeks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T08:00:29-08:00","id":763112,"title":"","content":"So are we gonna waste this thing ? Or is the game over ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T05:14:08-08:00","id":764861,"title":"","content":"I dunno, are we? I think I'm the lasf to respond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/memb